window.M1DATA={"topics":[{"n":1,"title":"Will and Going To","es":"Will y going to","cover":"u:photo-1597952681778-21b365d312ca","parts":[{"id":"t1p1","topic":1,"part":1,"title":"Predictions & instant decisions","es":"Predicciones y decisiones al instante","acts":["learn","crystalBall","fill","sort","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>En inglés hay dos futuros muy comunes y <b>no son intercambiables</b> en todos los casos:</p>\n<p>🔮 <b>WILL</b> → predicciones basadas en tu <b>opinión o creencia</b> (<i>I think AI <b>will</b> change everything</i>), <b>decisiones tomadas en el momento</b> (<i>The phone's ringing. — I'<b>ll</b> get it!</i>), ofrecimientos y promesas (<i>I'<b>ll</b> help you</i>).</p>\n<p>👀 <b>GOING TO</b> → predicciones con <b>evidencia presente</b>, algo que ya ves venir (<i>Look at those clouds! It'<b>s going to</b> rain</i>).</p>\n<p>⚠️ Errores típicos: <i>I think it won't rain</i> suena raro; lo natural es <b>I don't think it will rain</b>. El adverbio va <b>después</b> de will y <b>antes</b> de won't: <i>She'll <b>probably</b> call</i> · <i>She <b>probably</b> won't call</i>.</p>","tips":["En conversación <b>I will</b> casi siempre se contrae: <i>I'll</i> suena <i>ail</i>.","<b>going to</b> en habla rápida suena <i>gonna</i>: entiéndelo, pero escríbelo completo en emails formales.","<b>won't</b> (will not) suena <i>uóunt</i>; no lo confundas con <b>want</b> (<i>uánt</i>)."],"vocab":[{"en":"I'll take care of it.","es":"Yo me encargo.","img":"u:photo-1781268034959-8706486c22a4","v":"f","au":"a14be06cd8"},{"en":"I'll get the door.","es":"Yo abro la puerta.","img":"u:photo-1774464711267-4590ba6f5acd","v":"m","au":"160c585dd6"},{"en":"It's going to pour.","es":"Va a caer un aguacero.","img":"u:photo-1597952681778-21b365d312ca","v":"f","au":"528e3ce23d"},{"en":"I think prices will go up.","es":"Creo que los precios van a subir.","img":"u:photo-1685640206182-c51b8aa9b686","v":"m","au":"703cf559d9"},{"en":"That's going to cost a fortune.","es":"Eso va a costar una fortuna.","img":"u:photo-1758523419048-eeb546daac05","v":"f","au":"8697b1a9da"},{"en":"I'm sure you'll do great.","es":"Seguro que te irá genial.","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"m","au":"a5090b73a1"},{"en":"I bet it won't last.","es":"Apuesto a que no durará.","img":"u:photo-1629385697093-57be2cc97fa6","v":"f","au":"2e3649f398"},{"en":"probably / definitely","es":"probablemente / definitivamente","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"m","au":"17a4385d7a"},{"en":"a long shot","es":"algo muy poco probable","img":"u:photo-1641531105535-1ead3c1784ab","v":"f","au":"618079501e"},{"en":"to make up your mind","es":"decidirse","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"m","au":"0e8f814232"},{"en":"on the spur of the moment","es":"de improviso, sin planearlo","img":"u:photo-1759132756413-1665271486af","v":"f","au":"3d43d5a226"},{"en":"a sure thing","es":"algo seguro","img":"u:photo-1549923746-c502d488b3ea","v":"m","au":"4a56ce16df"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Look at those clouds! It's going to pour.","es":"¡Mira esas nubes! Va a caer un aguacero.","img":"u:photo-1597952681778-21b365d312ca","v":"f","au":"4b84691f94"},{"en":"I think remote work will become the norm.","es":"Creo que el trabajo remoto se volverá la norma.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"m","au":"33b8815eb7"},{"en":"The phone's ringing. Don't worry, I'll get it.","es":"Está sonando el teléfono. Tranquilo, yo contesto.","img":"u:photo-1691380302295-b19eda6ae52b","v":"f","au":"72d600b572"},{"en":"He's driving way too fast. He's going to crash.","es":"Va demasiado rápido. Va a chocar.","img":"u:photo-1564668836804-05a2de350bb6","v":"m","au":"c12a394f7d"},{"en":"You'll probably feel jet-lagged for a couple of days.","es":"Probablemente tendrás jet lag un par de días.","img":"u:photo-1569629743817-70d8db6c323b","v":"f","au":"59f357c764"},{"en":"I promise I won't tell anyone.","es":"Te prometo que no le diré a nadie.","img":"u:photo-1621452773781-0f992fd1f5cb","v":"m","au":"dfa937bdf8"}],"fill":[{"s":"Watch out! You ___ spill your coffee!","a":"are going to","o":["will","go to"],"h":"evidencia presente → going to","full":"Watch out! You are going to spill your coffee!","au":"861f317160"},{"s":"I'm freezing. — Hold on, I ___ close the window.","a":"will","o":["am going to","go to"],"h":"decisión en el momento","full":"I'm freezing. — Hold on, I will close the window.","au":"2d5463be80"},{"s":"In my opinion, AI ___ replace many office jobs.","a":"will","o":["is going","goes to"],"h":"opinión sobre el futuro","full":"In my opinion, AI will replace many office jobs.","au":"7175ab62f6"},{"s":"I don't think it ___ snow in Miami this year.","a":"will","o":["won't","is"],"h":"\"I don't think + will\"","full":"I don't think it will snow in Miami this year.","au":"f8a65cc3c3"},{"s":"Her eyes are closing. She ___ fall asleep any minute.","a":"is going to","o":["will","goes to"],"h":"evidencia visible","full":"Her eyes are closing. She is going to fall asleep any minute.","au":"1c75ac5802"},{"s":"Traffic is terrible. I'll ___ be late.","a":"probably","o":["probable","probably to"],"h":"will + probably","full":"Traffic is terrible. I'll probably be late.","au":"a459a6850b"}],"sort":{"cats":["Evidence","Opinion","Instant decision"],"items":[{"w":"Look! It's going to fall.","c":"Evidence","au":"bcef2babc7"},{"w":"She's pale. She's going to faint.","c":"Evidence","au":"1930318859"},{"w":"The sky is black. It's going to rain.","c":"Evidence","au":"e81e45e993"},{"w":"I think she'll love it.","c":"Opinion","au":"1d17e919ba"},{"w":"I'm sure they'll win.","c":"Opinion","au":"11f6159b4e"},{"w":"Prices will probably go up.","c":"Opinion","au":"5bc541d915"},{"w":"I'll get it!","c":"Instant decision","au":"7fe22eaea5"},{"w":"I'll have the salmon, please.","c":"Instant decision","au":"b2a6253dab"},{"w":"Wait, I'll help you.","c":"Instant decision","au":"5b8f427f0c"}]},"goal":{"en":"To make predictions and instant decisions with will and going to.","es":"Hacer predicciones y tomar decisiones al instante con will y going to."},"warm":[{"q":"What do you think your city will look like in twenty years?","au":"0d0fdf3419","es":"¿Cómo crees que será tu ciudad dentro de veinte años?","ex":"I think it will have more electric cars and taller buildings."},{"q":"Have you ever made a big decision on the spur of the moment?","au":"770cdf5355","es":"¿Alguna vez has tomado una gran decisión de improviso?","ex":"Yes, I once quit my job and traveled for a month."}],"reading":{"title":"The future of work, according to Ana","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","text":"Ana Torres is a career coach in San Antonio, and her clients always ask her the same question: what will work look like in ten years? \"Honestly, nobody knows for sure,\" she says, \"but I think most office jobs will become hybrid, and companies will probably care more about skills than degrees.\" Some trends, however, are already visible. \"Look at the numbers: AI tools are everywhere. Many routine tasks are going to disappear, and that's not an opinion, it's happening right now.\" Ana believes this is good news for people who keep learning. \"I'm sure people who adapt will do great.\" Last week a nervous client told her he had lost his job. Ana didn't hesitate: \"Okay, I'll help you update your résumé tonight, and I'll call a recruiter I know tomorrow.\" Her advice is simple: don't wait for the future to surprise you. Make up your mind about the skills you want, and start today.","au":"eeeba5be7f","q":[{"s":"Ana is a career coach in San Antonio.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She is completely sure about the future of work.","a":"no"},{"s":"She thinks many routine tasks are going to disappear.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She told her client she would call him next month.","a":"no"},{"s":"She decided to help the client on the spot.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you think English will be more important in the future?","a":"Yes, I think it will be even more important for work.","es":"¿Crees que el inglés será más importante en el futuro?","qau":"ee3362c3ef","aau":"ef7d3a2bf8"},{"q":"Look at the sky. What's going to happen?","a":"It's going to rain. Look at those dark clouds.","es":"Mira el cielo. ¿Qué va a pasar?","qau":"6b1052e56c","aau":"babf47f69c"},{"q":"Your friend is carrying heavy bags. What do you say?","a":"Let me help you. I'll carry one of them.","es":"Tu amigo lleva bolsas pesadas. ¿Qué le dices?","qau":"0db4e477f2","aau":"08ecd1e478"},{"q":"What will you probably do this weekend?","a":"I'll probably stay home and relax.","es":"¿Qué harás probablemente este fin de semana?","qau":"d330cf8cb1","aau":"818e7d29fa"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 3 predicciones sobre tu ciudad o tu trabajo con will (opinión) y 2 con going to (con evidencia). Explica la evidencia.","kw":["will","going to"],"n":5,"model":"I think my city will have more electric buses. Prices will probably go up. I don't think people will stop using cars. My company is hiring a lot, so it's going to grow. Look at the traffic: we're going to be late."}},{"id":"t1p2","topic":1,"part":2,"title":"Plans, intentions & promises","es":"Planes, intenciones y promesas","acts":["learn","ceoPlanner","dialogue","unscramble","memory","speak"],"tip":"<p>📅 <b>GOING TO</b> = plan o <b>intención ya decidida</b> antes de hablar: <i>I'<b>m going to</b> ask for a raise.</i></p>\n<p>🤝 <b>Presente continuo</b> = plan <b>acordado con otras personas</b>, con hora/lugar: <i>We'<b>re meeting</b> the client at three.</i></p>\n<p>💬 <b>WILL</b> = ofrecimientos, promesas, pedidos y decisiones del momento: <i>I'<b>ll</b> call you back. <b>Will</b> you help me?</i></p>\n<p>🙋 <b>Shall I / Shall we...?</b> = ofrecer o sugerir de forma amable: <i><b>Shall I</b> book a table?</i></p>\n<p>⏱️ <b>be about to</b> = estar a punto de · <b>be likely to</b> = ser probable que.</p>","tips":["<b>Shall I</b> suena <i>shal ai</i>; es elegante y muy usado para ofrecer ayuda.","En <b>We're meeting</b> une las palabras: <i>uir-míring</i> (la t suena como r suave).","<b>about to</b> se pronuncia rápido: <i>abáut-tu</i> → <i>abáuru</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"I'm going to ask for a raise.","es":"Voy a pedir un aumento.","img":"u:photo-1758518729912-bf3a84c400e0","v":"m","au":"70d8449521"},{"en":"We're meeting the client at three.","es":"Nos reunimos con el cliente a las tres.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"24cb1ee07a"},{"en":"Shall I book a table?","es":"¿Reservo una mesa?","img":"u:photo-1744776411221-702f2848b0b2","v":"f","au":"7be0f9ed39"},{"en":"I'll call you back.","es":"Te devuelvo la llamada.","img":"u:photo-1758873268528-af4613d099b6","v":"m","au":"b022a33d72"},{"en":"I'm about to leave.","es":"Estoy a punto de salir.","img":"u:photo-1713947505221-8a11da8aa744","v":"f","au":"df05d22784"},{"en":"I'm planning to move to Austin.","es":"Planeo mudarme a Austin.","img":"u:photo-1766040923580-16ad32fae8b4","v":"m","au":"5d5b6733ba"},{"en":"It's likely to be delayed.","es":"Es probable que se retrase.","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"bd5082139b"},{"en":"a New Year's resolution","es":"un propósito de Año Nuevo","img":"u:photo-1560986752-2e31d9507413","v":"m","au":"a4b8842d02"},{"en":"to follow through","es":"cumplir lo que uno se propone","img":"u:photo-1719299246416-b4c069be9caf","v":"f","au":"e807269d8a"},{"en":"to set a goal","es":"fijarse una meta","img":"u:photo-1562217180-021f74991332","v":"m","au":"aaaee26e89"},{"en":"a deadline","es":"una fecha límite","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"01b36cf6d5"},{"en":"to give it a shot","es":"intentarlo","img":"u:photo-1525201548942-d8732f6617a0","v":"m","au":"2bfe4c23d4"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I'm going to start saving for a house next year.","es":"Voy a empezar a ahorrar para una casa el próximo año.","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"f","au":"19b911d80e"},{"en":"We're flying to Seattle on Friday morning.","es":"Volamos a Seattle el viernes por la mañana.","img":"u:photo-1569629743817-70d8db6c323b","v":"m","au":"c0bd15d4e9"},{"en":"Shall I send you the report tonight?","es":"¿Te envío el informe esta noche?","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"584733ea31"},{"en":"I'll help you with the presentation, I promise.","es":"Te ayudaré con la presentación, lo prometo.","img":"u:photo-1576267423048-15c0040fec78","v":"m","au":"5533c524c2"},{"en":"The meeting is about to start. Please mute your phones.","es":"La reunión está a punto de empezar. Silencien sus celulares.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"75adcad7d4"},{"en":"Are you going to take the job in Denver?","es":"¿Vas a aceptar el trabajo en Denver?","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"m","au":"7d0e9dca36"}],"fill":[{"s":"I've already decided: I ___ quit sugar this year.","a":"am going to","o":["will","going"],"h":"intención ya decidida","full":"I've already decided: I am going to quit sugar this year.","au":"cb3df758e8"},{"s":"We're out of milk? Oh, I ___ get some on my way home.","a":"will","o":["am going to","go to"],"h":"decisión del momento","full":"We're out of milk? Oh, I will get some on my way home.","au":"9d3fe34783"},{"s":"___ I carry that box for you?","a":"Shall","o":["Will","Do"],"h":"ofrecimiento (Shall I...?)","full":"Shall I carry that box for you?","au":"a5025cbb48"},{"s":"Hurry up! The train is about ___ leave.","a":"to","o":["for","of"],"h":"be about to","full":"Hurry up! The train is about to leave.","au":"68446e8d74"},{"s":"We ___ dinner with the Garcías on Saturday. It's all arranged.","a":"are having","o":["will have","have"],"h":"plan acordado → presente continuo","full":"We are having dinner with the Garcías on Saturday. It's all arranged.","au":"b452459ae3"},{"s":"Don't worry, I ___ forget your birthday this time.","a":"won't","o":["am not","don't"],"h":"promesa negativa","full":"Don't worry, I won't forget your birthday this time.","au":"a43db19b52"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Planning the team retreat","es":"Planeando el retiro del equipo","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","lines":[{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"So, the retreat is in three weeks. What are we going to do about the venue?","au":"7f4b4fb01c"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"I've already called a lodge near Lake Tahoe. We're meeting the manager on Thursday.","au":"97d7c8993b"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"Great. And who's going to handle the catering?","au":"36cb9ab0a7"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"Hmm, nobody yet. Oh, I know! I'll ask Priya. She's organized events before.","au":"687d1af3e0"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"Perfect. The budget is tight, though. I think it'll be hard to get everything.","au":"fbb9eb8235"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"Don't worry. I'll send you a breakdown by Monday, I promise.","au":"45dbf2e50a"},{"who":"Laura","v":"f","t":"Shall I book the bus, then?","au":"88f8e8d5d6"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"Yes, please. I'm about to jump on a call, so I'll text you the details later.","au":"56b46d08a1"}],"q":[{"q":"When are they meeting the lodge manager?","a":"On Thursday.","o":["On Monday.","In three weeks."]},{"q":"Why does Mike suggest Priya?","a":"She has organized events before.","o":["She lives near Lake Tahoe.","She manages the budget."]},{"q":"What will Laura do?","a":"Book the bus.","o":["Call the lodge.","Prepare the catering."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about plans, arrangements, offers and promises.","es":"Hablar de planes, citas acordadas, ofrecimientos y promesas."},"warm":[{"q":"What are you going to do differently this year?","au":"436412c44e","es":"¿Qué vas a hacer diferente este año?","ex":"I'm going to exercise more and spend less money."},{"q":"Do you usually follow through on your New Year's resolutions?","au":"7d39080597","es":"¿Normalmente cumples tus propósitos de Año Nuevo?","ex":"Not really. I usually give up in February!"}],"reading":{"title":"Resolutions that actually work","img":"u:photo-1562217180-021f74991332","text":"Every January, millions of Americans say, \"This year I'm going to get in shape,\" or \"I'm going to save more money.\" By February, most of them have given up. Psychologist Mark Ellis, who runs a popular podcast in Seattle, says the problem isn't motivation; it's planning. \"An intention is not a plan,\" he explains. \"If you're going to run a marathon, decide when you're training. Put it in your calendar: I'm running with my neighbor on Tuesday at six.\" Ellis also recommends making promises to other people. \"When you tell a friend, 'I'll send you my progress every Sunday,' you're much more likely to follow through.\" His last tip is about small steps. \"Don't try to change your whole life at once. Set one realistic goal, give it a shot for thirty days, and then decide what's next.\" This year, Ellis is planning to learn Spanish. He has already booked his first class for next Monday.","au":"4fd678938d","q":[{"s":"Most people keep their resolutions until December.","a":"no"},{"s":"Mark Ellis thinks the main problem is planning.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He says an intention is the same as a plan.","a":"no"},{"s":"He recommends making promises to other people.","a":"yes"},{"s":"His first Spanish class is next Monday.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What are you going to do after this class?","a":"I'm going to have dinner and check my emails.","es":"¿Qué vas a hacer después de esta clase?","qau":"091c81bee7","aau":"1cf3d027b8"},{"q":"Are you doing anything special this weekend?","a":"Yes, I'm meeting some friends on Saturday.","es":"¿Vas a hacer algo especial este fin de semana?","qau":"f7e11631d9","aau":"75e3863680"},{"q":"Shall I explain it again?","a":"Yes, please. That would be great.","es":"¿Lo explico otra vez?","qau":"8d9c81e5bc","aau":"ec256ee30a"},{"q":"What goal have you set for this year?","a":"I'm going to improve my English and get a better job.","es":"¿Qué meta te has puesto para este año?","qau":"d0c5fc0dd7","aau":"dbf49ed356"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu plan para el próximo mes: 2 intenciones (going to), 2 citas ya acordadas (presente continuo) y 1 promesa (will).","kw":["going to","I'll"],"n":5,"model":"I'm going to wake up earlier. I'm going to read one book in English. I'm meeting my boss on Monday at ten. We're flying to Orlando on the 20th. I'll call my grandmother every Sunday, I promise."}}]},{"n":2,"title":"Possessive Adjectives","es":"Adjetivos posesivos","cover":"u:photo-1741156386380-0236c72eb6f9","parts":[{"id":"t2p1","topic":2,"part":1,"title":"My own, its vs. it's & body parts","es":"Own, its/it's y partes del cuerpo","acts":["learn","spanglishScan","fill","matchLines","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>🧍 <b>Partes del cuerpo y ropa</b>: el español usa artículo, el inglés usa <b>posesivo</b>. <i>Me duele <u>la</u> cabeza</i> → <b>My</b> head hurts. <i>Se quitó <u>los</u> zapatos</i> → He took off <b>his</b> shoes.</p>\n<p>🔀 El posesivo concuerda con el <b>dueño</b>, no con la cosa: <i>Mark called <b>his</b> sister · Ana called <b>her</b> brother.</i> (en español los dos son “su”).</p>\n<p>🐶 <b>its</b> = su (de una cosa/animal/empresa) · <b>it's</b> = it is / it has. <i>The company changed <b>its</b> logo. <b>It's</b> new.</i></p>\n<p>🏠 <b>own</b> refuerza la posesión: <i>my <b>own</b> car · a car of my <b>own</b> · I did it <b>on my own</b></i> (solo, sin ayuda).</p>","tips":["<b>its</b> e <b>it's</b> suenan igual: <i>its</i>. La diferencia solo se ve al escribir.","<b>your</b> y <b>you're</b> también suenan casi igual: <i>yor</i>.","En <b>their</b>, <b>there</b> y <b>they're</b> la pronunciación es la misma: <i>dér</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"my own place","es":"mi propio lugar","img":"u:photo-1666282167632-c613fbeb163c","v":"f","au":"97aaf6255d"},{"en":"a room of her own","es":"una habitación propia","img":"u:photo-1703783010857-9bd7a7b97c50","v":"f","au":"cf36bc9e81"},{"en":"on my own","es":"por mi cuenta, solo","img":"u:photo-1527824404775-dce343118ebc","v":"m","au":"7d824b5787"},{"en":"its battery","es":"su batería (de una cosa)","img":"u:photo-1557767382-97b28f5488e7","v":"m","au":"6e43f0cee0"},{"en":"It's broken.","es":"Está roto.","img":"u:photo-1643461394487-7e2856b215b8","v":"f","au":"cc1e6e50a5"},{"en":"She broke her arm.","es":"Se rompió el brazo.","img":"u:photo-1762347921012-79c5b5a7b9a0","v":"f","au":"1d2912360a"},{"en":"He shook his head.","es":"Negó con la cabeza.","img":"u:photo-1622566359362-539a508d6af5","v":"m","au":"218faa00da"},{"en":"Raise your hand.","es":"Levanta la mano.","img":"u:photo-1758270704286-83476deb3bd1","v":"f","au":"27e6f24df2"},{"en":"They lost their luggage.","es":"Perdieron su equipaje.","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"m","au":"3ec650e122"},{"en":"the company and its values","es":"la empresa y sus valores","img":"u:photo-1758691736975-9f7f643d178e","v":"f","au":"8da6d819c3"},{"en":"Mind your own business.","es":"No te metas en lo que no te importa.","img":"u:photo-1544717301-9cdcb1f5940f","v":"m","au":"d54d8033ab"},{"en":"your vs. you're","es":"your (tu) / you're (tú eres)","img":"#your ≠ you're","v":"f","au":"98fd012df7"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I finally have my own apartment in Brooklyn.","es":"Por fin tengo mi propio apartamento en Brooklyn.","img":"u:photo-1666282167632-c613fbeb163c","v":"f","au":"21083c5205"},{"en":"Carlos hurt his back moving furniture.","es":"Carlos se lastimó la espalda moviendo muebles.","img":"u:photo-1662534938224-d716af0d6127","v":"m","au":"f00618359a"},{"en":"The company changed its logo last year.","es":"La empresa cambió su logo el año pasado.","img":"u:photo-1551263640-1c007852f616","v":"f","au":"c9204d0521"},{"en":"Put your hands in your pockets. It's freezing!","es":"Mete las manos en los bolsillos. ¡Está helando!","img":"u:photo-1583170492868-dd617c96fdee","v":"m","au":"fd3a1f820d"},{"en":"She wants a business of her own.","es":"Ella quiere un negocio propio.","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"f","au":"2a343cd775"},{"en":"My neighbors painted their house bright blue.","es":"Mis vecinos pintaron su casa de azul brillante.","img":"u:photo-1555636222-cae831e670b3","v":"m","au":"452810a78a"}],"fill":[{"s":"I washed ___ hair this morning.","a":"my","o":["the","mine"],"h":"partes del cuerpo → posesivo","full":"I washed my hair this morning.","au":"4c6177b9a4"},{"s":"The dog wagged ___ tail when I got home.","a":"its","o":["it's","his"],"h":"its = su (de un animal/cosa)","full":"The dog wagged its tail when I got home.","au":"6c04b90aaf"},{"s":"___ going to be a long day.","a":"It's","o":["Its","It"],"h":"It's = It is","full":"It's going to be a long day.","au":"fa6795b748"},{"s":"María lives with ___ husband in Phoenix.","a":"her","o":["his","their"],"h":"su (de ella)","full":"María lives with her husband in Phoenix.","au":"9abe785a44"},{"s":"Mark called ___ sister last night.","a":"his","o":["her","its"],"h":"depende del dueño: Mark","full":"Mark called his sister last night.","au":"ce205bc406"},{"s":"I'd love to have a car of my ___.","a":"own","o":["self","mine"],"h":"of my own","full":"I'd love to have a car of my own.","au":"d0cf5d385f"},{"s":"Did you brush ___ teeth?","a":"your","o":["the","you're"],"h":"your = tu","full":"Did you brush your teeth?","au":"0a806c51f5"}],"goal":{"en":"To use possessive adjectives naturally, including own, its and body parts.","es":"Usar los adjetivos posesivos con naturalidad: own, its y partes del cuerpo."},"warm":[{"q":"Would you like to have a business of your own? Why?","au":"67509d4706","es":"¿Te gustaría tener un negocio propio? ¿Por qué?","ex":"Yes, I'd love to have my own café because I love coffee."},{"q":"Have you ever broken your arm or your leg?","au":"14d4bbb487","es":"¿Alguna vez te has roto el brazo o la pierna?","ex":"Yes, I broke my arm when I was ten."}],"reading":{"title":"A place of my own","img":"u:photo-1666282167632-c613fbeb163c","text":"For years, Paula shared an apartment in Queens with two roommates. Her room was tiny, its window faced a brick wall, and she never had a moment to herself. \"I love my friends,\" she says, \"but I needed a place of my own.\" Last spring she finally signed the lease for a small studio in Jersey City. It's not big, but it's hers, and its kitchen has a huge window with a view of the Manhattan skyline. The first weekend was chaotic. Paula painted the walls on her own, hurt her back carrying a mirror, and cut her finger opening a box. Her brother came over with his toolbox and helped her hang the shelves. \"My neighbors are lovely,\" she adds. \"Their dog wags its tail every time I come home.\" Now Paula works from her own desk, cooks her own meals, and decorates the place her way. \"It's my little kingdom,\" she laughs.","au":"33352d306b","q":[{"s":"Paula used to live with two roommates.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her old room had a beautiful view.","a":"no"},{"s":"She painted the walls with her brother.","a":"no"},{"s":"She hurt her back carrying a mirror.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her neighbors' dog is unfriendly.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you have your own car?","a":"Yes, I have my own car. It's a small Toyota.","es":"¿Tienes tu propio carro?","qau":"a920a3d7b6","aau":"ab4d2dbcad"},{"q":"What does a company show on its website?","a":"It shows its products, its prices and its values.","es":"¿Qué muestra una empresa en su página web?","qau":"8cf5376a1c","aau":"e73e8a1476"},{"q":"What do you do when your head hurts?","a":"When my head hurts, I take a pill and rest.","es":"¿Qué haces cuando te duele la cabeza?","qau":"db0182d99d","aau":"87f5c8fc7e"},{"q":"Did you learn English on your own?","a":"Not completely. I've had teachers, but I also practice on my own.","es":"¿Aprendiste inglés por tu cuenta?","qau":"f191a586be","aau":"9f9033bf25"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe tu casa o tu cuarto ideal usando my own / of my own, its, y una frase con una parte del cuerpo (ej. I hurt my...).","kw":["own","its"],"n":5,"model":"I'd love a house of my own near the beach. Its kitchen would be big and bright. I'd have my own office. My brother would visit with his kids. Last year I hurt my knee moving, so I want a house with no stairs!"}},{"id":"t2p2","topic":2,"part":2,"title":"Whose? 's or of?","es":"¿De quién? 's u of","acts":["learn","apostropheLab","fill","dialogue","oddOneOut","speak"],"tip":"<p>👤 <b>'s</b> para personas, animales, empresas y lugares: <i>my boss<b>'s</b> office · Apple<b>'s</b> CEO · New York<b>'s</b> skyline</i>.</p>\n<p>👥 Plural terminado en -s → solo apóstrofo: <i>my parent<b>s'</b> house</i>. Plural irregular → <b>'s</b>: <i>the children<b>'s</b> toys, women<b>'s</b> shoes</i>.</p>\n<p>📄 <b>of</b> para cosas y partes: <i>the end <b>of</b> the movie · the top <b>of</b> the page</i> (no <i>the movie's end</i>, aunque a veces se oye).</p>\n<p>⏳ Tiempo con 's: <i>a day<b>'s</b> work · two week<b>s'</b> vacation</i>. Casa/negocio: <i>at my sister<b>'s</b></i> (= en casa de mi hermana), <i>at the dentist<b>'s</b></i>.</p>\n<p>❓ <b>whose</b> = ¿de quién? / cuyo: <i><b>Whose</b> phone is this? · the man <b>whose</b> car was stolen</i>.</p>","tips":["<b>boss's</b> se pronuncia con una sílaba extra: <i>bósiz</i>.","<b>parents'</b> suena igual que <b>parents</b>: el apóstrofo no se oye.","<b>Whose</b> y <b>who's</b> suenan igual: <i>jus</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"Whose phone is this?","es":"¿De quién es este celular?","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"f","au":"660c924c10"},{"en":"my boss's office","es":"la oficina de mi jefe","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","v":"m","au":"cc0085a2c9"},{"en":"my parents' house","es":"la casa de mis padres","img":"u:photo-1570129477492-45c003edd2be","v":"f","au":"ae501d3842"},{"en":"the children's toys","es":"los juguetes de los niños","img":"u:photo-1627764940620-90393d0e8c34","v":"m","au":"c38bd2e897"},{"en":"the end of the movie","es":"el final de la película","img":"u:photo-1702308954905-341065817003","v":"f","au":"f0bc682562"},{"en":"the top of the page","es":"la parte de arriba de la página","img":"u:photo-1524639064490-254e0a1db723","v":"m","au":"459f38453d"},{"en":"a day's work","es":"el trabajo de un día","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"c7644c5849"},{"en":"at my sister's","es":"en casa de mi hermana","img":"u:photo-1663627650051-9fdc3a53a075","v":"m","au":"07437fc8ea"},{"en":"James and Ana's wedding","es":"la boda de James y Ana","img":"u:photo-1536567307162-551e460b7fc2","v":"f","au":"4d21d7a9ed"},{"en":"the man whose car was stolen","es":"el hombre cuyo carro fue robado","img":"u:photo-1556474835-47da4fcf709c","v":"m","au":"44612cd92e"},{"en":"the company's profits","es":"las ganancias de la empresa","img":"u:photo-1590283603385-17ffb3a7f29f","v":"f","au":"cb8a72f5cd"},{"en":"New York's skyline","es":"el horizonte de Nueva York","img":"u:photo-1477959858617-67f85cf4f1df","v":"m","au":"060a200902"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Whose jacket is on the back of my chair?","es":"¿De quién es la chaqueta en el respaldo de mi silla?","img":"u:photo-1754386738300-bb6b4af09657","v":"f","au":"1fbdb88c45"},{"en":"We're staying at my in-laws' place in San Diego.","es":"Nos quedamos en casa de mis suegros en San Diego.","img":"u:photo-1570129477492-45c003edd2be","v":"m","au":"0c73ecffd6"},{"en":"The end of the meeting was a bit tense.","es":"El final de la reunión fue un poco tenso.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"a304a08211"},{"en":"That's the woman whose son plays for the Lakers.","es":"Esa es la mujer cuyo hijo juega para los Lakers.","img":"u:photo-1533923156502-be31530547c4","v":"m","au":"8d7293f2d1"},{"en":"I really need a good night's sleep.","es":"De verdad necesito una buena noche de sueño.","img":"u:photo-1531353826977-0941b4779a1c","v":"f","au":"b9c466064c"},{"en":"The company's new CEO starts next week.","es":"El nuevo CEO de la empresa empieza la próxima semana.","img":"u:photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a","v":"m","au":"f58b48981c"}],"fill":[{"s":"This is my ___ new car.","a":"brother's","o":["brothers","brother"],"h":"un hermano → 's","full":"This is my brother's new car.","au":"4335bdc6ad"},{"s":"The ___ locker room is on the left.","a":"women's","o":["womens'","women"],"h":"plural irregular + 's","full":"The women's locker room is on the left.","au":"f190c11742"},{"s":"We had dinner at the ___ house.","a":"Johnsons'","o":["Johnson's","Johnsons"],"h":"la familia Johnson → s'","full":"We had dinner at the Johnsons' house.","au":"6bdaf43fb0"},{"s":"The ___ of the table is broken.","a":"leg","o":["leg's","legs'"],"h":"cosa → of","full":"The leg of the table is broken.","au":"27ea11004d"},{"s":"I'm taking two ___ vacation in July.","a":"weeks'","o":["week's","weeks"],"h":"expresión de tiempo en plural","full":"I'm taking two weeks' vacation in July.","au":"ece9a168b3"},{"s":"The student ___ laptop was stolen called the police.","a":"whose","o":["who's","who"],"h":"whose = cuyo","full":"The student whose laptop was stolen called the police.","au":"6e05c73d88"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Moving into a shared apartment","es":"Mudándose a un apartamento compartido","img":"u:photo-1766040923580-16ad32fae8b4","lines":[{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Okay, whose boxes are these in the hallway?","au":"fa4a79b090"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"The big ones are my sister's. She's picking them up on Sunday.","au":"6cad755bbf"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Got it. And the bike by the door? Is it Jake's?","au":"65acacfc78"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"No, Jake's bike is in the garage. That one belongs to the neighbors' son.","au":"d763be04b9"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Ha! Well, the end of the hallway is going to be my office corner.","au":"0eae62378e"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"Fine by me. Just don't touch the plants. They're my mom's.","au":"8a3a25b1a8"},{"who":"Sam","v":"m","t":"Deal. By the way, whose idea was it to paint the kitchen orange?","au":"5c39b18126"},{"who":"Nina","v":"f","t":"The landlord's! Don't look at me.","au":"c672a64eb9"}],"q":[{"q":"Whose are the big boxes?","a":"Nina's sister's.","o":["Sam's.","The neighbors'."]},{"q":"Where is Jake's bike?","a":"In the garage.","o":["By the door.","In the hallway."]},{"q":"Whose idea was the orange kitchen?","a":"The landlord's.","o":["Nina's mom's.","Sam's."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To show possession with 's, s', of and whose.","es":"Expresar posesión con 's, s', of y whose."},"warm":[{"q":"Whose advice do you usually follow?","au":"2557dd504b","es":"¿De quién sigues normalmente los consejos?","ex":"I usually follow my mother's advice."},{"q":"Do you prefer to stay at a hotel or at a relative's house when you travel?","au":"42c2a8ab76","es":"¿Prefieres quedarte en un hotel o en casa de un familiar cuando viajas?","ex":"I prefer a hotel, but I sometimes stay at my aunt's."}],"reading":{"title":"The mystery of the missing cake","img":"u:photo-1464349153735-7db50ed83c84","text":"It was my parents' thirtieth wedding anniversary, and the whole family was at my sister's house in Tampa. My brother-in-law's famous chocolate cake was waiting in the kitchen. At the end of the dinner, my nephew ran in shouting, \"The cake is gone!\" Everyone looked at the dog, but Max's bowl was clean, and the cake's box was still on the counter, empty. Whose idea was this? My cousins' kids were playing in the yard, so they couldn't have done it. Then I noticed chocolate on the corner of my uncle's mouth. He smiled. \"A man whose wife has put him on a diet,\" he said, \"deserves a break once in a while.\" We all laughed. In the end, my mother's neighbor saved the night: she brought over a pie from the bakery at the end of the street. It wasn't a day's work, but it was delicious.","au":"093a69818c","q":[{"s":"The party was at the writer's sister's house.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The cake was made by the brother-in-law.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The dog ate the cake.","a":"no"},{"s":"The uncle's wife had put him on a diet.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The neighbor baked a new chocolate cake.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Whose phone is that?","a":"It's my sister's phone.","es":"¿De quién es ese celular?","qau":"ac77245b14","aau":"70ae2eaf2b"},{"q":"What's your best friend's name?","a":"My best friend's name is Laura.","es":"¿Cómo se llama tu mejor amigo(a)?","qau":"84c6106dc9","aau":"d201f48558"},{"q":"Where do you spend the holidays?","a":"Usually at my parents' house.","es":"¿Dónde pasas las fiestas?","qau":"11ddf50971","aau":"b7dab10da6"},{"q":"What's at the end of your street?","a":"There's a small park at the end of my street.","es":"¿Qué hay al final de tu calle?","qau":"ab7969f0c9","aau":"b5909ba8ca"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 5 oraciones sobre tu familia o tu trabajo usando 's, s', of y whose (ej. My parents' house..., the end of..., a friend whose...).","kw":["'s","whose"],"n":5,"model":"My parents' house is in Houston. My brother's wife is a nurse. The top of my desk is always messy. I have a coworker whose son lives in Japan. I need a week's vacation!"}}]},{"n":3,"title":"Possessive Pronouns","es":"Pronombres posesivos","cover":"u:photo-1627638822925-c9eb55d07f3f","parts":[{"id":"t3p1","topic":3,"part":1,"title":"Mine, yours, theirs: whose is it?","es":"Mine, yours, theirs: ¿de quién es?","acts":["learn","lostFound","fill","sort","bubblePop","speak"],"tip":"<p>Los <b>pronombres posesivos</b> reemplazan <b>adjetivo + sustantivo</b>: <i>This is <u>my laptop</u> → This laptop is <b>mine</b>.</i></p>\n<p>my → <b>mine</b> · your → <b>yours</b> · his → <b>his</b> · her → <b>hers</b> · our → <b>ours</b> · their → <b>theirs</b></p>\n<p>⚠️ <b>Nunca</b> llevan artículo ni apóstrofo: <s>the mine</s>, <s>your's</s>, <s>her's</s>. Tampoco cambian en plural: <i>These keys are <b>mine</b></i> (no <s>mines</s>).</p>\n<p>❓ <b>Whose is it?</b> / <b>Whose is this?</b> = ¿De quién es? → <i>It's <b>hers</b>.</i></p>","tips":["<b>yours</b> suena <i>yors</i>, <b>ours</b> suena <i>áuers</i> o <i>ars</i>.","<b>theirs</b> suena <i>ders</i>, con la lengua entre los dientes al inicio.","En <b>hers</b> la h se aspira suave: <i>jers</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"It's mine.","es":"Es mío.","img":"u:photo-1790336829851-b07dc80776e8","v":"m","au":"ba8934b087"},{"en":"Is this yours?","es":"¿Esto es tuyo?","img":"u:photo-1672819030357-464e40e5abd8","v":"f","au":"2b6e4f6905"},{"en":"That one is hers.","es":"Ese es de ella.","img":"u:photo-1641736494066-bd18237ede26","v":"f","au":"b7c3bb3f59"},{"en":"The decision is his.","es":"La decisión es de él.","img":"u:photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a","v":"m","au":"79332ca426"},{"en":"The victory is ours.","es":"La victoria es nuestra.","img":"u:photo-1758691737584-a8f17fb34475","v":"m","au":"204649f8e0"},{"en":"The house is theirs.","es":"La casa es de ellos.","img":"u:photo-1570129477492-45c003edd2be","v":"f","au":"4887894f3e"},{"en":"Whose is it?","es":"¿De quién es?","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"f","au":"2aa2112290"},{"en":"Mine's the red one.","es":"El mío es el rojo.","img":"u:photo-1666375311741-f926eb70ad4b","v":"m","au":"63ab94b7b3"},{"en":"Your idea is better than mine.","es":"Tu idea es mejor que la mía.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"e85ac81a13"},{"en":"Theirs is bigger.","es":"El de ellos es más grande.","img":"u:photo-1565883969738-05b2e01c47b9","v":"m","au":"825bcca937"},{"en":"I borrowed hers.","es":"Tomé prestado el de ella.","img":"u:photo-1598024055266-e772a5f8c128","v":"f","au":"20d273828a"},{"en":"Hands off, that's ours!","es":"¡No lo toques, eso es nuestro!","img":"u:photo-1713946598491-4f85decbeaaf","v":"m","au":"f1029be437"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Excuse me, I think that seat is mine.","es":"Disculpe, creo que ese asiento es mío.","img":"u:photo-1790579985325-558e18dc6c19","v":"f","au":"9c7e92e17f"},{"en":"Is this charger yours or hers?","es":"¿Este cargador es tuyo o de ella?","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"m","au":"b804f2e16c"},{"en":"Our office is small, but theirs is huge.","es":"Nuestra oficina es pequeña, pero la de ellos es enorme.","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","v":"f","au":"dfe5ade25f"},{"en":"A colleague of mine lives in Atlanta.","es":"Un colega mío vive en Atlanta.","img":"u:photo-1576267423048-15c0040fec78","v":"m","au":"85fa92db3d"},{"en":"Whose suitcase is this? It's ours.","es":"¿De quién es esta maleta? Es nuestra.","img":"u:photo-1648737967037-96967e9151b5","v":"f","au":"46b1ebc272"},{"en":"The choice is yours.","es":"La decisión es tuya.","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"m","au":"eb81ead2a3"}],"fill":[{"s":"That isn't your coffee. It's ___.","a":"mine","o":["my","me"],"h":"pronombre sin sustantivo","full":"That isn't your coffee. It's mine.","au":"95686f9af3"},{"s":"Is this umbrella ___?","a":"yours","o":["your","your's"],"h":"sin apóstrofo","full":"Is this umbrella yours?","au":"c072813357"},{"s":"Their kids are older than ___.","a":"ours","o":["our","us"],"h":"el de nosotros","full":"Their kids are older than ours.","au":"fa308983a1"},{"s":"The idea was ___, not his.","a":"hers","o":["her","her's"],"h":"de ella (sin apóstrofo)","full":"The idea was hers, not his.","au":"758ae0538b"},{"s":"___ is the gray car next to the elevator.","a":"Mine","o":["My","Me"],"h":"el mío","full":"Mine is the gray car next to the elevator.","au":"6cc31e6a7c"},{"s":"Those aren't my keys. ___ have a red keychain.","a":"Mine","o":["My","Mines"],"h":"mine (nunca \"mines\")","full":"Those aren't my keys. Mine have a red keychain.","au":"365138b423"}],"sort":{"cats":["Adjective + noun","Pronoun alone"],"items":[{"w":"my bag","c":"Adjective + noun","au":"57e40760a1"},{"w":"your seat","c":"Adjective + noun","au":"2a66c38385"},{"w":"her idea","c":"Adjective + noun","au":"629c206b6c"},{"w":"their house","c":"Adjective + noun","au":"aa9013939a"},{"w":"our team","c":"Adjective + noun","au":"35323504bc"},{"w":"mine","c":"Pronoun alone","au":"7739f69a50"},{"w":"yours","c":"Pronoun alone","au":"220ca735ed"},{"w":"hers","c":"Pronoun alone","au":"1a68208e41"},{"w":"theirs","c":"Pronoun alone","au":"77cee9cd37"},{"w":"ours","c":"Pronoun alone","au":"0fd3386d0d"}]},"goal":{"en":"To use possessive pronouns to talk about who owns what.","es":"Usar los pronombres posesivos para hablar de quién es dueño de qué."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever taken someone else's bag or umbrella by mistake?","au":"28add915e2","es":"¿Alguna vez te has llevado el bolso o el paraguas de otra persona por error?","ex":"Yes! I once took my coworker's umbrella."},{"q":"Is your neighborhood quieter or noisier than your parents'?","au":"86f03d0463","es":"¿Tu barrio es más tranquilo o más ruidoso que el de tus padres?","ex":"Mine is noisier than theirs. I live downtown."}],"reading":{"title":"The hotel's lost and found","img":"u:photo-1759038085950-1234ca8f5fed","text":"Maya works at the front desk of a busy hotel in downtown Nashville, and her favorite part of the job is the lost and found. \"Guests leave everything here,\" she says. \"Phones, laptops, guitars, even a wedding dress once.\" Returning things is harder than it sounds. Last month two guests claimed the same black suitcase. \"It's mine,\" said the first man. \"No, it's mine,\" the other insisted. Maya asked a simple question: \"What's inside yours?\" The first man said, \"Shirts and a camera.\" The second said, \"Mine has a cowboy hat on top.\" She opened it, and there was the hat. The suitcase was his. Another time, a couple called from the airport. \"We left our tablet in the room. Is it there?\" It was, but there was also a pink tablet. \"Ours is silver,\" they explained, \"so the pink one isn't ours.\" Maya laughs: \"Every object has a story. My job is to find whose story it is.\"","au":"64b4cb51d0","q":[{"s":"Maya works at a hotel in Nashville.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Someone once left a wedding dress at the hotel.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Both men said the black suitcase was theirs.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The suitcase belonged to the first man.","a":"no"},{"s":"The couple's tablet was pink.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Is this pen yours?","a":"No, it isn't mine. I think it's hers.","es":"¿Este bolígrafo es tuyo?","qau":"56522bdf66","aau":"d3f01a953a"},{"q":"Whose car is that?","a":"It's ours. We bought it last year.","es":"¿De quién es ese carro?","qau":"0d27dedefc","aau":"76d4aa6643"},{"q":"Is your phone the same as mine?","a":"No, mine is older than yours.","es":"¿Tu celular es igual al mío?","qau":"77bea49c29","aau":"5098cc08c5"},{"q":"Whose idea was it?","a":"It was theirs, not ours.","es":"¿De quién fue la idea?","qau":"5b0806bb7e","aau":"0c76413f5e"}],"hw":{"es":"Imagina que trabajas en objetos perdidos. Escribe 5 oraciones con mine, yours, his, hers, ours o theirs (ej. The black umbrella is hers).","kw":["mine","theirs"],"n":5,"model":"The black umbrella is hers. The laptop is his because it has his name on it. These keys aren't mine. The two suitcases are theirs. Is this phone yours?"}},{"id":"t3p2","topic":3,"part":2,"title":"A friend of mine & typical errors","es":"A friend of mine y errores típicos","acts":["learn","gavelJudge","dialogue","fill","catchWord","speak"],"tip":"<p>👫 <b>Doble posesivo</b>: <i>un amigo mío</i> = <b>a friend of mine</b> (no <s>a friend of me</s>). Igual: <i>a cousin <b>of hers</b>, a habit <b>of his</b>, this car <b>of ours</b></i>.</p>\n<p>✂️ <b>Elipsis</b>: el pronombre evita repetir: <i>My flight was canceled, and so was <b>theirs</b>. · My phone is old. <b>Mine</b> too.</i></p>\n<p>❗ <b>Whose</b> (de quién) ≠ <b>Who's</b> (who is / who has): <i><b>Whose</b> turn is it? · <b>Who's</b> coming tonight?</i></p>\n<p>🚫 Errores típicos del hispanohablante: <s>the mine</s> → <b>mine</b> · <s>Is yours this?</s> → <b>Is this yours?</b> · <s>a friend of him</s> → <b>a friend of his</b>.</p>","tips":["<b>a friend of mine</b> se dice de corrido: <i>afréndovmáin</i>.","En <b>Whose turn</b> la s se une a la t: <i>jus-térn</i>.","<b>So is mine</b>: el acento va en <b>mine</b>."],"vocab":[{"en":"a cousin of hers","es":"una prima de ella","img":"u:photo-1663627650051-9fdc3a53a075","v":"f","au":"c266225420"},{"en":"an old classmate of his","es":"un viejo compañero de él","img":"u:photo-1758270704763-22072a90d3b6","v":"m","au":"c0808f995b"},{"en":"this car of ours","es":"este carro nuestro","img":"u:photo-1666375311741-f926eb70ad4b","v":"f","au":"7e010639a7"},{"en":"Who's coming?","es":"¿Quién viene?","img":"u:photo-1621112904887-419379ce6824","v":"m","au":"f9fb46b2e4"},{"en":"Whose turn is it?","es":"¿A quién le toca?","img":"u:photo-1503482618211-c70b46ede8b0","v":"f","au":"759178078e"},{"en":"So is mine.","es":"El mío también.","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"m","au":"8d6cd5fea0"},{"en":"Mine too.","es":"El mío también (informal).","img":"u:photo-1713946598491-4f85decbeaaf","v":"f","au":"04391fd3f2"},{"en":"Neither is ours.","es":"El nuestro tampoco.","img":"u:photo-1760623681430-9224e69d9683","v":"f","au":"3516ce2a6c"},{"en":"That's none of your business.","es":"Eso no es asunto tuyo.","img":"u:photo-1544717301-9cdcb1f5940f","v":"m","au":"d48abf3c44"},{"en":"It's anyone's guess.","es":"Nadie lo sabe con certeza.","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"m","au":"855626108a"},{"en":"My home is yours.","es":"Mi casa es tu casa.","img":"u:photo-1675179181127-2c0666e2334d","v":"f","au":"a66bbc1211"},{"en":"your fair share","es":"tu parte justa","img":"u:photo-1778795165220-954068f205c6","v":"f","au":"61216f8fb3"}],"sentences":[{"en":"A coworker of mine just moved to Portland.","es":"Un compañero de trabajo mío se acaba de mudar a Portland.","img":"u:photo-1713947505221-8a11da8aa744","v":"f","au":"83843c01d9"},{"en":"Whose turn is it to wash the dishes?","es":"¿A quién le toca lavar los platos?","img":"u:photo-1484632105053-8662f3194e7f","v":"m","au":"dd0315db16"},{"en":"My flight was canceled, and so was theirs.","es":"Mi vuelo fue cancelado, y el de ellos también.","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"70e83ce0a4"},{"en":"That's an old habit of his.","es":"Es una vieja costumbre de él.","img":"u:photo-1495020689067-958852a7765e","v":"m","au":"06f78326c9"},{"en":"This neighborhood of ours is getting expensive.","es":"Este barrio nuestro se está poniendo caro.","img":"u:photo-1555636222-cae831e670b3","v":"f","au":"84893b9554"},{"en":"Who's going to pay for all this?","es":"¿Quién va a pagar todo esto?","img":"u:photo-1556742031-c6961e8560b0","v":"m","au":"9e6a279ce5"}],"fill":[{"s":"Lucy is a close friend of ___.","a":"mine","o":["me","my"],"h":"a friend of mine","full":"Lucy is a close friend of mine.","au":"23259051c3"},{"s":"___ car is parked outside?","a":"Whose","o":["Who's","Who"],"h":"¿de quién?","full":"Whose car is parked outside?","au":"fb17348015"},{"s":"___ ready to order?","a":"Who's","o":["Whose","Who"],"h":"who is","full":"Who's ready to order?","au":"39dd838393"},{"s":"My phone died, and so did ___.","a":"hers","o":["her","she's"],"h":"elipsis con pronombre","full":"My phone died, and so did hers.","au":"5ce24f8f23"},{"s":"This is a favorite song of ___.","a":"his","o":["him","he"],"h":"of + pronombre posesivo","full":"This is a favorite song of his.","au":"5c8145ee4f"},{"s":"Our office is bigger than ___.","a":"theirs","o":["their","them"],"h":"comparación","full":"Our office is bigger than theirs.","au":"642c6a4f28"},{"s":"I forgot my laptop. Can I use ___?","a":"yours","o":["your","you"],"h":"sin sustantivo","full":"I forgot my laptop. Can I use yours?","au":"4a64b569fe"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Lost and found at the coworking space","es":"Objetos perdidos en el coworking","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","lines":[{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Hi, Diego. Someone left a gray hoodie in the meeting room. Is it yours?","au":"cc707298c0"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Not mine. Mine is navy blue. Maybe it's Kevin's?","au":"93a8a36d3c"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Kevin's isn't gray either. Whose could it be?","au":"816666cd48"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Oh, wait. A friend of mine came by yesterday. I think it's hers.","au":"8cc85e217d"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Okay. And these headphones? There's a sticker with a cactus on them.","au":"9094d44a8c"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Those are definitely Tom's. That cactus sticker is a running joke of his.","au":"1c0a663ab1"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Ha! Great. Who's going to give them back to him?","au":"ddfc8a5c94"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"I will. His desk is next to mine.","au":"c88a55d755"}],"q":[{"q":"What color is Diego's hoodie?","a":"Navy blue.","o":["Gray.","Black."]},{"q":"Whose is the gray hoodie, probably?","a":"A friend of Diego's.","o":["Kevin's.","Rachel's."]},{"q":"Why will Diego return the headphones?","a":"Tom's desk is next to his.","o":["They are his.","Rachel asked Kevin."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To use double possessives and avoid typical errors with possessive pronouns.","es":"Usar el doble posesivo y evitar errores típicos con los pronombres posesivos."},"warm":[{"q":"Tell me about a friend of yours who lives in another country.","au":"ef2d145bcd","es":"Háblame de un amigo tuyo que viva en otro país.","ex":"A friend of mine lives in Canada. She's a nurse in Toronto."},{"q":"Whose opinion matters most to you when you make a big decision?","au":"eee3ba5319","es":"¿De quién es la opinión que más te importa cuando tomas una gran decisión?","ex":"My wife's opinion matters most to me."}],"reading":{"title":"A friend of mine, a lesson of mine","img":"u:photo-1583606784123-7c244f00d29c","text":"When I moved to Los Angeles from Monterrey, my English was good, but a few small mistakes kept showing up. My first week at work, I told my manager, \"Mr. Reed, a friend of me wants to apply here.\" He smiled and said, \"You mean a friend of mine?\" I was embarrassed, but he explained it kindly. A week later I asked a coworker, \"Is yours this coffee?\" She laughed and answered, \"Is this yours? No, it's Kevin's. Mine is the one with the cat.\" Little by little, I started noticing the rule: possessive pronouns stand alone. Nobody says \"the mine\" or \"mines.\" Now I help new employees from Latin America. A colleague of ours from Lima recently asked me, \"Who's laptop is this?\" I told him, \"Who's means who is. You need whose.\" He wrote it down. Mistakes aren't a problem; they're simply part of the process. This lesson of mine might help you, too.","au":"fdbb075b1c","q":[{"s":"The writer moved to Los Angeles from Monterrey.","a":"yes"},{"s":"His manager was angry about his mistake.","a":"no"},{"s":"The coffee belonged to Kevin.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The coworker's cup has a dog on it.","a":"no"},{"s":"The writer now helps new employees with their English.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Can you tell me about a friend of yours?","a":"Sure. A friend of mine is a chef in Miami.","es":"¿Me puedes hablar de un amigo tuyo?","qau":"e42431224e","aau":"111144412d"},{"q":"Who's coming to the party tonight?","a":"Ana and Luis are coming, but Mark isn't.","es":"¿Quién viene a la fiesta esta noche?","qau":"b41c7f76ad","aau":"210efae548"},{"q":"My phone is always dying. What about yours?","a":"Mine too. The battery is terrible.","es":"A mi celular siempre se le acaba la batería. ¿Y el tuyo?","qau":"2b79c0d9b6","aau":"4456230e29"},{"q":"Whose turn is it to pay?","a":"It's yours! I paid last time.","es":"¿A quién le toca pagar?","qau":"efdb12edb8","aau":"acbdb532f7"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un párrafo corto sobre 'a friend of mine' y usa también whose, who's y una elipsis (ej. My job is stressful, and so is his).","kw":["of mine","whose"],"n":5,"model":"A friend of mine, Sara, lives in Denver. She's a designer whose clients are all over the world. Who's her biggest client? A tech company in Seattle. Her job is stressful, and so is mine. Her apartment is bigger than mine, but mine is cheaper!"}}]},{"n":4,"title":"The Present Perfect","es":"El presente perfecto","cover":"u:photo-1527333656061-ca7adf608ae1","parts":[{"id":"t4p1","topic":4,"part":1,"title":"Life experiences: ever, never, just, already, yet","es":"Experiencias: ever, never, just, already, yet","acts":["learn","bucketList","fill","listenChoose","spinWheel","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>presente perfecto</b> = <b>have / has + participio</b>: <i>I <b>have seen</b>, she <b>has tried</b></i>.</p>\n<p>🌎 Úsalo para <b>experiencias de vida</b> sin decir cuándo: <i>I'<b>ve been</b> to Mexico three times.</i> Si dices cuándo, cambia a pasado simple.</p>\n<p>🔑 Palabras clave: <b>ever</b> (alguna vez, en preguntas) · <b>never</b> (nunca) · <b>just</b> (acabar de) · <b>already</b> (ya, afirmativo) · <b>yet</b> (ya / todavía, en preguntas y negativas, al final).</p>\n<p>✈️ <b>been</b> = fue y volvió · <b>gone</b> = se fue y sigue allá: <i>She's <b>been</b> to Paris</i> vs <i>She's <b>gone</b> to Paris</i>.</p>","tips":["Contrae siempre en conversación: <b>I've</b> (<i>aiv</i>), <b>she's</b>, <b>haven't</b> (<i>jávent</i>).","<b>already</b> suena <i>olrédi</i>; <b>yet</b> suena <i>yet</i>, no <i>jet</i>.","En <b>Have you ever</b> se une todo: <i>javiuéver</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"Have you ever been to Alaska?","es":"¿Alguna vez has ido a Alaska?","img":"u:photo-1673114819432-1aa36952dd3e","v":"f","au":"a4ff72d9e8"},{"en":"I've never tried sushi.","es":"Nunca he probado el sushi.","img":"u:photo-1553621042-f6e147245754","v":"m","au":"6b484cadbf"},{"en":"She's just landed.","es":"Ella acaba de aterrizar.","img":"u:photo-1783809728662-f96dc769be0e","v":"f","au":"bd5548872a"},{"en":"I've already paid.","es":"Ya pagué.","img":"u:photo-1556742031-c6961e8560b0","v":"m","au":"a2d366f038"},{"en":"Have you finished yet?","es":"¿Ya terminaste?","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"3e9a883458"},{"en":"I haven't decided yet.","es":"Todavía no he decidido.","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"m","au":"2f42e22da3"},{"en":"once in a lifetime","es":"una vez en la vida","img":"u:photo-1531366936337-7c912a4589a7","v":"f","au":"feec59ab3f"},{"en":"to go skydiving","es":"hacer paracaidismo","img":"u:photo-1659221876406-31a3746f41b9","v":"m","au":"3ea387ba05"},{"en":"to run a marathon","es":"correr una maratón","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"f","au":"a670b7606d"},{"en":"a bucket list","es":"lista de cosas por hacer en la vida","img":"u:photo-1562217180-021f74991332","v":"m","au":"75aa1a8969"},{"en":"been vs. gone","es":"fue y volvió / se fue y sigue allá","img":"#been ≠ gone","v":"f","au":"1a52e28c75"},{"en":"so far","es":"hasta ahora","img":"u:photo-1672819030357-464e40e5abd8","v":"m","au":"9b7768cf77"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Have you ever eaten alligator in New Orleans?","es":"¿Alguna vez has comido caimán en Nueva Orleans?","img":"u:photo-1772223883618-2fc68b7fe8b9","v":"f","au":"aee791976a"},{"en":"I've never seen the Grand Canyon, but it's on my bucket list.","es":"Nunca he visto el Gran Cañón, pero está en mi lista.","img":"u:photo-1527333656061-ca7adf608ae1","v":"m","au":"8d30ae1b40"},{"en":"We've just signed the contract!","es":"¡Acabamos de firmar el contrato!","img":"u:photo-1549923746-c502d488b3ea","v":"f","au":"eb3994fd2d"},{"en":"Has the package arrived yet?","es":"¿Ya llegó el paquete?","img":"u:photo-1630448927918-1dbcd8ba439b","v":"m","au":"db45c42e7e"},{"en":"I've already sent the invoice.","es":"Ya envié la factura.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"5f11305f32"},{"en":"She's gone to Chicago for a conference.","es":"Se fue a Chicago a una conferencia.","img":"u:photo-1527824404775-dce343118ebc","v":"m","au":"3d904e9960"}],"fill":[{"s":"Have you ___ been to Las Vegas?","a":"ever","o":["never","yet"],"h":"pregunta sobre experiencia","full":"Have you ever been to Las Vegas?","au":"85af744e62"},{"s":"I've ___ tried skydiving. I'm too scared!","a":"never","o":["ever","yet"],"h":"nunca","full":"I've never tried skydiving. I'm too scared!","au":"b1d3eb2419"},{"s":"Has Kevin finished the report ___?","a":"yet","o":["already","just"],"h":"al final de la pregunta","full":"Has Kevin finished the report yet?","au":"cf3c019c1e"},{"s":"The taxi has ___ arrived. Let's go!","a":"just","o":["yet","ever"],"h":"hace un instante","full":"The taxi has just arrived. Let's go!","au":"b4bbc8ff66"},{"s":"I've ___ booked the hotel, so don't worry.","a":"already","o":["yet","ever"],"h":"ya (afirmativo)","full":"I've already booked the hotel, so don't worry.","au":"31b34efd44"},{"s":"They've ___ to Hawaii twice. They loved it.","a":"been","o":["gone","went"],"h":"fueron y volvieron","full":"They've been to Hawaii twice. They loved it.","au":"2e0f741cd9"},{"s":"Max isn't here. He's ___ to the gym.","a":"gone","o":["been","went"],"h":"se fue y sigue allá","full":"Max isn't here. He's gone to the gym.","au":"f0752acb90"}],"goal":{"en":"To talk about life experiences and recent events with the present perfect.","es":"Hablar de experiencias de vida y eventos recientes con el presente perfecto."},"warm":[{"q":"What's the most exciting place you've ever been to?","au":"f01e1d2c0b","es":"¿Cuál es el lugar más emocionante en el que has estado?","ex":"The most exciting place I've ever been to is New York."},{"q":"Is there anything on your bucket list that you haven't done yet?","au":"df36252972","es":"¿Hay algo en tu lista de sueños que todavía no hayas hecho?","ex":"Yes, I haven't seen the northern lights yet."}],"reading":{"title":"Fifty before fifty","img":"u:photo-1562217180-021f74991332","text":"When Rebecca Lin turned forty, she wrote a list called \"Fifty Before Fifty\": fifty experiences she wanted to have before her fiftieth birthday. Eight years later, she has already checked off forty-three of them. She has run two marathons, she has gone skydiving over the Nevada desert, and she has seen the northern lights in Alaska. \"That was a once-in-a-lifetime experience,\" she says. \"I've never felt so small and so happy at the same time.\" Some items have been harder. She hasn't learned to surf yet, and she has never visited Antarctica. \"I've just booked a surf camp in San Diego for next month, so number forty-four is coming!\" Rebecca's list has inspired thousands of followers online. \"People ask me if I've ever been scared. Of course I have! But I've learned that regret is scarier than fear.\" Have you ever written your own list? Rebecca says it's never too late to start.","au":"13179cca4d","q":[{"s":"Rebecca wrote her list when she turned forty.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She has completed all fifty experiences.","a":"no"},{"s":"She has seen the northern lights in Alaska.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She has already learned to surf.","a":"no"},{"s":"She has just booked a surf camp in San Diego.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Have you ever been to the United States?","a":"Yes, I have. I've been to Miami twice.","es":"¿Alguna vez has ido a Estados Unidos?","qau":"51f04a6d2c","aau":"aaea440fc3"},{"q":"Have you finished your homework yet?","a":"Not yet. I've just started it.","es":"¿Ya terminaste tu tarea?","qau":"d432eb579b","aau":"820e88bae2"},{"q":"What's something you've never done?","a":"I've never gone skydiving.","es":"¿Qué es algo que nunca has hecho?","qau":"83e54a7259","aau":"595ca9e1bd"},{"q":"Have you already had lunch today?","a":"Yes, I've already had lunch.","es":"¿Ya almorzaste hoy?","qau":"03a905e8c2","aau":"8becc34131"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu propia 'bucket list': 3 cosas que ya has hecho (already / ever) y 3 que todavía no has hecho (never / yet).","kw":["already","yet"],"n":6,"model":"I've already been to New York. I've run a 10K race. I've tried Japanese food. I've never seen the northern lights. I haven't learned to dance salsa yet. I've never been to Alaska."}},{"id":"t4p2","topic":4,"part":2,"title":"For, since & present perfect vs. past simple","es":"For, since y presente perfecto vs. pasado simple","acts":["learn","resumeTimeline","dialogue","fill","matchLines","speak"],"tip":"<p>⏳ <b>for</b> + período (cuánto tiempo): <i>for ten years, for a long time</i> · <b>since</b> + punto de inicio: <i>since 2019, since June, since I was a kid</i>.</p>\n<p>🇪🇸➡️🇺🇸 <i>Vivo aquí <u>desde hace</u> diez años / <u>Llevo</u> diez años aquí</i> → <b>I've lived here for ten years</b> (no <s>I live here for ten years</s>).</p>\n<p>🔚 <b>Pasado simple</b> = tiempo <b>terminado</b> y específico: <i>yesterday, in 2018, last year, two days ago</i>.</p>\n<p>🔄 <b>Presente perfecto</b> = tiempo <b>no terminado</b> o sin especificar: <i>today, this week, lately, so far</i>.</p>\n<p>💡 Conversación típica: pregunta en presente perfecto → detalles en pasado: <i>Have you ever been to Denver? — Yes, I <b>went</b> there last spring.</i></p>","tips":["<b>since</b> suena <i>sins</i>; no lo confundas con <b>science</b> (<i>sáiens</i>).","<b>It's been ages</b>: la t de <i>It's</i> casi desaparece: <i>sbin-éiyis</i>.","<b>lately</b> suena <i>léitli</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"I've lived here for ten years.","es":"Vivo aquí desde hace diez años.","img":"u:photo-1624204386084-dd8c05e32226","v":"f","au":"b9e73dcd27"},{"en":"She's worked there since 2019.","es":"Trabaja allí desde 2019.","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"f","au":"a91dfed8c4"},{"en":"How long have you known him?","es":"¿Hace cuánto lo conoces?","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"m","au":"0b5616dddc"},{"en":"I moved to Dallas in 2018.","es":"Me mudé a Dallas en 2018.","img":"u:photo-1766040923580-16ad32fae8b4","v":"m","au":"adcec66197"},{"en":"We've been married since June.","es":"Estamos casados desde junio.","img":"u:photo-1536567307162-551e460b7fc2","v":"f","au":"4147c86dad"},{"en":"It's been ages!","es":"¡Hace siglos!","img":"u:photo-1530047139082-5435ca3c4614","v":"m","au":"916880f583"},{"en":"lately","es":"últimamente","img":"u:photo-1610354878912-08f1ab8ae913","v":"f","au":"f309176813"},{"en":"recently","es":"recientemente","img":"u:photo-1722487631997-cf1e0f92c2c4","v":"m","au":"1e984be1c6"},{"en":"this year","es":"este año (no ha terminado)","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"4db82e7681"},{"en":"last year","es":"el año pasado (ya terminó)","img":"u:photo-1632772998001-cc9bf6f7c852","v":"m","au":"76fb590b6e"},{"en":"to get promoted","es":"ser ascendido","img":"u:photo-1576267423048-15c0040fec78","v":"f","au":"7ee3b23a85"},{"en":"work experience","es":"experiencia laboral","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"m","au":"f9fc2384a8"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I've worked in tech for almost eight years.","es":"Llevo casi ocho años trabajando en tecnología.","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","v":"f","au":"e5814bd880"},{"en":"We've known each other since college.","es":"Nos conocemos desde la universidad.","img":"u:photo-1583606784123-7c244f00d29c","v":"m","au":"9630369b2b"},{"en":"I started this job two years ago.","es":"Empecé este trabajo hace dos años.","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"3c2d100027"},{"en":"Have you seen any good shows lately?","es":"¿Has visto alguna buena serie últimamente?","img":"u:photo-1758525862392-1b25015f3fe1","v":"m","au":"5d964bef9d"},{"en":"I've been to Denver twice. I went there last spring.","es":"He ido a Denver dos veces. Fui la primavera pasada.","img":"u:photo-1612441804231-77a36b284856","v":"f","au":"9c08323a0d"},{"en":"How long have you had your car?","es":"¿Hace cuánto tienes tu carro?","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"m","au":"b95eb8a3b1"}],"fill":[{"s":"I've had this phone ___ two years.","a":"for","o":["since","ago"],"h":"período de tiempo","full":"I've had this phone for two years.","au":"e98d541d3b"},{"s":"She's lived in Miami ___ 2015.","a":"since","o":["for","in"],"h":"punto de inicio","full":"She's lived in Miami since 2015.","au":"85611ece19"},{"s":"We ___ to Orlando last summer.","a":"went","o":["have gone","have been"],"h":"tiempo terminado → pasado simple","full":"We went to Orlando last summer.","au":"58070344b2"},{"s":"I ___ three cups of coffee today.","a":"have had","o":["had","has had"],"h":"hoy no ha terminado","full":"I have had three cups of coffee today.","au":"079a2ff774"},{"s":"How long ___ you known your best friend?","a":"have","o":["do","did"],"h":"how long + presente perfecto","full":"How long have you known your best friend?","au":"5ead79f6b7"},{"s":"He ___ his job in 2021.","a":"quit","o":["has quit","has quitted"],"h":"año específico → pasado","full":"He quit his job in 2021.","au":"77622e6949"},{"s":"They ___ married for twenty years.","a":"have been","o":["are","were"],"h":"llevan 20 años casados","full":"They have been married for twenty years.","au":"02daa16721"}],"dialogue":{"title":"A job interview in Austin","es":"Una entrevista de trabajo en Austin","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","lines":[{"who":"Interviewer","v":"f","t":"Thanks for coming in, Andrés. How long have you worked in customer success?","au":"47d326e69f"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"For about six years. I started at a small startup in Miami in 2019.","au":"d5d111d5ef"},{"who":"Interviewer","v":"f","t":"And where are you working now?","au":"3248f0fc21"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"I've been at CloudNest since 2022. I got promoted to team lead last year.","au":"48dcf54fcb"},{"who":"Interviewer","v":"f","t":"Impressive. Have you ever managed a remote team?","au":"0385b04f19"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"Yes, I have. I've managed people in four time zones so far.","au":"790eeced13"},{"who":"Interviewer","v":"f","t":"Great. Have you visited our office before?","au":"ae89ee4af8"},{"who":"Andrés","v":"m","t":"No, I haven't. I only moved to Austin last month, but I love it already.","au":"1b2d0b4b15"}],"q":[{"q":"When did Andrés start in Miami?","a":"In 2019.","o":["In 2022.","Last year."]},{"q":"How long has he been at CloudNest?","a":"Since 2022.","o":["For six years.","Since last month."]},{"q":"When did he move to Austin?","a":"Last month.","o":["In 2019.","Last year."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To use for and since, and choose between present perfect and past simple.","es":"Usar for y since, y elegir entre presente perfecto y pasado simple."},"warm":[{"q":"How long have you lived in your current home?","au":"e9533861cf","es":"¿Hace cuánto vives en tu casa actual?","ex":"I've lived here for six years."},{"q":"When did you start studying English?","au":"63f3af5933","es":"¿Cuándo empezaste a estudiar inglés?","ex":"I started in 2020, during the pandemic."}],"reading":{"title":"From line cook to restaurant owner","img":"u:photo-1622021142947-da7dedc7c39a","text":"Javier Morales has owned La Brasa, a popular Latin restaurant in Denver, since 2020. But his story started much earlier. He moved to the United States from Guatemala in 2008 and got his first job as a dishwasher in a hotel kitchen. \"I didn't speak much English, and I worked twelve hours a day,\" he remembers. In 2012 he became a line cook, and three years later he got promoted to sous-chef. Javier has worked in kitchens for more than fifteen years, and he has cooked for celebrities, politicians and food critics. \"I've made many mistakes,\" he admits, \"but I've learned from every one of them.\" Last year La Brasa won a local award for best new menu, and this year Javier has already hired six new employees. He has also started a free cooking program for teenagers. \"I've been lucky,\" he says, \"but luck is what happens when you work hard for a long time.\"","au":"2e338ccb6e","q":[{"s":"Javier has owned La Brasa since 2020.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He moved to the United States in 2012.","a":"no"},{"s":"His first job was as a dishwasher.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He has worked in kitchens for less than ten years.","a":"no"},{"s":"He has hired six employees this year.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How long have you studied English?","a":"I've studied English for three years.","es":"¿Hace cuánto estudias inglés?","qau":"63c3dc5d0d","aau":"778f758f8b"},{"q":"When did you start your current job?","a":"I started it in 2021.","es":"¿Cuándo empezaste tu trabajo actual?","qau":"5ccd408b2c","aau":"2f37841fd6"},{"q":"Have you been busy lately?","a":"Yes, I've been very busy at work lately.","es":"¿Has estado ocupado(a) últimamente?","qau":"0a59ba9d16","aau":"effa567c96"},{"q":"How long have you known your best friend?","a":"I've known her since we were in high school.","es":"¿Hace cuánto conoces a tu mejor amigo(a)?","qau":"5ead79f6b7","aau":"d155f98f40"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu mini biografía profesional: 3 oraciones en pasado simple (con año) y 3 en presente perfecto con for / since.","kw":["for","since"],"n":6,"model":"I finished college in 2015. I got my first job in 2016. I've worked in sales since 2018. I've lived in my apartment for five years. I've studied English for two years. I've had my car since 2019."}}]},{"n":5,"title":"The Past Perfect","es":"El pasado perfecto","cover":"u:photo-1450897918656-527057db59d3","parts":[{"id":"t5p1","topic":5,"part":1,"title":"Before that: sequencing past events","es":"Antes de eso: secuencia de eventos","acts":["learn","tooLate","fill","unscramble","raceGame","speak"],"tip":"<p>El <b>pasado perfecto</b> = <b>had + participio</b>. Sirve para hablar de una acción <b>anterior</b> a otra acción del pasado.</p>\n<p>⏪ <i>When I got to the airport, my flight <b>had left</b>.</i> (primero salió el vuelo, después llegué yo)<br>⏩ <i>When I got to the airport, my flight <b>left</b>.</i> (llegué y justo después salió)</p>\n<p>🏁 <b>By the time</b> + pasado simple → pasado perfecto: <i>By the time the police arrived, the thief <b>had escaped</b>.</i></p>\n<p>🔑 Con <b>already, just, never</b>: <i>She <b>had just</b> left. I <b>had never</b> flown before.</i></p>\n<p>💡 Con <b>before / after</b> el orden ya es claro, así que el pasado simple también es correcto: <i>After I finished, I left.</i></p>","tips":["<b>had</b> casi siempre se contrae: <i>I'd, she'd, we'd</i> (<i>aid, shid, uid</i>).","Ojo: <b>I'd</b> también puede ser <b>I would</b>; el participio te dice cuál es.","<b>By the time</b> se pronuncia <i>baide-táim</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"had already left","es":"ya se había ido","img":"u:photo-1713865469268-310e28436199","v":"f","au":"a28887286d"},{"en":"had never seen","es":"nunca había visto","img":"u:photo-1485738422979-f5c462d49f74","v":"m","au":"ed9d063979"},{"en":"By the time I arrived, ...","es":"Para cuando llegué, ...","img":"u:photo-1623975522495-82ea8c48de56","v":"m","au":"c816ac91da"},{"en":"after I had finished","es":"después de haber terminado","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"bd117c8f55"},{"en":"before the movie started","es":"antes de que empezara la película","img":"u:photo-1702308954905-341065817003","v":"f","au":"1a47c24104"},{"en":"the flight had been canceled","es":"el vuelo había sido cancelado","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"28c511e283"},{"en":"I realized I had forgotten","es":"me di cuenta de que había olvidado","img":"u:photo-1770199105692-9e52ff137cad","v":"m","au":"a3150a28cb"},{"en":"the battery had died","es":"la batería se había agotado","img":"u:photo-1557767382-97b28f5488e7","v":"f","au":"aadbd3de24"},{"en":"the store had closed","es":"la tienda había cerrado","img":"u:photo-1727767579106-c30a4c1c74c5","v":"m","au":"ac935f12c7"},{"en":"to miss the flight","es":"perder el vuelo","img":"u:photo-1450897918656-527057db59d3","v":"f","au":"1f91e44b77"},{"en":"just in time","es":"justo a tiempo","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"a0fbd959ec"}],"sentences":[{"en":"By the time we got to the stadium, the game had already started.","es":"Para cuando llegamos al estadio, el partido ya había empezado.","img":"u:photo-1651179853369-c20d476891f8","v":"f","au":"da3d6c7c4b"},{"en":"I had never flown first class before that trip.","es":"Nunca había volado en primera clase antes de ese viaje.","img":"u:photo-1608023136037-626dad6c6188","v":"m","au":"16ca08e6ff"},{"en":"When I checked my phone, the battery had died.","es":"Cuando revisé mi celular, la batería se había agotado.","img":"u:photo-1557767382-97b28f5488e7","v":"f","au":"f933ae8c9f"},{"en":"She had just left when you called.","es":"Ella se acababa de ir cuando llamaste.","img":"u:photo-1713865469268-310e28436199","v":"m","au":"0d2440be5d"},{"en":"We realized we had left the passports at the hotel.","es":"Nos dimos cuenta de que habíamos dejado los pasaportes en el hotel.","img":"u:photo-1641736494066-bd18237ede26","v":"f","au":"1670cf7208"},{"en":"After he had saved enough money, he opened his own café.","es":"Después de ahorrar lo suficiente, abrió su propio café.","img":"u:photo-1586011066531-f3a64f20d51d","v":"m","au":"17552f09bc"}],"fill":[{"s":"When I got to the gate, my flight ___.","a":"had already left","o":["already left","has left"],"h":"se fue antes de que yo llegara","full":"When I got to the gate, my flight had already left.","au":"003248d4ea"},{"s":"By the time the police arrived, the thief ___.","a":"had escaped","o":["has escaped","escapes"],"h":"antes de que llegara la policía","full":"By the time the police arrived, the thief had escaped.","au":"1f2ecdce28"},{"s":"She ___ never seen snow before she moved to Boston.","a":"had","o":["has","did"],"h":"experiencia anterior en el pasado","full":"She had never seen snow before she moved to Boston.","au":"fe4972de1f"},{"s":"I couldn't pay because I ___ my wallet at home.","a":"had left","o":["have left","leave"],"h":"causa anterior","full":"I couldn't pay because I had left my wallet at home.","au":"7b6b2f442f"},{"s":"When the guests arrived, we ___ already eaten.","a":"had","o":["have","were"],"h":"antes de que llegaran","full":"When the guests arrived, we had already eaten.","au":"9537a94395"},{"s":"He was nervous because he ___ spoken in public before.","a":"had never","o":["has never","never had"],"h":"nunca antes","full":"He was nervous because he had never spoken in public before.","au":"5b9456a616"}],"goal":{"en":"To order events in the past with the past perfect.","es":"Ordenar eventos en el pasado con el pasado perfecto."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever arrived somewhere and realized you had forgotten something important?","au":"eb4abbb4f8","es":"¿Alguna vez llegaste a un lugar y te diste cuenta de que habías olvidado algo importante?","ex":"Yes, I got to the airport and realized I had forgotten my passport."},{"q":"What had you done by the time you were twenty?","au":"f758e46357","es":"¿Qué habías hecho para cuando tenías veinte años?","ex":"By the time I was twenty, I had finished school and started working."}],"reading":{"title":"The longest morning","img":"u:photo-1450897918656-527057db59d3","text":"Last March, Tom had a job interview in Boston at nine o'clock. He had prepared for weeks, he had ironed his best shirt, and he had set two alarms. Nothing could go wrong, or so he thought. When he woke up, the power had gone out during the night and both alarms had died with his phone. By the time he got to the train station, his train had already left. He took a taxi, but halfway there he realized he had left his résumé on the kitchen table. Tom called the office to apologize. To his surprise, the receptionist laughed: the interviewer's flight had been delayed, so the interview had been moved to eleven. Tom arrived just in time, printed a new copy of his résumé at a copy shop, and walked in calmly. Two days later he got the job. \"I had never felt so stressed,\" he says, \"or so lucky.\"","au":"9ebaf6bd18","q":[{"s":"Tom's interview was in Boston.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He hadn't prepared for the interview.","a":"no"},{"s":"His train had left before he got to the station.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He had left his résumé in the taxi.","a":"no"},{"s":"The interview had been moved to eleven.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What had you done before you came to class today?","a":"I had finished work and had dinner.","es":"¿Qué habías hecho antes de venir a clase hoy?","qau":"0c528a3d88","aau":"79bd52e1d2"},{"q":"Had you ever studied English before this course?","a":"Yes, I had studied it in high school.","es":"¿Habías estudiado inglés antes de este curso?","qau":"56108d0b4a","aau":"6ae5d2696e"},{"q":"What happened when you got to the airport late?","a":"When I got there, the gate had already closed.","es":"¿Qué pasó cuando llegaste tarde al aeropuerto?","qau":"7c2a4df398","aau":"8a16efa577"},{"q":"By the time you were 18, had you traveled abroad?","a":"No, I hadn't. My first trip was at 25.","es":"Para cuando tenías 18 años, ¿habías viajado al exterior?","qau":"820674256a","aau":"8da5ef1911"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 5 oraciones sobre un día en que todo salió mal. Usa by the time, when y already con el pasado perfecto.","kw":["had","by the time"],"n":5,"model":"By the time I woke up, my bus had already left. When I got to the office, the meeting had started. I realized I had forgotten my laptop. My boss had already called me twice. Luckily, my coworker had saved me a seat."}},{"id":"t5p2","topic":5,"part":2,"title":"Telling a story","es":"Contar una historia","acts":["learn","noirCase","dialogue","fill","sayPop","speak"],"tip":"<p>Para <b>contar una historia</b> en inglés se combinan tres tiempos:</p>\n<p>🎬 <b>Pasado simple</b> = los eventos principales, en orden: <i>I <b>got</b> to the hotel and <b>checked</b> in.</i><br>🎞️ <b>Pasado continuo</b> = el fondo, lo que estaba pasando: <i>It <b>was raining</b> and everyone <b>was waiting</b>.</i><br>⏪ <b>Pasado perfecto</b> = un “flashback”, algo que pasó antes: <i>I realized I <b>had left</b> my wallet in the taxi.</i></p>\n<p>🔗 Conectores narrativos: <b>It all started when</b>, <b>all of a sudden</b>, <b>meanwhile</b>, <b>to make matters worse</b>, <b>it turned out that</b>, <b>eventually</b> (finalmente — ¡no es “eventualmente”!).</p>\n<p>⚠️ No abuses del pasado perfecto: úsalo solo cuando necesites “retroceder” en la historia.</p>","tips":["<b>eventually</b> se pronuncia <i>ivénchuali</i> y significa <b>finalmente</b>.","<b>meanwhile</b> suena <i>mín-uail</i>.","En <b>It turned out</b> une las palabras: <i>itérn-dáut</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"It all started when...","es":"Todo empezó cuando...","img":"u:photo-1528569937393-ee892b976859","v":"f","au":"fadb6f243b"},{"en":"Little did I know...","es":"Poco sabía yo...","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"m","au":"7b2708dc96"},{"en":"It turned out that...","es":"Resultó que...","img":"u:photo-1713256452479-5a20056c0340","v":"f","au":"8caf43811b"},{"en":"To make matters worse, ...","es":"Para empeorar las cosas, ...","img":"u:photo-1519692933481-e162a57d6721","v":"m","au":"38a568d9bf"},{"en":"eventually","es":"finalmente, con el tiempo","img":"u:photo-1552650272-b8a34e21bc4b","v":"f","au":"eeef3efa29"},{"en":"meanwhile","es":"mientras tanto","img":"u:photo-1774949884464-7be323ddeee2","v":"m","au":"68695566fe"},{"en":"All of a sudden, ...","es":"De repente, ...","img":"u:photo-1559087867-ce4c91325525","v":"f","au":"48d208b373"},{"en":"had been robbed","es":"había sido robado","img":"u:photo-1751152110851-ec8c5b94132f","v":"m","au":"b5062747b3"},{"en":"to get stranded","es":"quedarse varado","img":"u:photo-1514757811270-01b9230c4192","v":"f","au":"2a87a51923"},{"en":"I couldn't believe my eyes.","es":"No podía creer lo que veía.","img":"u:photo-1702677852474-9801fc432f0f","v":"m","au":"c6d12de3b0"},{"en":"in the nick of time","es":"justo a tiempo","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"f","au":"c3e16bf5a3"},{"en":"a twist of fate","es":"un giro del destino","img":"u:photo-1429743305873-d4065c15f93e","v":"m","au":"4b4642d5ef"}],"sentences":[{"en":"It turned out that someone had taken my suitcase by mistake.","es":"Resultó que alguien se había llevado mi maleta por error.","img":"u:photo-1648737967037-96967e9151b5","v":"f","au":"a192d56592"},{"en":"When I got back to my car, someone had broken the window.","es":"Cuando volví a mi carro, alguien había roto la ventana.","img":"u:photo-1751152110851-ec8c5b94132f","v":"m","au":"af5e6c7340"},{"en":"To make matters worse, I had left my wallet at the hotel.","es":"Para empeorar las cosas, había dejado mi billetera en el hotel.","img":"u:photo-1620109176813-e91290f6c795","v":"f","au":"d23a765cc0"},{"en":"All of a sudden, the lights went out.","es":"De repente, se fue la luz.","img":"u:photo-1601922046210-41e129a3e64a","v":"m","au":"ef66d5dc08"},{"en":"Eventually, we found a mechanic who had worked in Texas for years.","es":"Finalmente encontramos un mecánico que había trabajado en Texas por años.","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"f","au":"d210b6c404"},{"en":"Little did I know that she had planned a surprise party.","es":"Poco sabía yo que ella había planeado una fiesta sorpresa.","img":"u:photo-1625649611137-df49dc542f6a","v":"m","au":"1513f15330"}],"fill":[{"s":"I ___ in that hotel before, so I knew the way.","a":"had stayed","o":["have stayed","stay"],"h":"experiencia anterior","full":"I had stayed in that hotel before, so I knew the way.","au":"d48883ca4d"},{"s":"All of a sudden, the fire alarm ___ off.","a":"went","o":["had gone","has gone"],"h":"evento principal → pasado simple","full":"All of a sudden, the fire alarm went off.","au":"eb2c77077b"},{"s":"It turned out that my cousin ___ the same ticket.","a":"had bought","o":["has bought","buys"],"h":"evento anterior","full":"It turned out that my cousin had bought the same ticket.","au":"9174cecdb3"},{"s":"While we ___ dinner, the power went out.","a":"were having","o":["had had","have"],"h":"acción de fondo → pasado continuo","full":"While we were having dinner, the power went out.","au":"4d80c0d1cf"},{"s":"___, after three hours, the plane took off.","a":"Eventually","o":["Meanwhile","Already"],"h":"finalmente","full":"Eventually, after three hours, the plane took off.","au":"464bb0faa5"},{"s":"She recognized him at once because they ___ before.","a":"had met","o":["have met","meet"],"h":"se habían conocido antes","full":"She recognized him at once because they had met before.","au":"53db4e4661"}],"dialogue":{"title":"A travel nightmare","es":"Una pesadilla de viaje","img":"u:photo-1450897918656-527057db59d3","lines":[{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"So, how was your trip to Phoenix?","au":"cab58c9565"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Don't ask! It all started when my alarm didn't go off. By the time I woke up, my Uber had already left.","au":"2bc45b5678"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"Oh no! Did you miss your flight?","au":"e62489ddd9"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Almost. I got to the gate in the nick of time, but then it turned out the flight had been delayed for three hours.","au":"fd24503e78"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"At least you made it.","au":"54382ac486"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Wait, there's more. When I landed, I realized I had left my laptop on the plane.","au":"605f165ab7"},{"who":"Jenna","v":"f","t":"You're kidding! Did you get it back?","au":"44e6bffed6"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Eventually, yes. A flight attendant had found it and taken it to the airline office.","au":"e0a52cc218"}],"q":[{"q":"Why did Luis wake up late?","a":"His alarm didn't go off.","o":["His flight was delayed.","He was sick."]},{"q":"What had happened to his flight?","a":"It had been delayed.","o":["It had left.","It had been canceled."]},{"q":"Who had found the laptop?","a":"A flight attendant.","o":["Jenna.","The Uber driver."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To tell a story using narrative tenses and connectors.","es":"Contar una historia usando los tiempos narrativos y conectores."},"warm":[{"q":"What's the funniest or strangest thing that has happened to you on a trip?","au":"a1d0db4cf4","es":"¿Qué es lo más gracioso o extraño que te ha pasado en un viaje?","ex":"Once, the airline sent my suitcase to another country!"},{"q":"Do you prefer telling stories or listening to them?","au":"12c5e2a832","es":"¿Prefieres contar historias o escucharlas?","ex":"I prefer listening to them, but I love funny stories."}],"reading":{"title":"The wrong suitcase","img":"u:photo-1648737967037-96967e9151b5","text":"It all started at the airport in Atlanta. I was exhausted because I had worked all night, so I grabbed my black suitcase from the carousel and took a taxi to the hotel. Meanwhile, it was raining heavily and the traffic was terrible. When I finally opened the suitcase in my room, I couldn't believe my eyes. Instead of my clothes, there were three cowboy hats, a pair of red boots and a book in German. It turned out that I had taken someone else's suitcase. To make matters worse, my presentation for the next morning was in mine. I called the airline, and they told me a man named Klaus had reported a missing suitcase an hour earlier. Little did I know that he was staying at my hotel! Eventually, we met in the lobby and exchanged bags, laughing. Klaus had already opened mine, too. \"Nice shoes,\" he said. \"But not my size.\"","au":"770bdb65c9","q":[{"s":"The writer had worked all night before the flight.","a":"yes"},{"s":"It was sunny when she took the taxi.","a":"no"},{"s":"She found cowboy hats in the suitcase.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Klaus had reported his missing suitcase.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Klaus was staying at a different hotel.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What were you doing when the story started?","a":"I was waiting for my flight in Miami.","es":"¿Qué estabas haciendo cuando empezó la historia?","qau":"b9e1e4de66","aau":"1ba089ff4b"},{"q":"What had happened before you arrived?","a":"Someone had taken my seat on the plane.","es":"¿Qué había pasado antes de que llegaras?","qau":"d26461b646","aau":"f233fc8fa2"},{"q":"How did the story end?","a":"Eventually, everything worked out and we laughed about it.","es":"¿Cómo terminó la historia?","qau":"a9f3bbf7f8","aau":"388d9985af"},{"q":"What's a good way to start a story?","a":"It all started when I was on vacation in San Diego.","es":"¿Cuál es una buena manera de empezar una historia?","qau":"05afda747a","aau":"7d04fde7f1"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe una historia corta (6+ oraciones) sobre un viaje o un día inolvidable. Usa pasado simple, continuo y perfecto, y al menos 3 conectores.","kw":["had","eventually"],"n":6,"model":"It all started when I was driving to Orlando. It was raining and I was listening to music. All of a sudden, my car stopped. I realized I had forgotten to fill the tank. To make matters worse, my phone had died. Eventually, a kind truck driver helped me."}}]},{"n":6,"title":"Prepositions of Time","es":"Preposiciones de tiempo","cover":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","parts":[{"id":"t6p1","topic":6,"part":1,"title":"In, on, at · by vs. until","es":"In, on, at · by vs. until","acts":["learn","timeZoom","sort","fill","speed","speak"],"tip":"<p>Imagina una <b>pirámide</b> 🔺 de lo más preciso a lo más general:</p>\n<p>⏰ <b>AT</b> = punto exacto: <i>at 9 a.m., at noon, at night, at the moment, at Thanksgiving</i> (la temporada).<br>📅 <b>ON</b> = días y fechas: <i>on Monday, on July 4th, on my birthday, on Monday morning, on the weekend</i> (EE. UU.).<br>🌍 <b>IN</b> = períodos largos: <i>in May, in 2030, in the summer, in the 1990s, in the morning</i>.</p>\n<p>🚫 Sin preposición con <b>this, next, last, every</b>: <i>I'll see you <b>next Monday</b></i> (no <s>on next Monday</s>).</p>\n<p>⏳ <b>in + período</b> = dentro de: <i>I'll call you <b>in</b> ten minutes.</i></p>\n<p>🏁 <b>by</b> = fecha límite, a más tardar (<i>Send it <b>by</b> Friday</i>) · <b>until</b> = acción continua hasta ese momento (<i>I'll be here <b>until</b> six</i>).</p>","tips":["<b>until</b> suena <i>antíl</i>, con acento al final.","<b>sharp</b> después de la hora = en punto exacto: <i>at nine sharp</i>.","En <b>on the weekend</b> une todo: <i>ondeuíkend</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"at 9 a.m. sharp","es":"a las 9 en punto","img":"u:photo-1563861826100-9cb868fdbe1c","v":"f","au":"786de0e688"},{"en":"on Monday morning","es":"el lunes por la mañana","img":"u:photo-1632772998001-cc9bf6f7c852","v":"m","au":"9670afad84"},{"en":"in the 1990s","es":"en los años noventa","img":"u:photo-1528569937393-ee892b976859","v":"f","au":"4bc8cbde51"},{"en":"on the weekend","es":"el fin de semana (EE. UU.)","img":"u:photo-1755003842792-9d2b7ad08862","v":"m","au":"494194bc92"},{"en":"on Christmas Eve","es":"en Nochebuena","img":"u:photo-1543258103-a62bdc069871","v":"f","au":"3da34d07a3"},{"en":"at Thanksgiving","es":"en (la época de) Acción de Gracias","img":"u:photo-1669151846702-09426d89bba0","v":"m","au":"807e6fc526"},{"en":"in two weeks","es":"dentro de dos semanas","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"f","au":"16729549cd"},{"en":"by Friday","es":"para el viernes (a más tardar)","img":"u:photo-1775363949971-0e4919c66856","v":"m","au":"a62845ef88"},{"en":"until 6 p.m.","es":"hasta las 6 p.m.","img":"u:photo-1713947505221-8a11da8aa744","v":"f","au":"6a7c141e1f"},{"en":"at the moment","es":"en este momento","img":"u:photo-1758873268528-af4613d099b6","v":"m","au":"022954590e"},{"en":"on my birthday","es":"en mi cumpleaños","img":"u:photo-1464349153735-7db50ed83c84","v":"f","au":"dc8653bd1a"},{"en":"in the early morning","es":"temprano en la mañana","img":"u:photo-1552650272-b8a34e21bc4b","v":"m","au":"b08af8d107"}],"sentences":[{"en":"The webinar starts at 10 a.m. Pacific Time.","es":"El webinar empieza a las 10 a.m. hora del Pacífico.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"5a9326cfc3"},{"en":"We usually visit my grandparents on Thanksgiving Day.","es":"Normalmente visitamos a mis abuelos el Día de Acción de Gracias.","img":"u:photo-1669151846702-09426d89bba0","v":"m","au":"0e97995ea4"},{"en":"I need the signed contract by Friday at noon.","es":"Necesito el contrato firmado para el viernes al mediodía.","img":"u:photo-1585336261022-680e295ce3fe","v":"f","au":"89a346ceee"},{"en":"The store is open until midnight on weekends.","es":"La tienda abre hasta la medianoche los fines de semana.","img":"u:photo-1698389912782-93fe4c0d3b90","v":"m","au":"192020781e"},{"en":"My parents got married in the summer of 1995.","es":"Mis padres se casaron en el verano de 1995.","img":"u:photo-1536567307162-551e460b7fc2","v":"f","au":"ab1c14ecf1"},{"en":"I'll call you back in ten minutes.","es":"Te devuelvo la llamada en diez minutos.","img":"u:photo-1758873268528-af4613d099b6","v":"m","au":"19f15b2e6b"}],"fill":[{"s":"The conference is ___ May 14th.","a":"on","o":["in","at"],"h":"fecha exacta","full":"The conference is on May 14th.","au":"81ea1bed5e"},{"s":"I was born ___ 1992.","a":"in","o":["on","at"],"h":"año","full":"I was born in 1992.","au":"7f98a0c532"},{"s":"Please submit the report ___ Thursday.","a":"by","o":["until","in"],"h":"fecha límite","full":"Please submit the report by Thursday.","au":"76723b9d18"},{"s":"We waited ___ 11 p.m., but she never came.","a":"until","o":["by","in"],"h":"acción continua hasta","full":"We waited until 11 p.m., but she never came.","au":"50962ad3ff"},{"s":"The museum is closed ___ Christmas Day.","a":"on","o":["in","at"],"h":"día específico","full":"The museum is closed on Christmas Day.","au":"d0f25994cf"},{"s":"I'll see you ___ Monday.","a":"next","o":["on next","at next"],"h":"sin preposición con next","full":"I'll see you next Monday.","au":"7034f14d86"},{"s":"My flight lands ___ night.","a":"at","o":["in","on"],"h":"at night","full":"My flight lands at night.","au":"03277c680e"}],"sort":{"cats":["AT","ON","IN"],"items":[{"w":"noon","c":"AT","au":"09efe579a4"},{"w":"5:30 p.m.","c":"AT","au":"cf60ac13b4"},{"w":"night","c":"AT","au":"a48a679458"},{"w":"Tuesday","c":"ON","au":"68596ee0a6"},{"w":"July 4th","c":"ON","au":"1f32272693"},{"w":"my birthday","c":"ON","au":"efd219e365"},{"w":"Christmas Day","c":"ON","au":"a052b5c053"},{"w":"2030","c":"IN","au":"7a2fb5eeda"},{"w":"the summer","c":"IN","au":"9ca1b0f329"},{"w":"the morning","c":"IN","au":"964d7d9bd4"},{"w":"the 1980s","c":"IN","au":"d5cb6048b9"}]},"goal":{"en":"To use in, on, at, by and until with times and dates.","es":"Usar in, on, at, by y until con horas y fechas."},"warm":[{"q":"What do you usually do on the weekend?","au":"c25b83a90f","es":"¿Qué haces normalmente el fin de semana?","ex":"On the weekend I usually visit my family and rest."},{"q":"What's something you have to finish by the end of this month?","au":"136864d764","es":"¿Qué tienes que terminar para final de este mes?","ex":"I have to finish a big report by the end of the month."}],"reading":{"title":"A very American calendar","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","text":"When Lucía moved to Atlanta for her new job, she discovered that the American calendar has its own rhythm. In January everyone starts the year with resolutions, and on the third Monday of the month there's a holiday for Martin Luther King Jr. In February people celebrate Valentine's Day on the 14th, and in the spring families travel during Spring Break. The big summer celebration is on July 4th, with fireworks at night. \"At Thanksgiving, my American coworkers go home to their families,\" Lucía says. \"It's always on the fourth Thursday in November, and the stores open early the next morning for Black Friday.\" Work deadlines also surprised her. Her boss once wrote: \"Please send the budget by Friday.\" Lucía waited until Friday afternoon. \"By means no later than,\" he explained kindly. \"Next time, send it earlier.\" Now Lucía plans everything ahead, and she never works late on Christmas Eve.","au":"81910a9e81","q":[{"s":"Lucía moved to Atlanta for work.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The Martin Luther King Jr. holiday is in February.","a":"no"},{"s":"Thanksgiving is always on the fourth Thursday in November.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her boss wanted the budget no later than Friday.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She always works late on Christmas Eve.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"When is your birthday?","a":"It's on March 12th.","es":"¿Cuándo es tu cumpleaños?","qau":"60d49dcce9","aau":"5123f3af11"},{"q":"What time do you start work?","a":"I start at eight in the morning.","es":"¿A qué hora empiezas a trabajar?","qau":"aefedfb211","aau":"b36ae4fc87"},{"q":"Until what time do you usually stay at work?","a":"I usually stay until six p.m.","es":"¿Hasta qué hora te quedas normalmente en el trabajo?","qau":"92eadfff3e","aau":"2610feec9c"},{"q":"By when do you need to finish your next project?","a":"I need to finish it by the end of the month.","es":"¿Para cuándo necesitas terminar tu próximo proyecto?","qau":"75229e9f48","aau":"ad9e1f4cd0"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu agenda de la próxima semana con 6 oraciones usando at, on, in, by y until (ej. I have a meeting on Monday at 9).","kw":["by","until"],"n":6,"model":"On Monday at nine I have a team meeting. I'll work until six. I need to send the report by Wednesday. On Thursday evening I'm going to the gym. My cousin's birthday is on Saturday. In two weeks I'm traveling to Miami."}},{"id":"t6p2","topic":6,"part":2,"title":"During, for, while, within · in time vs. on time","es":"During, for, while, within · in time vs. on time","acts":["learn","podcastBleep","dialogue","fill","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>El español usa <b>“durante”</b> para todo; el inglés distingue:</p>\n<p>📍 <b>during</b> + sustantivo = <b>cuándo</b>: <i>during the meeting, during the flight</i>.<br>⏱️ <b>for</b> + período = <b>cuánto tiempo</b>: <i>for three hours, for a week</i>.<br>🔗 <b>while</b> + sujeto + verbo: <i>while I was driving</i>.</p>\n<p>📦 <b>within</b> = dentro de un plazo máximo: <i>within 24 hours</i> · <b>from ... to / until</b> = de ... a: <i>from 9 to 5</i>.</p>\n<p>🎯 <b>on time</b> = puntual (a la hora programada) · <b>in time</b> = con tiempo suficiente, antes de que sea tarde: <i>We got there just <b>in time</b> for dinner.</i></p>\n<p>🔚 <b>at the end of</b> = al final de algo (momento) · <b>in the end</b> = finalmente, después de todo.</p>","tips":["<b>during</b> suena <i>dúring</i>, con la r suave americana.","<b>within</b> suena <i>uidín</i>, con la th suave.","<b>throughout</b> suena <i>zruáut</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"during the meeting","es":"durante la reunión","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"5bbb4842d3"},{"en":"for three hours","es":"durante tres horas","img":"u:photo-1563861826100-9cb868fdbe1c","v":"m","au":"87c071c827"},{"en":"while I was driving","es":"mientras manejaba","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"f","au":"b12111ca53"},{"en":"within 24 hours","es":"en un plazo de 24 horas","img":"u:photo-1758523670564-d1d6a734dc0b","v":"m","au":"0139ced35b"},{"en":"from 9 to 5","es":"de 9 a 5","img":"u:photo-1461088945293-0c17689e48ac","v":"f","au":"2174a4fa07"},{"en":"on time","es":"puntual, a la hora exacta","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"2f6a0dd95a"},{"en":"in time","es":"a tiempo, con margen","img":"u:photo-1546589807-582d855db5ea","v":"f","au":"e2c1698779"},{"en":"at the end of the month","es":"a final de mes","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"m","au":"c1389cd902"},{"en":"in the end","es":"al final, finalmente","img":"u:photo-1518135714426-c18f5ffb6f4d","v":"f","au":"d72a1e7252"},{"en":"throughout the year","es":"durante todo el año","img":"u:photo-1772602842460-647399980585","v":"m","au":"229ab8105b"},{"en":"ahead of schedule","es":"antes de lo previsto","img":"u:photo-1621905252507-b35492cc74b4","v":"f","au":"9f6efb46cc"},{"en":"behind schedule","es":"atrasado","img":"u:photo-1623975522495-82ea8c48de56","v":"m","au":"768dc65d78"}],"sentences":[{"en":"My phone rang during the job interview. So embarrassing!","es":"Mi celular sonó durante la entrevista. ¡Qué vergüenza!","img":"u:photo-1672380135241-c024f7fbfa13","v":"f","au":"9db3c52ee0"},{"en":"We were stuck in traffic for two hours.","es":"Estuvimos atascados en el tráfico por dos horas.","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"55ef3bdfa9"},{"en":"I listened to a podcast while I was jogging.","es":"Escuché un pódcast mientras trotaba.","img":"u:photo-1774793153240-e5de76dc87f2","v":"f","au":"251a9602a8"},{"en":"Refunds are processed within five business days.","es":"Los reembolsos se procesan en un plazo de cinco días hábiles.","img":"u:photo-1556742031-c6961e8560b0","v":"m","au":"719800a938"},{"en":"The train left on time, and we got there just in time for dinner.","es":"El tren salió puntual y llegamos justo a tiempo para la cena.","img":"u:photo-1693572322416-9ea4b36482ce","v":"f","au":"464467affa"},{"en":"We argued for hours, but in the end we agreed.","es":"Discutimos por horas, pero al final nos pusimos de acuerdo.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"m","au":"33b95c50b0"}],"fill":[{"s":"I fell asleep ___ the movie.","a":"during","o":["for","while"],"h":"durante + sustantivo","full":"I fell asleep during the movie.","au":"9b99b33885"},{"s":"She lived in Chicago ___ five years.","a":"for","o":["during","while"],"h":"duración","full":"She lived in Chicago for five years.","au":"8bda140d58"},{"s":"Someone called ___ you were in the shower.","a":"while","o":["during","for"],"h":"while + oración","full":"Someone called while you were in the shower.","au":"37edfaff01"},{"s":"You must return the item ___ 30 days.","a":"within","o":["while","during"],"h":"plazo máximo","full":"You must return the item within 30 days.","au":"1aabac6707"},{"s":"The flight was delayed, but we arrived ___ for the wedding.","a":"in time","o":["on time","at time"],"h":"con tiempo suficiente","full":"The flight was delayed, but we arrived in time for the wedding.","au":"871e553149"},{"s":"The CEO will give a speech ___ the end of the event.","a":"at","o":["in","on"],"h":"at the end of","full":"The CEO will give a speech at the end of the event.","au":"8f7b1e1fd9"},{"s":"We had a lot of problems, but ___ the end everything worked out.","a":"in","o":["at","on"],"h":"finalmente","full":"We had a lot of problems, but in the end everything worked out.","au":"1b2921b08a"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Rescheduling a delivery","es":"Reprogramando una entrega","img":"u:photo-1758523670564-d1d6a734dc0b","lines":[{"who":"Agent","v":"f","t":"Thank you for calling QuickShip. How can I help you today?","au":"29d6b93e29"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Hi. My package was supposed to arrive on Tuesday, but nobody came during the day.","au":"18a0b11e48"},{"who":"Agent","v":"f","t":"I'm sorry about that. The driver tried to deliver it at 2 p.m., while you were out.","au":"7e28794d24"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"I see. Can you deliver it again by Friday? I'm flying to Boston on Saturday.","au":"8c02c5d6fb"},{"who":"Agent","v":"f","t":"Sure. We can deliver it on Thursday, from 9 to 1.","au":"8329ec418a"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Perfect. I'll be home until noon. Will it arrive on time?","au":"b67fea20d7"},{"who":"Agent","v":"f","t":"Yes. And if there's any problem, we'll refund you within 24 hours.","au":"3fbf377c84"},{"who":"Daniel","v":"m","t":"Great, thanks. In the end, that works even better for me.","au":"3d3704bf27"}],"q":[{"q":"When did the driver try to deliver the package?","a":"On Tuesday at 2 p.m.","o":["On Thursday morning.","On Friday."]},{"q":"When is Daniel flying to Boston?","a":"On Saturday.","o":["On Thursday.","On Friday."]},{"q":"When will they deliver the package?","a":"On Thursday, from 9 to 1.","o":["On Friday by noon.","On Tuesday afternoon."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To use during, for, while, within and expressions like in time and on time.","es":"Usar during, for, while, within y expresiones como in time y on time."},"warm":[{"q":"Are you usually on time, or are you always running a little late?","au":"5c0c7dfd49","es":"¿Normalmente eres puntual o siempre vas un poco tarde?","ex":"I'm usually on time. I hate being late."},{"q":"What do you like to do while you're commuting?","au":"573da528f0","es":"¿Qué te gusta hacer mientras te desplazas al trabajo?","ex":"I listen to podcasts while I'm driving."}],"reading":{"title":"The 30-day delivery challenge","img":"u:photo-1758523670564-d1d6a734dc0b","text":"Last year, an online furniture store in Ohio had a serious problem: customers were complaining that their orders never arrived on time. The new operations manager, Kevin Park, decided to try a 30-day challenge. During the first week, his team studied every delay. \"We found that trucks were waiting at the warehouse for hours while drivers looked for paperwork,\" he explains. For the next two weeks, they tested a digital system that sent all the documents to the drivers' phones. They also promised customers a delivery window: \"Your order will arrive within three business days, from 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.\" Not everything went well. At the end of the second week, the system crashed during a big sale. But in the end, the results were impressive. By the end of the month, 94 percent of orders had arrived on time, and many customers received their furniture in time for the holidays. Kevin's team celebrated with pizza, ahead of schedule.","au":"270e94d730","q":[{"s":"Customers were complaining about late deliveries.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Trucks waited at the warehouse because drivers were sleeping.","a":"no"},{"s":"The new system sent documents to the drivers' phones.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The system worked perfectly during the big sale.","a":"no"},{"s":"By the end of the month, 94 percent of orders arrived on time.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What do you do while you're waiting in line?","a":"I usually check my phone or listen to a podcast.","es":"¿Qué haces mientras esperas en una fila?","qau":"8c522d2a77","aau":"d4f24cff8d"},{"q":"How long did you study last night?","a":"I studied for about an hour.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo estudiaste anoche?","qau":"c1093f9502","aau":"0365f926ec"},{"q":"Do you usually arrive on time for appointments?","a":"Yes, I'm usually on time, sometimes even early.","es":"¿Normalmente llegas puntual a tus citas?","qau":"f40d6e44a0","aau":"0731fab62e"},{"q":"What happened during your last vacation?","a":"During my last vacation, it rained for three days.","es":"¿Qué pasó durante tus últimas vacaciones?","qau":"181056f070","aau":"2ab6224506"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe sobre un proyecto o viaje reciente con 5 oraciones usando during, for, while, within y in the end.","kw":["during","while"],"n":5,"model":"During my last trip to Chicago, it was very cold. We stayed there for five days. While we were walking downtown, it started to snow. The hotel promised to answer within an hour. In the end, it was an amazing trip."}}]},{"n":7,"title":"Prepositions of Place","es":"Preposiciones de lugar","cover":"u:photo-1440330033336-7dcff4630cef","parts":[{"id":"t7p1","topic":7,"part":1,"title":"In, on, at · across, along, through","es":"In, on, at · across, along, through","acts":["learn","droneFlight","fill","matchLines","oddOneOut","speak"],"tip":"<p>📍 <b>AT</b> = un punto, o un lugar por su función: <i>at the airport, at work, at the door, at 25 Main Street</i> (dirección exacta).<br>📦 <b>IN</b> = dentro de un espacio: <i>in the elevator, in Chicago, in the car, in a taxi</i>.<br>🟫 <b>ON</b> = superficie, pisos, calles (EE. UU.) y transporte público: <i>on the 5th floor, on Main Street, on the bus, on a plane</i>.</p>\n<p>🧭 Movimiento y posición:<br><b>across</b> = de un lado al otro · <b>along</b> = siguiendo una línea (río, calle, playa) · <b>through</b> = por dentro de (túnel, bosque) · <b>opposite</b> = enfrente · <b>beyond</b> = más allá de.</p>\n<p>🚗 Ojo: <b>in</b> a car / a taxi (no puedes caminar dentro) · <b>on</b> a bus / train / plane (sí puedes).</p>","tips":["<b>through</b> suena <i>zru</i>, con la lengua entre los dientes.","<b>across</b> suena <i>akrós</i>; no digas <i>acrosh</i>.","<b>beyond</b> suena <i>biyónd</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"at the airport","es":"en el aeropuerto","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"07793d6fda"},{"en":"in the elevator","es":"en el ascensor","img":"u:photo-1758448721149-aa0ce8e1b2c9","v":"m","au":"559cc6e571"},{"en":"on the 5th floor","es":"en el quinto piso","img":"u:photo-1624204386084-dd8c05e32226","v":"f","au":"ec6a21aba6"},{"en":"on the bus","es":"en el bus","img":"u:photo-1515616428283-3c97ebd69070","v":"m","au":"09e25e07c2"},{"en":"across the river","es":"al otro lado del río","img":"u:photo-1690300700246-e3db107c5c2f","v":"f","au":"e9df04387a"},{"en":"along the beach","es":"a lo largo de la playa","img":"u:photo-1604949210966-9440c324823f","v":"m","au":"f8c2e2b0ee"},{"en":"through the tunnel","es":"a través del túnel","img":"u:photo-1677076219280-23f893081509","v":"f","au":"69b3b484d5"},{"en":"opposite the bank","es":"enfrente del banco","img":"u:photo-1684679674829-fc7b436ec8e8","v":"m","au":"d1f8d7617b"},{"en":"beyond the mountains","es":"más allá de las montañas","img":"u:photo-1612441804231-77a36b284856","v":"f","au":"0067fa4db7"},{"en":"on the corner","es":"en la esquina","img":"u:photo-1760371909304-c8bffd3a7e62","v":"m","au":"f29a187c34"},{"en":"at the top of the stairs","es":"en lo alto de las escaleras","img":"u:photo-1645567454913-56c730ee1bb5","v":"f","au":"2a2a2ae24e"},{"en":"in the middle of nowhere","es":"en medio de la nada","img":"u:photo-1511173855943-aeec034188a9","v":"m","au":"36843546b9"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I'm at the airport, but my luggage is still in Chicago.","es":"Estoy en el aeropuerto, pero mi equipaje sigue en Chicago.","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"f","au":"edc0655946"},{"en":"Our office is on the 12th floor, opposite the elevators.","es":"Nuestra oficina está en el piso 12, frente a los ascensores.","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","v":"m","au":"c71b8e46c8"},{"en":"We walked across the Brooklyn Bridge at sunset.","es":"Cruzamos el puente de Brooklyn al atardecer.","img":"u:photo-1477882244523-716124bf91a1","v":"f","au":"bdf7625f9f"},{"en":"There's a bike path along the river.","es":"Hay una ciclovía a lo largo del río.","img":"u:photo-1787910382238-492619322dc2","v":"m","au":"e6733485e6"},{"en":"The road goes through a long tunnel under the bay.","es":"La carretera pasa por un túnel largo bajo la bahía.","img":"u:photo-1677076219280-23f893081509","v":"f","au":"32e4037512"},{"en":"Get in the car. We're running late!","es":"¡Súbete al carro! Vamos tarde.","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"m","au":"ac03fccbbe"}],"fill":[{"s":"I'll meet you ___ the airport, at Gate B12.","a":"at","o":["in","on"],"h":"lugar como punto de encuentro","full":"I'll meet you at the airport, at Gate B12.","au":"7b1fd38712"},{"s":"She lives ___ the third floor.","a":"on","o":["in","at"],"h":"pisos","full":"She lives on the third floor.","au":"c3aa8fece7"},{"s":"We swam ___ the lake to the other side.","a":"across","o":["along","through"],"h":"de un lado al otro","full":"We swam across the lake to the other side.","au":"d874c17cec"},{"s":"The train goes ___ a tunnel under the river.","a":"through","o":["across","along"],"h":"por dentro","full":"The train goes through a tunnel under the river.","au":"fa82994a2e"},{"s":"There are palm trees ___ the boulevard.","a":"along","o":["across","through"],"h":"a lo largo","full":"There are palm trees along the boulevard.","au":"f2a801748f"},{"s":"The pharmacy is ___ the bank, on the other side of the street.","a":"opposite","o":["beyond","along"],"h":"enfrente","full":"The pharmacy is opposite the bank, on the other side of the street.","au":"11025566dd"},{"s":"I left my keys ___ the car.","a":"in","o":["on","at"],"h":"carro → in","full":"I left my keys in the car.","au":"09fe89e097"}],"goal":{"en":"To describe where things are and how they move with prepositions of place.","es":"Describir dónde están las cosas y cómo se mueven con preposiciones de lugar."},"warm":[{"q":"What's on the walls of your bedroom?","au":"30764802bb","es":"¿Qué hay en las paredes de tu cuarto?","ex":"There's a big mirror and two photos on the walls."},{"q":"Would you like to live on a high floor or near the ground? Why?","au":"27a2ec79c3","es":"¿Te gustaría vivir en un piso alto o cerca del suelo? ¿Por qué?","ex":"On a high floor, because the view is better."}],"reading":{"title":"A morning run in San Francisco","img":"u:photo-1690300700246-e3db107c5c2f","text":"Every Saturday, Emily runs the same route through San Francisco, and she says it's the best way to see the city. She starts at her apartment on the fourth floor of an old building in North Beach. She jogs down the hill, across Columbus Avenue, and along the Embarcadero, where the water is on her right and the Ferry Building is in front of her. \"At that hour, there are only a few people on the street and seagulls everywhere,\" she says. Then she runs through a small park, past a café opposite the old pier, and under the Bay Bridge. On clear mornings she can see the hills beyond the bay. \"Sometimes I stop at the top of the stairs on Telegraph Hill just to breathe and enjoy the view.\" After an hour, she's back at her building, but she never takes the elevator. \"Four floors of stairs,\" she laughs. \"That's my cool-down.\"","au":"f803fcc434","q":[{"s":"Emily lives on the fourth floor.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She runs along the Embarcadero.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The water is on her left on the Embarcadero.","a":"no"},{"s":"She runs over the Bay Bridge.","a":"no"},{"s":"She always takes the elevator after her run.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Where do you live?","a":"I live in an apartment on the third floor.","es":"¿Dónde vives?","qau":"6b98c2cb40","aau":"f41c224b99"},{"q":"What's opposite your house?","a":"There's a small park opposite my house.","es":"¿Qué hay enfrente de tu casa?","qau":"1739f10a2c","aau":"1d167a6053"},{"q":"Where were you this morning?","a":"I was at work, in a meeting.","es":"¿Dónde estabas esta mañana?","qau":"f2fd129842","aau":"6e7ef69d5a"},{"q":"Have you ever walked across a famous bridge?","a":"Yes, I've walked across the Golden Gate Bridge.","es":"¿Alguna vez has cruzado a pie un puente famoso?","qau":"282f39dd8a","aau":"dffbef1cbd"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe tu ruta favorita para caminar, correr o manejar. Usa al menos 5 preposiciones: across, along, through, opposite, on, at, in.","kw":["across","along"],"n":5,"model":"I start at my house on Oak Street. I walk along the river for ten minutes. Then I go across a small bridge and through a park. There's a bakery opposite the park. I finish at the gym on the corner."}},{"id":"t7p2","topic":7,"part":2,"title":"Directions in a US city","es":"Direcciones en una ciudad de EE. UU.","acts":["learn","gridCity","dialogue","fill","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>🗺️ Para dar direcciones usa el <b>imperativo</b>: <i><b>Go</b> straight, <b>turn</b> left, <b>cross</b> the street, <b>take</b> the second right.</i></p>\n<p>🏙️ Frases preposicionales clave: <i><b>on the corner of</b> Main and 2nd · <b>across from</b> (= opposite, muy americano) · <b>next to</b> · <b>between</b> X and Y · <b>in front of</b> · <b>behind</b> · <b>at the end of</b> the street · <b>around the corner</b></i>.</p>\n<p>📫 <b>on</b> + calle (<i>on Elm Street</i>) · <b>at</b> + dirección exacta (<i>at 350 Fifth Avenue</i>).</p>\n<p>🙏 Para preguntar de forma amable: <i>Excuse me, <b>could you tell me how to get to</b> ...? · <b>Is there a</b> pharmacy <b>around here</b>?</i></p>","tips":["En EE. UU. se cuentan las distancias en <b>blocks</b> (cuadras): <i>two blocks down</i>.","<b>across from</b> se dice de corrido: <i>akrós-from</i>.","<b>You can't miss it</b>: la t de <i>can't</i> casi no suena: <i>yu-kén-mísit</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"Go straight for two blocks.","es":"Sigue derecho dos cuadras.","img":"u:photo-1774949884464-7be323ddeee2","v":"f","au":"4fa968cb7d"},{"en":"Turn left on Main Street.","es":"Gira a la izquierda en Main Street.","img":"u:photo-1783172189528-08225407491b","v":"m","au":"aa6e7787c7"},{"en":"It's on your right.","es":"Está a tu derecha.","img":"u:photo-1672819030357-464e40e5abd8","v":"f","au":"d54d8108b4"},{"en":"at the intersection","es":"en la intersección","img":"u:photo-1760371909304-c8bffd3a7e62","v":"m","au":"0e0f775797"},{"en":"right across from the park","es":"justo enfrente del parque","img":"u:photo-1519331379826-f10be5486c6f","v":"f","au":"411fce872d"},{"en":"next to the gas station","es":"al lado de la gasolinera","img":"u:photo-1695561324569-5e47c76dc0a3","v":"m","au":"ebc1f0c17d"},{"en":"between Fifth and Sixth Avenue","es":"entre la Quinta y la Sexta Avenida","img":"u:photo-1440330033336-7dcff4630cef","v":"f","au":"4a5fc9576a"},{"en":"at the end of the street","es":"al final de la calle","img":"u:photo-1555636222-cae831e670b3","v":"m","au":"e4672e9ec7"},{"en":"around the corner","es":"a la vuelta de la esquina","img":"u:photo-1760371909304-c8bffd3a7e62","v":"f","au":"5677452121"},{"en":"You can't miss it.","es":"No tiene pérdida.","img":"u:photo-1604488912264-dfed70450d76","v":"m","au":"9aeda70ef5"},{"en":"a crosswalk","es":"un paso peatonal","img":"u:photo-1518890714631-19d0b2fed537","v":"f","au":"153e3517d5"},{"en":"a block","es":"una cuadra","img":"u:photo-1477959858617-67f85cf4f1df","v":"m","au":"1ad4d6fb07"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Excuse me, could you tell me how to get to Union Station?","es":"Disculpe, ¿podría decirme cómo llegar a Union Station?","img":"u:photo-1648652678596-d3873bd0c157","v":"m","au":"29c4126b54"},{"en":"Go straight for three blocks and turn right on Elm Street.","es":"Sigue derecho tres cuadras y gira a la derecha en Elm Street.","img":"u:photo-1774949884464-7be323ddeee2","v":"f","au":"a932eeabde"},{"en":"The bank is on the corner of Main and 2nd.","es":"El banco está en la esquina de Main con la 2.ª.","img":"u:photo-1760371909304-c8bffd3a7e62","v":"m","au":"18279b0ede"},{"en":"There's a coffee shop right across from the hotel.","es":"Hay un café justo enfrente del hotel.","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"f","au":"7774e9b8fc"},{"en":"The museum is between the library and City Hall.","es":"El museo está entre la biblioteca y la alcaldía.","img":"u:photo-1780394956663-05ab87a150a5","v":"m","au":"8cf05378e4"},{"en":"It's just around the corner. You can't miss it.","es":"Está a la vuelta de la esquina. No tiene pérdida.","img":"u:photo-1604488912264-dfed70450d76","v":"f","au":"d77b935caa"}],"fill":[{"s":"Turn left ___ Oak Street.","a":"on","o":["in","at"],"h":"calles → on","full":"Turn left on Oak Street.","au":"1eb7aaa8f1"},{"s":"The hotel is ___ 350 Fifth Avenue.","a":"at","o":["on","in"],"h":"dirección exacta → at","full":"The hotel is at 350 Fifth Avenue.","au":"42fab7e578"},{"s":"The gym is ___ the bank and the bakery.","a":"between","o":["among","opposite"],"h":"entre dos cosas","full":"The gym is between the bank and the bakery.","au":"abfbc0cfe6"},{"s":"There's a parking lot ___ the building.","a":"behind","o":["between","among"],"h":"detrás","full":"There's a parking lot behind the building.","au":"3247d7387d"},{"s":"The café is right ___ from the park.","a":"across","o":["opposite","front"],"h":"across from = enfrente","full":"The café is right across from the park.","au":"748a2408ca"},{"s":"Go straight ___ two blocks.","a":"for","o":["during","since"],"h":"for + distancia","full":"Go straight for two blocks.","au":"ffdc125bd3"},{"s":"The ATM is ___ the end of the hall.","a":"at","o":["in","on"],"h":"at the end of","full":"The ATM is at the end of the hall.","au":"e60bbce098"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Lost in Chicago","es":"Perdida en Chicago","img":"u:photo-1648652678596-d3873bd0c157","lines":[{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Excuse me, officer. Could you tell me how to get to the Art Institute?","au":"bf4ae9fcd1"},{"who":"Officer","v":"m","t":"Sure. You're on State Street right now. Go straight for two blocks until you get to Adams.","au":"ff39e2dc65"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Two blocks, then Adams Street. Okay.","au":"aed50f9ddc"},{"who":"Officer","v":"m","t":"Turn left on Adams and walk east for about three blocks. You'll see the park.","au":"7d69349a29"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Is the museum in the park?","au":"5955f86db4"},{"who":"Officer","v":"m","t":"Not exactly. It's on Michigan Avenue, right across from the park. There are two big lion statues in front of it.","au":"e13615246f"},{"who":"Sofía","v":"f","t":"Lions! Great. Is there a coffee shop around here, by the way?","au":"6c6988595b"},{"who":"Officer","v":"m","t":"There's one just around the corner, next to the bank. You can't miss it.","au":"2d48be5c1a"}],"q":[{"q":"What street is Sofía on at the start?","a":"State Street.","o":["Adams Street.","Michigan Avenue."]},{"q":"Where is the Art Institute?","a":"Across from the park on Michigan Avenue.","o":["Inside the park.","Next to the bank."]},{"q":"Where is the coffee shop?","a":"Around the corner, next to the bank.","o":["In the museum.","On Adams Street."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To ask for and give directions in a US city.","es":"Pedir y dar direcciones en una ciudad de EE. UU."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever gotten lost in a city? What happened?","au":"8771ca5cd3","es":"¿Alguna vez te has perdido en una ciudad? ¿Qué pasó?","ex":"Yes, I got lost in Boston, but a woman helped me."},{"q":"Do you prefer using a map app or asking people for directions?","au":"fad0c4b6ac","es":"¿Prefieres usar una app de mapas o preguntar direcciones a la gente?","ex":"I prefer a map app, but asking people is good practice."}],"reading":{"title":"Welcome to the neighborhood","img":"u:photo-1555636222-cae831e670b3","text":"Welcome to Maple Grove! Here's a quick guide to help you find your way around. Our community center is at 120 Pine Street, on the corner of Pine and Third Avenue. If you need groceries, go straight down Pine for two blocks and turn left on Fifth Avenue. The supermarket is on your right, next to the gas station. Need a coffee? There's a great little café right across from the library, between the bookstore and the bank. The public library is open until 8 p.m. and has free Wi-Fi. For families with kids, Lincoln Park is at the end of Oak Street. Walk through the park and you'll find a playground behind the lake. The nearest bus stop is just around the corner from the community center, in front of the pharmacy. Buses to downtown leave every fifteen minutes. If you ever get lost, just ask a neighbor. People here are friendly, and you can't miss the big red water tower!","au":"c77f6ee865","q":[{"s":"The community center is on the corner of Pine and Third Avenue.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The supermarket is next to the library.","a":"no"},{"s":"The café is across from the library.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The playground is in front of the lake.","a":"no"},{"s":"The bus stop is in front of the pharmacy.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Excuse me, is there a pharmacy around here?","a":"Yes, there's one on the corner of Main and 2nd.","es":"Disculpe, ¿hay una farmacia por aquí?","qau":"023822c0ee","aau":"83766f6c6f"},{"q":"How do I get to the train station?","a":"Go straight for two blocks and turn left. It's on your right.","es":"¿Cómo llego a la estación de tren?","qau":"4a30978fec","aau":"965e74f538"},{"q":"What's next to your house?","a":"There's a small grocery store next to my house.","es":"¿Qué hay al lado de tu casa?","qau":"86228d2b2e","aau":"e96841f2dc"},{"q":"Where's the nearest ATM?","a":"It's right across from the bank, next to the café.","es":"¿Dónde está el cajero más cercano?","qau":"f2227cc137","aau":"b40f921c0f"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe las direcciones desde tu casa hasta un lugar cercano (tienda, parque, estación). Usa go straight, turn, on the corner of, across from y next to.","kw":["turn","across from"],"n":5,"model":"Leave my building and turn right. Go straight for three blocks. Turn left on the corner of Oak Street and 5th Avenue. The bakery is across from the park. It's next to the pharmacy, so you can't miss it."}}]},{"n":8,"title":"Comparatives and Superlatives","es":"Comparativos y superlativos","cover":"u:photo-1572766156884-828770df8d7e","parts":[{"id":"t8p1","topic":8,"part":1,"title":"Much better, far cheaper","es":"Mucho mejor, muchísimo más barato","acts":["learn","specShowdown","fill","sort","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>En nivel B2 no basta con decir <i>bigger</i> o <i>more expensive</i>: hay que decir <b>cuánta</b> diferencia hay.</p>\n<p>⬆️ <b>Diferencia grande</b>: <b>much / far / a lot / considerably</b> + comparativo → <i>Austin is <b>far</b> cheaper than San Francisco.</i><br>\n↗️ <b>Diferencia pequeña</b>: <b>a bit / a little / slightly</b> + comparativo → <i>This laptop is <b>slightly</b> lighter.</i></p>\n<p>🟰 <b>Igualdad</b>: <b>(just) as + adjetivo + as</b> → <i>The bus is <b>just as fast as</b> the train.</i><br>\n🚫 <b>Desigualdad</b>: <b>not as / not nearly as / nowhere near as … as</b> → <i>My new job is<b>n't nearly as stressful as</b> my old one.</i></p>\n<p>✖️ <b>Multiplicar</b>: <b>twice / three times as … as</b> → <i>Our new place is <b>twice as big as</b> the old one.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ Nunca digas <s>very bigger</s> ni <s>more cheaper</s>: <b>very</b> no va con comparativos y no se duplica el comparativo.</p>","tips":["<b>than</b> casi siempre suena débil: <i>dhən</i>. Une las palabras: <i>bigger than</i> → <i>bíguerdhən</i>.","En <b>as … as</b> la palabra <i>as</i> se reduce a <i>əz</i>: <i>əz fast əz</i>.","<b>comfortable</b> en EE. UU. suena <i>KÁMF-ter-bəl</i> (tres sílabas, no cuatro)."],"vocab":[{"en":"much more expensive","es":"mucho más caro","img":"u:photo-1773169206413-d48197b651d7","v":"f","au":"727a359236"},{"en":"far more convenient","es":"muchísimo más conveniente","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"m","au":"d4c4889929"},{"en":"a bit cheaper","es":"un poco más barato","img":"u:photo-1604719312266-d57b1438d4bf","v":"f","au":"70c566bb03"},{"en":"slightly bigger","es":"ligeramente más grande","img":"u:photo-1572766156884-828770df8d7e","v":"m","au":"ab17f7c84f"},{"en":"considerably faster","es":"considerablemente más rápido","img":"u:photo-1713918308760-5c9a02a8ca46","v":"f","au":"8a7d252ece"},{"en":"a lot more affordable","es":"mucho más asequible","img":"u:photo-1758523671285-9ff3f4e0ff38","v":"m","au":"2857228d61"},{"en":"just as reliable as","es":"igual de confiable que","img":"u:photo-1625047509248-ec889cbff17f","v":"f","au":"c9a4475b0f"},{"en":"not as crowded as","es":"no tan lleno como","img":"u:photo-1761839259488-2bdeeae794f5","v":"m","au":"07c6e91100"},{"en":"nowhere near as good as","es":"ni de cerca tan bueno como","img":"u:photo-1622566359362-539a508d6af5","v":"f","au":"9b5727ffca"},{"en":"twice as big as","es":"el doble de grande que","img":"u:photo-1666282167632-c613fbeb163c","v":"m","au":"e5c3245869"},{"en":"the same as","es":"igual que / lo mismo que","img":"u:photo-1669999666300-532838c49a6a","v":"f","au":"d80da78284"},{"en":"similar to","es":"parecido a","img":"u:photo-1718459724319-631e707cff92","v":"m","au":"d616c02825"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Living in Austin is much cheaper than living in San Francisco.","es":"Vivir en Austin es mucho más barato que vivir en San Francisco.","img":"u:photo-1588993608283-7f0eda4438be","v":"f","au":"87a14bea22"},{"en":"The new model is slightly lighter than the old one.","es":"El modelo nuevo es un poco más liviano que el viejo.","img":"u:photo-1498050108023-c5249f4df085","v":"m","au":"7d863193e1"},{"en":"Flying is far more convenient than driving across the country.","es":"Volar es muchísimo más conveniente que manejar por todo el país.","img":"u:photo-1569629743817-70d8db6c323b","v":"f","au":"70da883e29"},{"en":"My new commute isn't nearly as long as my old one.","es":"Mi nuevo trayecto no es ni de cerca tan largo como el anterior.","img":"u:photo-1449965408869-eaa3f722e40d","v":"m","au":"c51aadaf13"},{"en":"This apartment is twice as big as our old place.","es":"Este apartamento es el doble de grande que nuestro lugar anterior.","img":"u:photo-1666282167632-c613fbeb163c","v":"f","au":"1389f093f9"},{"en":"Online classes can be just as effective as face-to-face ones.","es":"Las clases en línea pueden ser igual de efectivas que las presenciales.","img":"u:photo-1758685848208-e108b6af94cc","v":"m","au":"41d15281a2"}],"fill":[{"s":"Seattle is ___ rainier than Phoenix.","a":"much","o":["very","more"],"h":"gran diferencia → much + comparativo","full":"Seattle is much rainier than Phoenix.","au":"ef244d6615"},{"s":"This hotel isn't as expensive ___ the one downtown.","a":"as","o":["than","like"],"h":"not as … as","full":"This hotel isn't as expensive as the one downtown.","au":"df69a914eb"},{"s":"The blue sofa is a ___ cheaper: only twenty dollars less.","a":"bit","o":["lot","much"],"h":"diferencia pequeña","full":"The blue sofa is a bit cheaper: only twenty dollars less.","au":"19070ac809"},{"s":"Her English is far ___ than mine.","a":"better","o":["gooder","more good"],"h":"good → better (irregular)","full":"Her English is far better than mine.","au":"e496cf04f4"},{"s":"On short trips, the train is just as fast ___ the plane.","a":"as","o":["than","that"],"h":"igualdad: as … as","full":"On short trips, the train is just as fast as the plane.","au":"564d496572"},{"s":"Our new office is ___ bigger than the old one. It's huge!","a":"far","o":["very","too"],"h":"far = muchísimo","full":"Our new office is far bigger than the old one. It's huge!","au":"7fb77f0a39"},{"s":"My salary is the same ___ yours.","a":"as","o":["than","like"],"h":"the same as","full":"My salary is the same as yours.","au":"d240a01242"}],"sort":{"cats":["⬆️ big difference","↗️ small difference","🟰 no difference"],"items":[{"w":"much more","c":"⬆️ big difference","au":"be985c72a4"},{"w":"far better","c":"⬆️ big difference","au":"807ca5fbba"},{"w":"a lot cheaper","c":"⬆️ big difference","au":"a6c69c76f9"},{"w":"considerably faster","c":"⬆️ big difference","au":"8a7d252ece"},{"w":"a bit faster","c":"↗️ small difference","au":"8ec59756ca"},{"w":"slightly older","c":"↗️ small difference","au":"3ad5b870af"},{"w":"a little more","c":"↗️ small difference","au":"b0e7ea436c"},{"w":"just as good as","c":"🟰 no difference","au":"b9ffbad085"},{"w":"the same as","c":"🟰 no difference","au":"d80da78284"},{"w":"as tall as","c":"🟰 no difference","au":"e79678cf19"}]},"goal":{"en":"To compare things precisely using much, far, slightly and as … as.","es":"Comparar con precisión usando much, far, slightly y as … as."},"warm":[{"q":"Is your city more expensive than it was five years ago?","au":"332c52f2cf","es":"¿Tu ciudad es más cara que hace cinco años?","ex":"Yes, it's much more expensive. Rent is almost twice as high."},{"q":"Which is more convenient for you: working from home or at the office?","au":"a208ef96fe","es":"¿Qué es más conveniente para ti: trabajar desde casa o en la oficina?","ex":"Working from home is far more convenient for me."}],"reading":{"title":"Austin or San Francisco?","img":"u:photo-1588993608283-7f0eda4438be","text":"When Valeria got two job offers last spring, she made a spreadsheet to compare them. The salary in San Francisco was slightly higher, about eight percent more. However, rent was a completely different story: a one-bedroom apartment there was far more expensive than in Austin, almost twice as much. Valeria also compared commutes. In San Francisco she would take a train, which is much more relaxing than driving, but the trip was considerably longer. In Austin the office was only fifteen minutes away. The weather was another factor. Austin is a lot hotter in the summer, and the winters aren't nearly as mild as people think. Still, she decided that the heat wasn't as bad as paying half her salary in rent. In the end, she chose Austin. \"My life isn't as exciting as my friends' lives in California,\" she jokes, \"but my savings account is a lot happier.\"","au":"f61793b94d","q":[{"s":"The salary in San Francisco was much higher than in Austin.","a":"no"},{"s":"Rent in San Francisco was almost twice as much as in Austin.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The commute in San Francisco was considerably longer.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Valeria thinks the heat in Austin is worse than paying very high rent.","a":"no"},{"s":"Valeria chose the job in Austin.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Is your city much bigger than your hometown?","a":"Yes, it's far bigger, and it's a lot more crowded.","es":"¿Tu ciudad es mucho más grande que tu pueblo natal?","qau":"b9c70b8c22","aau":"11950dc17f"},{"q":"Which is cheaper: cooking at home or eating out?","a":"Cooking at home is much cheaper than eating out.","es":"¿Qué es más barato: cocinar en casa o comer afuera?","qau":"00122929b2","aau":"c1b03e1015"},{"q":"Is your English as good as your best friend's?","a":"It's not as good as hers yet, but it's getting closer.","es":"¿Tu inglés es tan bueno como el de tu mejor amigo?","qau":"a0122b62af","aau":"13b8cc7c28"},{"q":"Are smartphones twice as expensive as they used to be?","a":"Some of them are almost twice as expensive.","es":"¿Los celulares cuestan el doble que antes?","qau":"09e7147b8c","aau":"113f21988e"}],"hw":{"es":"Compara dos ciudades, trabajos o productos que conozcas. Usa much/far/a bit + comparativo y as … as.","kw":["much","far","as"],"n":5,"model":"Miami is much warmer than Chicago. Chicago is far colder in the winter. Rent in Miami is a bit more expensive. Chicago's public transportation is far better. Miami isn't as busy as Chicago."}},{"id":"t8p2","topic":8,"part":2,"title":"The best I've ever had","es":"Lo mejor que he probado","acts":["learn","awardsNight","dialogue","fill","memory","speak"],"tip":"<p>✨ <b>The + comparativo …, the + comparativo …</b> = <i>cuanto más …, más …</i><br>\n<i><b>The more</b> you practice, <b>the more confident</b> you become.</i> · <i><b>The sooner, the better.</b></i></p>\n<p>📈 <b>Comparativo doble</b> = algo que cambia poco a poco (<i>cada vez más</i>):<br>\n<i>bigger <b>and</b> bigger</i> · <i><b>more and more</b> expensive</i> · <i>worse and worse</i></p>\n<p>🏆 <b>Superlativo + present perfect</b> = experiencias de toda la vida:<br>\n<i>It's <b>the best</b> pizza <b>I've ever had</b>.</i> · <i>the <b>most</b> beautiful place <b>I've ever seen</b></i></p>\n<p>🥇 Para reforzar el superlativo: <b>by far the …</b> (de lejos) · <b>one of the …</b> + plural · <b>the second / third largest</b> · <b>the least</b> (el menos).</p>","tips":["En <b>the more, the better</b> la <i>the</i> se dice rápido y suave: <i>dhə</i>.","<b>I've ever</b> se une: <i>áivévər</i>. No olvides la <i>v</i> de <i>I've</i>.","<b>largest</b> en EE. UU. suena con <i>r</i> marcada: <i>LÁR-dʒist</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"the more, the better","es":"cuanto más, mejor","img":"#The more, the better!","v":"f","au":"1fe226bf80"},{"en":"the sooner, the better","es":"cuanto antes, mejor","img":"u:photo-1676287566973-7e25f18f12a9","v":"m","au":"7c0d852044"},{"en":"by far the best","es":"de lejos el mejor","img":"u:photo-1578269174936-2709b6aeb913","v":"f","au":"9b5cd725ea"},{"en":"the best I've ever had","es":"el mejor que he probado","img":"u:photo-1723893905879-0e309c2a8e06","v":"m","au":"a24759fb2f"},{"en":"the worst I've ever seen","es":"el peor que he visto","img":"u:photo-1702308954905-341065817003","v":"f","au":"b8f24c6fa8"},{"en":"one of the most popular","es":"uno de los más populares","img":"u:photo-1501386761578-eac5c94b800a","v":"m","au":"7c93283c3c"},{"en":"the least expensive","es":"el menos caro","img":"u:photo-1604719312266-d57b1438d4bf","v":"f","au":"b6166c1d07"},{"en":"bigger and bigger","es":"cada vez más grande","img":"u:photo-1477959858617-67f85cf4f1df","v":"m","au":"d1e0845ff6"},{"en":"more and more expensive","es":"cada vez más caro","img":"u:photo-1764390555453-9e4035c7e283","v":"f","au":"a6173e74cc"},{"en":"the second largest","es":"el segundo más grande","img":"u:photo-1530089711124-9ca31fb9e863","v":"m","au":"edcb0e62f4"},{"en":"the most stressful","es":"el más estresante","img":"u:photo-1713947503867-3b27964f042b","v":"f","au":"141c1ea37f"}],"sentences":[{"en":"The more you practice, the more confident you become.","es":"Cuanto más practicas, más seguro te vuelves.","img":"u:photo-1580894732444-8ecded7900cd","v":"f","au":"83430a0a2b"},{"en":"This is by far the best pizza I've ever had in New York.","es":"Esta es de lejos la mejor pizza que he comido en Nueva York.","img":"u:photo-1604382354936-07c5d9983bd3","v":"m","au":"a0d7a50dc5"},{"en":"Rent in Miami is getting more and more expensive.","es":"El arriendo en Miami está cada vez más caro.","img":"u:photo-1717940749812-c202bec41ee5","v":"f","au":"357058fd35"},{"en":"It was the most stressful interview I've ever had.","es":"Fue la entrevista más estresante que he tenido.","img":"u:photo-1758520144437-f068ecaf0d83","v":"m","au":"fca6fc727e"},{"en":"The sooner we book the flights, the cheaper they'll be.","es":"Cuanto antes reservemos los vuelos, más baratos serán.","img":"u:photo-1536686896115-84529b61694c","v":"f","au":"7d72d645c0"},{"en":"Chicago is one of the most interesting cities I've ever visited.","es":"Chicago es una de las ciudades más interesantes que he visitado.","img":"u:photo-1493134799591-2c9eed26201a","v":"m","au":"9e9d4483ce"}],"fill":[{"s":"The ___ you sleep, the better you feel.","a":"more","o":["most","much"],"h":"the + comparativo, the + comparativo","full":"The more you sleep, the better you feel.","au":"af0d25d0e7"},{"s":"It's by far the ___ movie I've seen this year.","a":"best","o":["better","good"],"h":"by far + superlativo","full":"It's by far the best movie I've seen this year.","au":"d8e1df39ea"},{"s":"Gas prices are getting higher and ___.","a":"higher","o":["high","highest"],"h":"comparativo doble","full":"Gas prices are getting higher and higher.","au":"89c15498b9"},{"s":"This is the most delicious meal I've ___ eaten.","a":"ever","o":["never","already"],"h":"superlativo + I've ever","full":"This is the most delicious meal I've ever eaten.","au":"5faa9af5ea"},{"s":"The longer we wait, the ___ expensive the tickets get.","a":"more","o":["most","much"],"h":"the …, the more","full":"The longer we wait, the more expensive the tickets get.","au":"a951a76541"},{"s":"She's one of the ___ talented designers in the company.","a":"most","o":["more","much"],"h":"one of the most + plural","full":"She's one of the most talented designers in the company.","au":"8595c42fbf"},{"s":"Houston is the fourth ___ city in the United States.","a":"largest","o":["larger","large"],"h":"the fourth largest","full":"Houston is the fourth largest city in the United States.","au":"47fd7b9a3e"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Rating our road trip","es":"Calificando nuestro viaje por carretera","img":"u:photo-1756142008330-87dc106322a4","lines":[{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"So, what was the best part of the road trip for you?","au":"26de7a1bbd"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Honestly, the Grand Canyon. It's by far the most amazing place I've ever seen.","au":"c6f93067e3"},{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"I agree. Las Vegas was fun, but it was nowhere near as impressive.","au":"2e35df10d0"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"And the food in Santa Fe was the best I've had in years.","au":"ec8a7d3f7c"},{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"True! Although the hotel there was a bit more expensive than the others.","au":"24137bdfaf"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Well, the longer we stayed, the more we spent. That's travel!","au":"50eb70aef9"},{"who":"Emma","v":"f","t":"Next year let's plan earlier. The sooner we book, the cheaper it gets.","au":"b85594f9e8"},{"who":"Diego","v":"m","t":"Deal. And let's rent a slightly bigger car this time!","au":"7fb03c850f"}],"q":[{"q":"What was Diego's favorite place?","a":"The Grand Canyon.","o":["Las Vegas.","Santa Fe."]},{"q":"What did Emma say about the hotel in Santa Fe?","a":"It was a bit more expensive.","o":["It was the cheapest.","It was far bigger."]},{"q":"What do they want to do next year?","a":"Book earlier and rent a bigger car.","o":["Stay longer in Las Vegas.","Travel by plane."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To describe extremes and changes using superlatives, the … the … and double comparatives.","es":"Describir extremos y cambios con superlativos, the … the … y comparativos dobles."},"warm":[{"q":"What is the best meal you've ever had?","au":"15bd71dd34","es":"¿Cuál es la mejor comida que has probado?","ex":"The best meal I've ever had was a seafood dinner in Miami."},{"q":"What is the most beautiful place you've ever visited?","au":"579f64b99e","es":"¿Cuál es el lugar más hermoso que has visitado?","ex":"The most beautiful place I've ever visited is Yosemite."}],"reading":{"title":"The best trip of my life","img":"u:photo-1575527048208-6475b441e0a0","text":"People often ask me about the best trip I've ever taken. The answer is easy: driving Route 66 with my brother. It's by far the most memorable experience of my life. We started in Chicago and drove almost 2,500 miles to Santa Monica. The farther west we went, the emptier the roads became. In Texas and New Mexico, the towns got smaller and smaller, and the sky seemed bigger and bigger. The Grand Canyon was the most breathtaking place I've ever seen. We arrived at sunset, and it was one of the quietest moments of the whole trip. Of course, not everything was perfect. The worst motel we stayed in was in Arizona: it was the least comfortable bed I've ever slept in! Still, the more problems we had, the more we laughed. My advice? If you want to do it, go soon. The sooner you go, the better, because gas is getting more and more expensive every year.","au":"2e0b211a84","q":[{"s":"The writer drove Route 66 with his sister.","a":"no"},{"s":"The roads became emptier as they went west.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The Grand Canyon was the most breathtaking place he has ever seen.","a":"yes"},{"s":"The best motel was in Arizona.","a":"no"},{"s":"He thinks gas is getting cheaper every year.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What is the best movie you've ever seen?","a":"The best movie I've ever seen is Coco.","es":"¿Cuál es la mejor película que has visto?","qau":"a9d37150e6","aau":"5042e9ef8e"},{"q":"What is the hardest thing about learning English?","a":"The hardest thing is understanding fast conversations.","es":"¿Qué es lo más difícil de aprender inglés?","qau":"fdf3928791","aau":"cdeb694f0a"},{"q":"Is life getting more and more expensive?","a":"Yes, everything is getting more and more expensive.","es":"¿La vida está cada vez más cara?","qau":"23e01ee070","aau":"076a5152e3"},{"q":"Do you agree that the more you read, the more you learn?","a":"Yes, the more you read, the more vocabulary you learn.","es":"¿Estás de acuerdo en que cuanto más lees, más aprendes?","qau":"e51be0475b","aau":"9f4008b64b"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe una reseña de tu mejor viaje o restaurante. Usa superlativo + I've ever, by far, the … the … y un comparativo doble.","kw":["ever","the more","by far"],"n":5,"model":"The best restaurant I've ever been to is in Miami. It's by far the most delicious seafood in the city. The more you eat, the more you want. It's getting more and more popular. It's the most expensive place I've ever eaten at, but it's worth it."}}]},{"n":9,"title":"Used To and Be/Get Used To","es":"Used to y be/get used to","cover":"u:photo-1528569937393-ee892b976859","parts":[{"id":"t9p1","topic":9,"part":1,"title":"How things used to be","es":"Cómo eran las cosas antes","acts":["learn","thenNow","sort","fill","typeSentence","speak"],"tip":"<p>🕰️ <b>used to + verbo base</b> = algo que <b>solía</b> pasar o ser, y <b>ya no</b> es así.<br>\n<i>I <b>used to live</b> in Chicago.</i> (Ya no vivo allá.)</p>\n<p>➖ Negativa: <b>didn't use to</b> (¡sin <i>-d</i>!) → <i>She <b>didn't use to</b> drink coffee.</i><br>\n❓ Pregunta: <b>Did you use to …?</b> → <i><b>Did you use to</b> play sports?</i></p>\n<p>🔁 <b>would + verbo</b> también describe <b>acciones repetidas</b> del pasado (muy común al contar recuerdos):<br>\n<i>Every summer we <b>would</b> drive to the lake.</i></p>\n<p>⚠️ Con <b>estados</b> (live, have, be, own, know, like) solo se usa <b>used to</b>:<br>\n✅ <i>I used to have a dog.</i> · ❌ <s>I would have a dog.</s></p>\n<p>💡 <b>no longer</b> (formal, antes del verbo) = <b>not … anymore</b> (al final): <i>I <b>no longer</b> smoke.</i> = <i>I do<b>n't</b> smoke <b>anymore</b>.</i></p>","tips":["<b>used to</b> se pronuncia <i>IÚS-tə</i>, con <b>s</b> (no z) y la <i>d</i> desaparece.","<b>use to</b> (en negativa y pregunta) suena exactamente igual: <i>iústə</i>.","<b>would</b> se reduce mucho: <i>we'd</i> → <i>uíd</i>. La <i>l</i> nunca suena."],"vocab":[{"en":"used to live","es":"solía vivir","img":"u:photo-1528569937393-ee892b976859","v":"f","au":"204ecebd24"},{"en":"didn't use to","es":"no solía","img":"u:photo-1639986169769-feb3c3a92346","v":"m","au":"bceb0954e2"},{"en":"Did you use to …?","es":"¿Solías …?","img":"#Did you use to …?","v":"f","au":"184ad4d4d2"},{"en":"would spend hours","es":"pasaba horas (solía pasar)","img":"u:photo-1627764940620-90393d0e8c34","v":"m","au":"3c6932437b"},{"en":"back in the day","es":"en aquellos tiempos","img":"u:photo-1646098666651-9ab522ef05a0","v":"f","au":"a777b14fd7"},{"en":"when I was a kid","es":"cuando era niño","img":"u:photo-1595182747080-3b43712dd27d","v":"m","au":"b2055654fc"},{"en":"payphone","es":"teléfono público","img":"u:photo-1450818074504-fb9713fe584e","v":"f","au":"00f5e648da"},{"en":"rent movies","es":"alquilar películas","img":"u:photo-1646098666651-9ab522ef05a0","v":"m","au":"add0b0d023"},{"en":"write letters by hand","es":"escribir cartas a mano","img":"u:photo-1455390582262-044cdead277a","v":"f","au":"c48fc8713f"},{"en":"no longer","es":"ya no","img":"u:photo-1622708037376-5cba1a57f735","v":"m","au":"2916c3b705"},{"en":"not … anymore","es":"ya no (al final)","img":"u:photo-1758273705845-095eaa831790","v":"f","au":"d23ee78c5e"},{"en":"nowadays","es":"hoy en día","img":"u:photo-1592890288564-76628a30a657","v":"m","au":"ffaca6c921"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I used to live in Chicago, but now I live in Dallas.","es":"Antes vivía en Chicago, pero ahora vivo en Dallas.","img":"u:photo-1493134799591-2c9eed26201a","v":"f","au":"a77a7de180"},{"en":"We would spend every summer at my grandparents' farm.","es":"Pasábamos todos los veranos en la granja de mis abuelos.","img":"u:photo-1571524188026-cc1d649962ea","v":"m","au":"2571defd18"},{"en":"She didn't use to like spicy food, but now she loves it.","es":"Antes no le gustaba la comida picante, pero ahora le encanta.","img":"u:photo-1687881063470-a78e6ea2590e","v":"f","au":"047aa83d5e"},{"en":"Did you use to play any sports in high school?","es":"¿Practicabas algún deporte en la secundaria?","img":"u:photo-1663563624897-de8972d7ce93","v":"m","au":"97ea695a2b"},{"en":"People used to rent movies; nowadays they stream them.","es":"La gente alquilaba películas; hoy en día las ve por streaming.","img":"u:photo-1646098666651-9ab522ef05a0","v":"f","au":"a641e1e329"},{"en":"My dad would always tell us stories before bed.","es":"Mi papá siempre nos contaba historias antes de dormir.","img":"u:photo-1758687126981-417a59c589a9","v":"m","au":"3a19ce5e36"}],"fill":[{"s":"I ___ to have long hair when I was in college.","a":"used","o":["use","using"],"h":"hábito o estado pasado","full":"I used to have long hair when I was in college.","au":"6eaf30a886"},{"s":"She didn't ___ to work on weekends.","a":"use","o":["used","uses"],"h":"didn't + use (sin -d)","full":"She didn't use to work on weekends.","au":"1f42c6f190"},{"s":"Did you ___ to live near the beach?","a":"use","o":["used","using"],"h":"pregunta con did + use","full":"Did you use to live near the beach?","au":"42cec224ba"},{"s":"When we were kids, we ___ play outside until dark.","a":"would","o":["will","were"],"h":"acción repetida → would","full":"When we were kids, we would play outside until dark.","au":"781c31de24"},{"s":"I don't smoke ___. I quit five years ago.","a":"anymore","o":["already","yet"],"h":"not … anymore = ya no","full":"I don't smoke anymore. I quit five years ago.","au":"2436d64ac8"},{"s":"My grandfather ___ to own a small store in El Paso.","a":"used","o":["would","was"],"h":"estado (own) → solo used to","full":"My grandfather used to own a small store in El Paso.","au":"530f8dcff4"}],"sort":{"cats":["🔁 used to / would","🏠 only used to"],"items":[{"w":"play soccer every Saturday","c":"🔁 used to / would","au":"c6278b8391"},{"w":"walk to school","c":"🔁 used to / would","au":"4cbfb96f46"},{"w":"spend summers at the lake","c":"🔁 used to / would","au":"f59dab4d59"},{"w":"visit my aunt on Sundays","c":"🔁 used to / would","au":"78e1ce5c5d"},{"w":"write letters to my pen pal","c":"🔁 used to / would","au":"97383f3743"},{"w":"have a dog","c":"🏠 only used to","au":"f27142f794"},{"w":"live in Boston","c":"🏠 only used to","au":"68aa2955e4"},{"w":"be very shy","c":"🏠 only used to","au":"98d3d4bdcb"},{"w":"own a red car","c":"🏠 only used to","au":"6feacbb5dd"},{"w":"believe in Santa Claus","c":"🏠 only used to","au":"33a66c7287"}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about past habits and states using used to, would and didn't use to.","es":"Hablar de hábitos y estados pasados con used to, would y didn't use to."},"warm":[{"q":"What did you use to do after school when you were a kid?","au":"ae42090c76","es":"¿Qué solías hacer después del colegio cuando eras niño?","ex":"I used to play soccer with my friends in the street."},{"q":"Is there anything you used to like that you don't like anymore?","au":"bfe6108cc2","es":"¿Hay algo que te gustaba antes y que ya no te gusta?","ex":"I used to love soda, but I don't drink it anymore."}],"reading":{"title":"Life before smartphones","img":"u:photo-1450818074504-fb9713fe584e","text":"My grandmother Elena loves telling us how life used to be in Los Angeles in the 1970s. Back then, people didn't use to carry phones in their pockets. If you needed to call someone, you would look for a payphone and hope you had enough coins. On Friday nights, her family would go to the video store, although she says they used to argue for an hour about which movie to rent. Elena used to write long letters to her cousin in Puerto Rico, and she would wait weeks for an answer. \"We didn't use to know what everybody was eating for lunch,\" she laughs, \"and honestly, we didn't miss it.\" She also used to own a big yellow car with no air conditioning. Nowadays she has a smartphone and video-calls her cousin every Sunday. She no longer writes letters, but she still keeps all the old ones in a box under her bed.","au":"5daaa75576","q":[{"s":"In the 1970s people used to carry phones in their pockets.","a":"no"},{"s":"Elena's family would go to the video store on Friday nights.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She used to write letters to her cousin in Puerto Rico.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her old car had air conditioning.","a":"no"},{"s":"She doesn't write letters anymore.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Where did you use to live when you were a child?","a":"I used to live in a small town near the coast.","es":"¿Dónde vivías cuando eras niño?","qau":"90e645eab8","aau":"8e157c0568"},{"q":"What would you do on summer vacations?","a":"We would visit my grandparents and swim in the river.","es":"¿Qué hacías en las vacaciones?","qau":"50ccdc4b96","aau":"0353d1aaab"},{"q":"Did you use to play any sports?","a":"Yes, I used to play basketball every weekend.","es":"¿Practicabas algún deporte?","qau":"6566786d76","aau":"dccf7d2770"},{"q":"What didn't you use to like that you like now?","a":"I didn't use to like vegetables, but now I love them.","es":"¿Qué no te gustaba antes que ahora sí te gusta?","qau":"1ba8acdd68","aau":"5404318716"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe sobre tu infancia: 3 cosas que solías hacer (used to / would) y 2 cosas que no solías hacer (didn't use to).","kw":["used to","would","didn't use to"],"n":5,"model":"When I was a kid, I used to live near the beach. Every Saturday we would play soccer on the sand. I used to have a dog called Max. I didn't use to like reading. I didn't use to drink coffee, but now I drink three cups a day."}},{"id":"t9p2","topic":9,"part":2,"title":"Getting used to life in the U.S.","es":"Acostumbrándose a la vida en EE. UU.","acts":["learn","cultureShock","dialogue","fill","matchLines","speak"],"tip":"<p>⚠️ ¡Cuidado! <b>used to</b> (solía) ≠ <b>be used to</b> (estar acostumbrado).</p>\n<p>✅ <b>be used to + sustantivo / verbo-ING</b> = estar acostumbrado (un <b>estado</b>):<br>\n<i>I'<b>m used to working</b> long hours.</i> · <i>She <b>isn't used to</b> the cold.</i></p>\n<p>🔄 <b>get used to + sustantivo / verbo-ING</b> = acostumbrarse (un <b>proceso</b>):<br>\n<i>You'll <b>get used to</b> it.</i> · <i>I'm <b>getting used to driving</b> on the highway.</i> · <i>It took me a year to <b>get used to</b> the winters.</i></p>\n<p>🧠 Aquí <b>to</b> es una preposición, por eso va <b>-ing</b>: ❌ <s>I'm used to work</s> → ✅ <i>I'm used to work<b>ing</b></i>.</p>\n<p>Funciona en todos los tiempos: <i>I <b>was</b> used to …</i> · <i>I'<b>ll get</b> used to …</i> · <i>I'<b>ve gotten</b> used to …</i></p>","tips":["En <b>I'm used to</b> une todo: <i>áim-iús-tə</i>.","<b>gotten</b> es el participio americano de <i>get</i>: <i>I've gotten used to it</i> (en EE. UU.).","<b>homesick</b> se acentúa al inicio: <i>HÓUM-sik</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"be used to driving","es":"estar acostumbrado a manejar","img":"u:photo-1530685932526-48ec92998eaa","v":"m","au":"98969dde81"},{"en":"get used to the cold","es":"acostumbrarse al frío","img":"u:photo-1583170492868-dd617c96fdee","v":"f","au":"27c915fc1a"},{"en":"I'm not used to it","es":"no estoy acostumbrado","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"m","au":"9b1e046774"},{"en":"I'm getting used to it","es":"me estoy acostumbrando","img":"u:photo-1758600435233-258658d68648","v":"f","au":"6f4a5f933c"},{"en":"culture shock","es":"choque cultural","img":"u:photo-1527824404775-dce343118ebc","v":"m","au":"f2cf6cf789"},{"en":"adjust to","es":"adaptarse a","img":"u:photo-1758523671893-0ba21cf4260f","v":"f","au":"a63c7abae0"},{"en":"tipping","es":"dar propina","img":"u:photo-1778789752084-3639249582de","v":"m","au":"c5e7227d14"},{"en":"small talk","es":"conversación casual","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"f","au":"951dae8dd8"},{"en":"the imperial system","es":"el sistema imperial (millas, libras)","img":"u:photo-1550985543-49bee3167284","v":"m","au":"f4035e04a6"},{"en":"homesick","es":"con nostalgia (extrañar el hogar)","img":"u:photo-1642511241125-f0f8f4914907","v":"f","au":"b3c9546073"},{"en":"settle in","es":"instalarse y adaptarse","img":"u:photo-1758523671893-0ba21cf4260f","v":"m","au":"f98907207c"},{"en":"feel at home","es":"sentirse como en casa","img":"u:photo-1758273705845-095eaa831790","v":"f","au":"238a59bbb6"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I'm used to working long hours, so it doesn't bother me.","es":"Estoy acostumbrado a trabajar muchas horas, así que no me molesta.","img":"u:photo-1544717302-de2939b7ef71","v":"f","au":"d26325a6c3"},{"en":"It took me a year to get used to the winters in Minneapolis.","es":"Me tomó un año acostumbrarme a los inviernos de Minneapolis.","img":"u:photo-1677253170860-b5f20dab49c3","v":"m","au":"21a9fe430a"},{"en":"She isn't used to tipping twenty percent at restaurants.","es":"Ella no está acostumbrada a dejar veinte por ciento de propina.","img":"u:photo-1778789752084-3639249582de","v":"f","au":"5961bf25c3"},{"en":"Are you used to driving on the highway yet?","es":"¿Ya estás acostumbrado a manejar en la autopista?","img":"u:photo-1530685932526-48ec92998eaa","v":"m","au":"f719d80e23"},{"en":"You'll get used to it; just give it some time.","es":"Te vas a acostumbrar; solo dale tiempo.","img":"u:photo-1653762381632-2945469edb7b","v":"f","au":"495efcc73e"},{"en":"After six months, we finally felt at home in Denver.","es":"Después de seis meses, por fin nos sentimos en casa en Denver.","img":"u:photo-1758523671893-0ba21cf4260f","v":"m","au":"9c2908089e"}],"fill":[{"s":"I'm used to ___ up early.","a":"getting","o":["get","got"],"h":"be used to + -ing","full":"I'm used to getting up early.","au":"4cec4b69da"},{"s":"It's hard to get used ___ a new language.","a":"to","o":["with","at"],"h":"get used to","full":"It's hard to get used to a new language.","au":"fa4f61233f"},{"s":"He ___ used to the noise yet.","a":"isn't","o":["doesn't","didn't"],"h":"be used to (negativo)","full":"He isn't used to the noise yet.","au":"a6e4a6491b"},{"s":"Don't worry. You'll ___ used to it.","a":"get","o":["be","use"],"h":"proceso → get used to","full":"Don't worry. You'll get used to it.","au":"5a377f5714"},{"s":"I used to ___ in Mexico City, but now I live in Houston.","a":"live","o":["living","lived"],"h":"used to + base (solía)","full":"I used to live in Mexico City, but now I live in Houston.","au":"eba154595d"},{"s":"They're getting used to ___ in miles instead of kilometers.","a":"thinking","o":["think","thought"],"h":"get used to + -ing","full":"They're getting used to thinking in miles instead of kilometers.","au":"eaabb13699"}],"dialogue":{"title":"New in Atlanta","es":"Nueva en Atlanta","img":"u:photo-1783780933273-392188f83694","lines":[{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"So, Lucía, how are you settling in? It's been three months, right?","au":"7a5dc002df"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"Yes! I'm slowly getting used to life in Atlanta.","au":"29ef6e2d3f"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"What was the hardest thing to get used to?","au":"7c3148beb1"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"Driving everywhere! In Madrid I used to take the subway to work.","au":"a6cd82ce62"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"Ha! Most people here aren't used to walking long distances.","au":"7a4a3d9ce2"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"And the small talk with strangers. I'm still not used to that.","au":"11041bc313"},{"who":"Mike","v":"m","t":"You'll get used to it. Soon you'll be chatting with cashiers like a local.","au":"b36001ae78"},{"who":"Lucía","v":"f","t":"I hope so! At least I've already gotten used to tipping.","au":"61a43f1be5"}],"q":[{"q":"How long has Lucía been in Atlanta?","a":"Three months.","o":["Three years.","Six weeks."]},{"q":"How did she use to go to work in Madrid?","a":"By subway.","o":["By car.","On foot."]},{"q":"What is she still not used to?","a":"Small talk with strangers.","o":["Tipping.","Driving."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about adapting to new situations with be used to and get used to.","es":"Hablar de adaptarse a situaciones nuevas con be used to y get used to."},"warm":[{"q":"What was hard to get used to when you started your current job?","au":"ce2c46d18c","es":"¿A qué fue difícil acostumbrarte cuando empezaste tu trabajo actual?","ex":"It was hard to get used to waking up at five."},{"q":"Are you used to speaking English with strangers?","au":"986344a075","es":"¿Estás acostumbrado a hablar inglés con desconocidos?","ex":"Not yet, but I'm getting used to it."}],"reading":{"title":"Six months in Minneapolis","img":"u:photo-1677253170860-b5f20dab49c3","text":"When Andrés moved from Mexico City to Minneapolis for a job in engineering, he thought the hardest part would be the language. He was wrong. His English was fine, but he wasn't used to temperatures of twenty degrees below zero. \"The first winter was a shock,\" he says. \"I had to get used to wearing three layers of clothes just to walk to my car.\" He also had to get used to the imperial system. At work, everything was in inches and pounds, and he was used to thinking in centimeters and kilos. Another surprise was small talk. Back home, he wasn't used to chatting with cashiers, but in Minnesota everybody talks about the weather. Now, after six months, he's getting used to the cold, and he even enjoys ice skating on weekends. \"I'm still not used to dinner at six o'clock,\" he admits, \"but I'm sure I'll get used to that too.\"","au":"e46f92ad4f","q":[{"s":"Andrés thought the language would be the hardest part.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He was used to extremely cold winters.","a":"no"},{"s":"At work he had to get used to inches and pounds.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He is getting used to the cold.","a":"yes"},{"s":"He is already used to eating dinner at six o'clock.","a":"no"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Are you used to getting up early?","a":"Yes, I'm used to getting up at five for work.","es":"¿Estás acostumbrado a levantarte temprano?","qau":"0e468e775e","aau":"e12af80784"},{"q":"What would be hard to get used to in another country?","a":"It would be hard to get used to the food.","es":"¿A qué sería difícil acostumbrarte en otro país?","qau":"59ed8984bb","aau":"83268a9f0e"},{"q":"Have you gotten used to using English at work?","a":"I'm getting used to it, little by little.","es":"¿Ya te acostumbraste a usar inglés en el trabajo?","qau":"e2758233c1","aau":"c06101163e"},{"q":"Did you use to live somewhere else?","a":"Yes, I used to live in Lima, but now I'm used to life here.","es":"¿Vivías en otro lugar antes?","qau":"60e798dc07","aau":"308635f9e2"}],"hw":{"es":"Imagina que te mudas a otra ciudad de EE. UU. Escribe a qué estás acostumbrado, a qué no, y a qué te estás acostumbrando.","kw":["used to","get used to","getting used to"],"n":5,"model":"I'm used to warm weather, so Chicago is hard. I'm not used to driving in the snow. I'm getting used to the cold little by little. I need to get used to tipping at restaurants. I'm sure I'll get used to it soon."}}]},{"n":10,"title":"Enough and Wish","es":"Enough y wish","cover":"u:photo-1464349153735-7db50ed83c84","parts":[{"id":"t10p1","topic":10,"part":1,"title":"Too heavy, not old enough","es":"Demasiado pesado, no tiene la edad suficiente","acts":["learn","limitGauge","fill","listenChoose","raceGame","speak"],"tip":"<p>🔴 <b>too + adjetivo (+ for alguien) + to + verbo</b> = demasiado … para:<br>\n<i>This suitcase is <b>too heavy to</b> carry on.</i> · <i>The coffee is <b>too hot for me to</b> drink.</i></p>\n<p>🟢 <b>adjetivo + enough + to + verbo</b> = suficientemente … para (¡<b>enough</b> va DESPUÉS del adjetivo!):<br>\n<i>He isn't <b>old enough to</b> rent a car.</i> · ❌ <s>enough old</s></p>\n<p>🟢 <b>enough + sustantivo</b> (¡ANTES del sustantivo!): <i>We don't have <b>enough time</b>.</i></p>\n<p>📦 <b>too much</b> + incontable (<i>too much traffic</i>) · <b>too many</b> + plural (<i>too many people</i>).</p>\n<p>💥 Para reforzar: <b>far too / way too</b> (informal) → <i>It's <b>way too</b> expensive.</i><br>\n⚠️ <b>too</b> es negativo (un problema); para algo positivo usa <b>very</b> o <b>so</b>: <i>The hotel is <b>very</b> nice.</i></p>","tips":["<b>enough</b> se pronuncia <i>i-NÁF</i>: la <i>gh</i> suena como <b>f</b>.","<b>too</b> y <b>to</b> suenan parecido, pero <i>too</i> es largo y fuerte: <i>TÚU</i>; <i>to</i> es corto: <i>tə</i>.","<b>luggage</b> suena <i>LÁ-guidʒ</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"too tired to drive","es":"demasiado cansado para manejar","img":"u:photo-1610354878912-08f1ab8ae913","v":"f","au":"6ccef7fb27"},{"en":"old enough to vote","es":"con edad suficiente para votar","img":"u:photo-1782998307726-f93ec14eda24","v":"m","au":"e290137009"},{"en":"enough money to buy","es":"suficiente dinero para comprar","img":"u:photo-1593182440959-9d5165b29b59","v":"f","au":"0ece345a8e"},{"en":"not experienced enough","es":"sin suficiente experiencia","img":"u:photo-1758520144437-f068ecaf0d83","v":"m","au":"588ddf6752"},{"en":"too many people","es":"demasiada gente","img":"u:photo-1573358695783-005699a7fc94","v":"f","au":"dcaac42b8d"},{"en":"too much traffic","es":"demasiado tráfico","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"26ca118333"},{"en":"big enough for","es":"suficientemente grande para","img":"u:photo-1693578616322-c8abe6c7393d","v":"f","au":"6f4aa68bfa"},{"en":"far too expensive","es":"muchísimo más caro de lo aceptable","img":"u:photo-1773169206413-d48197b651d7","v":"m","au":"c80bf6dde8"},{"en":"carry-on bag","es":"equipaje de mano","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"f","au":"49ce7df0f2"},{"en":"overweight luggage","es":"equipaje con sobrepeso","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"m","au":"b8f7613679"},{"en":"meet the requirements","es":"cumplir los requisitos","img":"u:photo-1603796846097-bee99e4a601f","v":"f","au":"79751dcc93"},{"en":"qualify for","es":"calificar para","img":"u:photo-1562564055-71e051d33c19","v":"m","au":"6406f0fc5e"}],"sentences":[{"en":"My son isn't old enough to drive yet.","es":"Mi hijo todavía no tiene edad para manejar.","img":"u:photo-1527593167147-e9c94a5883e6","v":"f","au":"2eb2e78763"},{"en":"This suitcase is too heavy to take as a carry-on.","es":"Esta maleta es demasiado pesada para llevarla como equipaje de mano.","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","v":"m","au":"67aba7509f"},{"en":"We don't have enough time to visit both museums.","es":"No tenemos suficiente tiempo para visitar ambos museos.","img":"u:photo-1643288298077-f1d624de82ed","v":"f","au":"d388baaaf6"},{"en":"The coffee was too hot for me to drink.","es":"El café estaba demasiado caliente para que yo lo tomara.","img":"u:photo-1506372023823-741c83b836fe","v":"m","au":"f4e9eea565"},{"en":"Is your English good enough to work in customer service?","es":"¿Tu inglés es lo suficientemente bueno para trabajar en servicio al cliente?","img":"u:photo-1553775282-20af80779df7","v":"f","au":"f3b2cf4239"},{"en":"There were far too many people at the concert to find a seat.","es":"Había demasiada gente en el concierto para encontrar asiento.","img":"u:photo-1501386761578-eac5c94b800a","v":"m","au":"27bb77c171"}],"fill":[{"s":"She's ___ tired to go out tonight.","a":"too","o":["enough","very"],"h":"too + adjetivo + to","full":"She's too tired to go out tonight.","au":"9696fbb59a"},{"s":"He isn't tall ___ to play professional basketball.","a":"enough","o":["too","so"],"h":"adjetivo + enough","full":"He isn't tall enough to play professional basketball.","au":"22bd965b39"},{"s":"We don't have ___ chairs for everyone.","a":"enough","o":["too","too many"],"h":"enough + sustantivo","full":"We don't have enough chairs for everyone.","au":"38eb4d8a7d"},{"s":"There's too ___ sugar in this coffee.","a":"much","o":["many","enough"],"h":"too much + incontable","full":"There's too much sugar in this coffee.","au":"54da9990b0"},{"s":"The box was too heavy for me ___ lift.","a":"to","o":["for","of"],"h":"too … for me to + verbo","full":"The box was too heavy for me to lift.","au":"d8c649a7ab"},{"s":"Is the room big ___ for ten people?","a":"enough","o":["too","so"],"h":"adjetivo + enough","full":"Is the room big enough for ten people?","au":"4656d9a053"},{"s":"There are too ___ cars on the road today.","a":"many","o":["much","enough"],"h":"too many + plural","full":"There are too many cars on the road today.","au":"97bae47c65"}],"goal":{"en":"To talk about limits and requirements with too and enough + to-infinitive.","es":"Hablar de límites y requisitos con too y enough + infinitivo."},"warm":[{"q":"Do you have enough free time during the week?","au":"b7263efacc","es":"¿Tienes suficiente tiempo libre durante la semana?","ex":"No, I don't have enough time. I'm too busy with work."},{"q":"Is there anything you think you're too old or too young to do?","au":"6c7dbd7b5b","es":"¿Hay algo que creas que eres demasiado mayor o joven para hacer?","ex":"I don't think I'm too old to learn a new language."}],"reading":{"title":"Rules of the road trip","img":"u:photo-1762965119363-af950b523dca","text":"Planning a family trip to Orlando seemed easy until Mariana read the fine print. First, the airline: her suitcase was too heavy to check without paying an extra fee, and her backpack was slightly too big to count as a personal item. Then the car rental: her nephew Kevin, who is twenty-two, was old enough to drive, but he wasn't old enough to rent a car without a \"young driver\" fee. At the theme park, her youngest son, Leo, wasn't tall enough to ride the biggest roller coaster. He was furious! There was also too much to do and not enough time to see everything, so they had to choose. On the last day, the lines were far too long, and it was too hot to wait outside for two hours. Still, Mariana says the trip was worth it. \"Next year Leo will be tall enough, and I'll be smart enough to pack less!\"","au":"13f9146bc5","q":[{"s":"Mariana's suitcase was too heavy to check for free.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Kevin was old enough to rent a car with no extra fee.","a":"no"},{"s":"Leo was tall enough to ride the biggest roller coaster.","a":"no"},{"s":"They had enough time to see everything.","a":"no"},{"s":"Mariana plans to pack less next year.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Are you old enough to rent a car in the United States?","a":"Yes, I'm old enough, but I'd pay an extra fee.","es":"¿Tienes edad suficiente para alquilar un carro en EE. UU.?","qau":"b71f2c6529","aau":"41ae4edb72"},{"q":"Is your house big enough for a party?","a":"No, it's too small for more than ten people.","es":"¿Tu casa es lo suficientemente grande para una fiesta?","qau":"ca84cf2f47","aau":"352f6d803e"},{"q":"Do you have enough time to exercise?","a":"Not really. I'm too busy during the week.","es":"¿Tienes suficiente tiempo para hacer ejercicio?","qau":"b65141f29b","aau":"731fd5d5ee"},{"q":"Is there too much traffic in your city?","a":"Yes, there's far too much traffic in the mornings.","es":"¿Hay demasiado tráfico en tu ciudad?","qau":"d426bbb9b3","aau":"bc70cc4555"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe sobre un plan o viaje que salió mal: usa too + adjetivo + to, adjetivo + enough y enough + sustantivo.","kw":["too","enough"],"n":5,"model":"Last weekend we wanted to go to the beach. It was too cold to swim. My car wasn't big enough for everybody. We didn't have enough money for a hotel. There were too many people at the restaurant. Next time we'll plan better."}},{"id":"t10p2","topic":10,"part":2,"title":"I wish things were different","es":"Ojalá las cosas fueran diferentes","acts":["learn","genieLamp","dialogue","fill","speed","speak"],"tip":"<p>🌟 <b>wish</b> sirve para hablar de cosas que <b>no son reales</b> y nos gustaría cambiar. ¡El verbo “retrocede” un tiempo!</p>\n<p>1️⃣ Deseo sobre el <b>presente</b> → <b>wish + past simple</b>: <i>I <b>wish</b> I <b>had</b> more time.</i> (No tengo tiempo.)<br>\n👉 Con <i>be</i> se prefiere <b>were</b> para todos: <i>I wish I <b>were</b> taller.</i></p>\n<p>2️⃣ Arrepentimiento sobre el <b>pasado</b> → <b>wish + past perfect</b>: <i>I <b>wish</b> I <b>had studied</b> harder.</i> (No estudié.)</p>\n<p>3️⃣ Queja / quieres que <b>otra persona</b> cambie → <b>wish + would</b>: <i>I <b>wish</b> you <b>would</b> stop interrupting.</i><br>\n⚠️ No se usa <i>would</i> con uno mismo: ❌ <s>I wish I would …</s></p>\n<p>🔥 <b>If only …</b> = igual que <i>wish</i>, pero más emocional: <i><b>If only</b> I <b>hadn't</b> said that!</i></p>","tips":["<b>wish</b> tiene una <i>i</i> corta: <i>uísh</i>, no <i>uiish</i>.","<b>I'd</b> puede ser <i>I had</i> o <i>I would</i>: <i>I wish I'd known</i> = <i>I had known</i>.","<b>regret</b> se acentúa al final: <i>ri-GRÉT</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"I wish I had more time","es":"ojalá tuviera más tiempo","img":"u:photo-1790597038266-331053593165","v":"f","au":"e240f5b388"},{"en":"I wish I were taller","es":"ojalá fuera más alto","img":"u:photo-1752770719951-bbe2c0175ae7","v":"m","au":"c3f02d4363"},{"en":"I wish I had studied","es":"ojalá hubiera estudiado","img":"u:photo-1598981457915-aea220950616","v":"f","au":"5bcdbf416c"},{"en":"I wish you would stop","es":"ojalá dejaras de …","img":"u:photo-1688398159040-5aea0cd2a919","v":"m","au":"5421d1eb3e"},{"en":"If only I knew!","es":"¡Si tan solo supiera!","img":"u:photo-1649258539352-7ae1e3313cdb","v":"f","au":"6fbb32063b"},{"en":"If only I hadn't said that","es":"si tan solo no hubiera dicho eso","img":"u:photo-1494368308039-ed3393a402a4","v":"m","au":"79c91b1c23"},{"en":"regret","es":"arrepentirse / arrepentimiento","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"f","au":"02193a5705"},{"en":"missed opportunity","es":"oportunidad perdida","img":"u:photo-1615932702836-d8dc47e65225","v":"m","au":"cdd84c6cf6"},{"en":"wishful thinking","es":"ilusiones (pensar con el deseo)","img":"u:photo-1658279366796-e0c28623cd27","v":"f","au":"b50f3cffbd"},{"en":"make a wish","es":"pedir un deseo","img":"u:photo-1464349153735-7db50ed83c84","v":"m","au":"20515ecedb"},{"en":"in hindsight","es":"en retrospectiva","img":"u:photo-1528569937393-ee892b976859","v":"f","au":"2459eca873"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I wish I spoke Japanese; my trip to Tokyo would be much easier.","es":"Ojalá hablara japonés; mi viaje a Tokio sería mucho más fácil.","img":"u:photo-1573455494060-c5595004fb6c","v":"f","au":"38beeb99eb"},{"en":"I wish I had invested in that company ten years ago.","es":"Ojalá hubiera invertido en esa empresa hace diez años.","img":"u:photo-1590283603385-17ffb3a7f29f","v":"m","au":"3f364f5060"},{"en":"I wish my neighbors would turn down the music.","es":"Ojalá mis vecinos bajaran la música.","img":"u:photo-1688398159040-5aea0cd2a919","v":"f","au":"d5d4c0fe21"},{"en":"If only we had left earlier, we wouldn't have missed the flight.","es":"Si tan solo hubiéramos salido antes, no habríamos perdido el vuelo.","img":"u:photo-1746125047145-d6698eef563a","v":"m","au":"eaa8532fba"},{"en":"She wishes she lived closer to her family.","es":"Ella desearía vivir más cerca de su familia.","img":"u:photo-1638581925480-ebc84a2c3ab2","v":"f","au":"24e0cd1b1a"},{"en":"I wish I weren't so nervous before presentations.","es":"Ojalá no me pusiera tan nervioso antes de las presentaciones.","img":"u:photo-1553690300-93871c6a6654","v":"m","au":"b833fcb6a2"}],"fill":[{"s":"I wish I ___ more free time. (ahora)","a":"had","o":["have","would have"],"h":"presente → wish + past simple","full":"I wish I had more free time. (ahora)","au":"9b2f5cebd8"},{"s":"I wish I ___ harder for the exam last year.","a":"had studied","o":["studied","would study"],"h":"pasado → wish + past perfect","full":"I wish I had studied harder for the exam last year.","au":"93faa736aa"},{"s":"I wish you ___ stop interrupting me.","a":"would","o":["will","had"],"h":"queja → wish + would","full":"I wish you would stop interrupting me.","au":"8a73c4ed49"},{"s":"If only I ___ the answer! (ahora)","a":"knew","o":["know","had known"],"h":"presente → past simple","full":"If only I knew the answer! (ahora)","au":"2d231ce135"},{"s":"She wishes she ___ moved to Portland. (se arrepiente)","a":"hadn't","o":["didn't","wouldn't"],"h":"arrepentimiento → past perfect","full":"She wishes she hadn't moved to Portland. (se arrepiente)","au":"ab71f3a3a4"},{"s":"I wish it ___ stop raining.","a":"would","o":["will","is"],"h":"algo que quieres que cambie","full":"I wish it would stop raining.","au":"ca41722c64"},{"s":"I wish I ___ taller.","a":"were","o":["am","would be"],"h":"wish + were","full":"I wish I were taller.","au":"11df707506"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Regrets at the reunion","es":"Arrepentimientos en el reencuentro","img":"u:photo-1733341127795-bfc25edfb117","lines":[{"who":"Sarah","v":"f","t":"I can't believe it's been twenty years since high school!","au":"dad1b63a91"},{"who":"Tom","v":"m","t":"I know. Do you have any regrets?","au":"987d427b39"},{"who":"Sarah","v":"f","t":"A few. I wish I had studied abroad when I had the chance.","au":"18993a30a3"},{"who":"Tom","v":"m","t":"Me too. If only I had learned Spanish back then! I work with clients in Mexico now.","au":"5a8c4482ae"},{"who":"Sarah","v":"f","t":"It's never too late. I wish I had more free time, though.","au":"1b4c999edc"},{"who":"Tom","v":"m","t":"Same here. And I wish my boss would stop sending emails at midnight!","au":"a8664f6b3c"},{"who":"Sarah","v":"f","t":"Ha! Well, I'm glad we came tonight. I wish we did this more often.","au":"d5746e1208"},{"who":"Tom","v":"m","t":"Let's not wait another twenty years, then.","au":"932ac60bcf"}],"q":[{"q":"What does Sarah regret?","a":"Not studying abroad.","o":["Not learning Spanish.","Moving to Mexico."]},{"q":"Why does Tom wish he had learned Spanish?","a":"He works with clients in Mexico.","o":["He lives in Spain.","His boss speaks Spanish."]},{"q":"What does Tom wish his boss would do?","a":"Stop sending emails at midnight.","o":["Give him more vacation.","Learn Spanish."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To express wishes and regrets with wish, if only and would.","es":"Expresar deseos y arrepentimientos con wish, if only y would."},"warm":[{"q":"If you could change one thing about your daily routine, what would it be?","au":"397debf113","es":"Si pudieras cambiar una cosa de tu rutina diaria, ¿cuál sería?","ex":"I wish I didn't have to commute so far."},{"q":"Is there anything you wish you had done differently?","au":"50cc743d8b","es":"¿Hay algo que desearías haber hecho de otra manera?","ex":"I wish I had started learning English earlier."}],"reading":{"title":"Dear Advice Column","img":"u:photo-1658279366796-e0c28623cd27","text":"Dear Grace, I'm thirty-four and I have a good job in Phoenix, but I'm not happy. I wish I had followed my dream of becoming a chef. When I was twenty, I had the chance to study at a culinary school in New York, but I was too scared to move. If only I had been braver! Now I sit in an office all day and I wish I were in a kitchen instead. My husband says I complain too much. I wish he would understand how I feel. — Stuck in Phoenix.\n\nDear Stuck, regrets are normal, but you're only thirty-four! You talk as if your life were already over. Instead of wishing you had done things differently, ask what you can do now. Many community colleges offer evening cooking classes. Start small, cook for friends and see how it feels. One day you might wish you had started even sooner. — Grace","au":"0e6b235195","q":[{"s":"The writer works as a chef in Phoenix.","a":"no"},{"s":"She regrets not studying at a culinary school.","a":"yes"},{"s":"She wishes her husband would understand her.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Grace thinks it's too late for her to change.","a":"no"},{"s":"Grace suggests taking evening cooking classes.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What do you wish you could do better?","a":"I wish I could speak English more fluently.","es":"¿Qué desearías poder hacer mejor?","qau":"066b0a595b","aau":"8d4eafab3d"},{"q":"What do you wish you had done when you were younger?","a":"I wish I had traveled more.","es":"¿Qué desearías haber hecho cuando eras más joven?","qau":"9bfe47bd13","aau":"f133c85ae7"},{"q":"Is there anything you wish people would stop doing?","a":"I wish people would stop using their phones while driving.","es":"¿Hay algo que desearías que la gente dejara de hacer?","qau":"16ad6a719a","aau":"60fb3c6e12"},{"q":"What would you say: \"If only I …\"?","a":"If only I had more free time!","es":"¿Qué dirías: “Si tan solo yo …”?","qau":"efd580e6ea","aau":"4b6cf5527a"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe 5 deseos: 2 sobre el presente (wish + past), 2 arrepentimientos (wish + past perfect) y 1 queja (wish + would).","kw":["wish","had","would"],"n":5,"model":"I wish I lived closer to the beach. I wish I had more time for my family. I wish I had saved more money last year. I wish I hadn't sold my car. I wish my neighbor would stop parking in front of my house."}}]},{"n":11,"title":"Un/Countable Nouns","es":"Sustantivos contables e incontables","cover":"u:photo-1488459716781-31db52582fe9","parts":[{"id":"t11p1","topic":11,"part":1,"title":"How much? How many?","es":"¿Cuánto? ¿Cuántos?","acts":["learn","pantryScan","sort","fill","bubblePop","speak"],"tip":"<p>🔢 <b>Contables</b>: se pueden contar (<i>one egg, two eggs</i>) → <b>many</b>, <b>a few</b>, <b>How many …?</b><br>\n💧 <b>Incontables</b>: no tienen plural (<i>milk, rice, money, traffic</i>) → <b>much</b>, <b>a little</b>, <b>How much …?</b></p>\n<p>✅ <b>a lot of / lots of</b> sirven para los dos: <i>a lot of eggs</i>, <i>a lot of milk</i>.<br>\n👉 En oraciones afirmativas se prefiere <b>a lot of</b>; <b>much</b> suena formal en afirmativo y es normal en negativas y preguntas: <i>We don't have <b>much</b> time.</i></p>\n<p>🛒 <b>some</b> → afirmativas y <b>ofrecimientos/pedidos</b>: <i>Would you like <b>some</b> coffee?</i><br>\n❓ <b>any</b> → negativas y preguntas: <i>Is there <b>any</b> milk?</i> · <i>There isn't <b>any</b> bread.</i></p>\n<p>📦 Para “contar” incontables usa envases: <b>a carton of</b> milk · <b>a loaf of</b> bread · <b>a bottle of</b> oil · <b>a bag of</b> flour · <b>a can of</b> beans.</p>","tips":["<b>a lot of</b> se une: <i>ə-LÁ-rəv</i>. La <i>t</i> suena como una <i>r</i> suave.","<b>loaf</b> rima con <i>both</i> sin la th: <i>LÓUF</i>.","<b>carton</b> suena <i>KÁR-tən</i>, con la <i>t</i> casi tragada."],"vocab":[{"en":"How much milk is left?","es":"¿Cuánta leche queda?","img":"u:photo-1596151163116-98a5033814c2","v":"f","au":"beaa99da3f"},{"en":"How many eggs do we need?","es":"¿Cuántos huevos necesitamos?","img":"u:photo-1547654387-6182475cfe3e","v":"m","au":"4f6bdf3071"},{"en":"a lot of / lots of","es":"mucho / muchos","img":"u:photo-1488459716781-31db52582fe9","v":"f","au":"c43862efd5"},{"en":"some bread","es":"algo de pan","img":"u:photo-1586765501019-cbe3973ef8fa","v":"m","au":"deaab69c83"},{"en":"any rice","es":"algo de / nada de arroz","img":"u:photo-1536304993881-ff6e9eefa2a6","v":"f","au":"a9ed1c10b3"},{"en":"a carton of milk","es":"un cartón de leche","img":"u:photo-1553301803-768cd4a59b9c","v":"m","au":"222b453f36"},{"en":"a loaf of bread","es":"una barra de pan","img":"u:photo-1549931319-a545dcf3bc73","v":"f","au":"dcabd8de83"},{"en":"a bottle of olive oil","es":"una botella de aceite de oliva","img":"u:photo-1638324396229-632af05042dd","v":"m","au":"9764ad5593"},{"en":"a bag of flour","es":"una bolsa de harina","img":"u:photo-1761222191837-4448599c09fc","v":"f","au":"a27d121b2d"},{"en":"a can of beans","es":"una lata de frijoles","img":"u:photo-1738618140037-09e11c8e644a","v":"m","au":"44341b1e66"},{"en":"grocery list","es":"lista del mercado","img":"u:photo-1623265300459-dfc7609a0a55","v":"f","au":"7d5ad3ee23"},{"en":"run out of","es":"quedarse sin","img":"u:photo-1646592491578-01b3053d9053","v":"m","au":"f7a7b9a656"}],"sentences":[{"en":"How much money do we have left for groceries?","es":"¿Cuánto dinero nos queda para el mercado?","img":"u:photo-1556742031-c6961e8560b0","v":"f","au":"c6321f4388"},{"en":"We don't have many eggs, so let's buy a dozen.","es":"No tenemos muchos huevos, así que compremos una docena.","img":"u:photo-1547654387-6182475cfe3e","v":"m","au":"c9c1f970cc"},{"en":"Is there any milk in the fridge?","es":"¿Hay leche en la nevera?","img":"u:photo-1646592491578-01b3053d9053","v":"f","au":"a4183cb4c4"},{"en":"Could you grab a loaf of bread and some cheese?","es":"¿Puedes traer una barra de pan y algo de queso?","img":"u:photo-1586765501019-cbe3973ef8fa","v":"m","au":"50f7579c39"},{"en":"We've run out of coffee, so add it to the grocery list.","es":"Se nos acabó el café; agrégalo a la lista del mercado.","img":"u:photo-1623265300459-dfc7609a0a55","v":"f","au":"2afb96fac6"},{"en":"There's a lot of traffic, so it'll take a while.","es":"Hay mucho tráfico, así que va a demorar un rato.","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"b75b6d88f2"}],"fill":[{"s":"How ___ water do you drink a day?","a":"much","o":["many","lot"],"h":"water es incontable","full":"How much water do you drink a day?","au":"ff2bec84c9"},{"s":"How ___ people are coming to dinner?","a":"many","o":["much","lot"],"h":"people es contable (plural)","full":"How many people are coming to dinner?","au":"4d955f3c7b"},{"s":"There isn't ___ cheese left.","a":"any","o":["some","many"],"h":"negativo → any","full":"There isn't any cheese left.","au":"7097d5638c"},{"s":"Would you like ___ coffee?","a":"some","o":["any","many"],"h":"ofrecimiento → some","full":"Would you like some coffee?","au":"de140ea1e1"},{"s":"We have a ___ of work this week.","a":"lot","o":["lots","many"],"h":"a lot of","full":"We have a lot of work this week.","au":"481195aa41"},{"s":"I need a ___ of flour for the cake.","a":"bag","o":["piece","slice"],"h":"envase: a bag of","full":"I need a bag of flour for the cake.","au":"9b0f723d1f"},{"s":"We don't have ___ time. Hurry up!","a":"much","o":["many","lot"],"h":"negativo + incontable","full":"We don't have much time. Hurry up!","au":"36c2263991"}],"sort":{"cats":["🔢 countable","💧 uncountable"],"items":[{"w":"egg","c":"🔢 countable","au":"3bd256bb85"},{"w":"apple","c":"🔢 countable","au":"e9727b352f"},{"w":"bottle","c":"🔢 countable","au":"0132a43738"},{"w":"coin","c":"🔢 countable","au":"2c5701e51a"},{"w":"chair","c":"🔢 countable","au":"8ca63af9df"},{"w":"suggestion","c":"🔢 countable","au":"c8c997c4c6"},{"w":"money","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"5b264d7b0f"},{"w":"water","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"071af6ab0f"},{"w":"rice","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"b3bddee348"},{"w":"traffic","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"e39492925c"},{"w":"furniture","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"bd8bf51112"},{"w":"advice","c":"💧 uncountable","au":"9369ed5d2f"}]},"goal":{"en":"To talk about quantities with much, many, some, any, a lot of and containers.","es":"Hablar de cantidades con much, many, some, any, a lot of y envases."},"warm":[{"q":"How often do you go grocery shopping?","au":"9ae7661955","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia vas al supermercado?","ex":"I go once a week, usually on Saturdays."},{"q":"What do you always have in your fridge?","au":"f7b6826d7b","es":"¿Qué tienes siempre en tu nevera?","ex":"I always have some milk, a lot of fruit and a few eggs."}],"reading":{"title":"The Sunday grocery run","img":"u:photo-1623265300459-dfc7609a0a55","text":"Every Sunday, Carlos and his wife Megan check the kitchen before going to the supermarket in San Antonio. This week they found that they had run out of coffee, which is an emergency in their house. There wasn't much milk left either, only half a carton. \"How many eggs do we have?\" Megan asked. \"Not many. Maybe three,\" Carlos answered. They needed a lot of things for the week: a bag of rice, two cans of black beans, a bottle of olive oil and some fresh vegetables. They didn't need any bread because Megan's mother had baked a loaf on Saturday. At the store, Carlos wanted to buy lots of snacks, but Megan reminded him that they didn't have much money left in the budget. In the end, they spent ninety dollars and stuck to the list, except for one chocolate bar. \"How much did that cost?\" Megan asked. \"Not much,\" Carlos smiled.","au":"1841a0d3ba","q":[{"s":"Carlos and Megan had a lot of coffee at home.","a":"no"},{"s":"They had only a few eggs.","a":"yes"},{"s":"They needed to buy bread.","a":"no"},{"s":"They didn't have much money left in the budget.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Carlos bought one item that wasn't on the list.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"How much water do you drink a day?","a":"I drink about two liters a day.","es":"¿Cuánta agua tomas al día?","qau":"ff2bec84c9","aau":"e892a01086"},{"q":"How many people live in your house?","a":"Four people live in my house.","es":"¿Cuántas personas viven en tu casa?","qau":"422d6a3ba1","aau":"809bcb31c7"},{"q":"Is there any food you never buy?","a":"I never buy any soda.","es":"¿Hay alguna comida que nunca compres?","qau":"56ee16c2b4","aau":"ee06f69e41"},{"q":"What do you usually buy a lot of?","a":"I usually buy a lot of fruit and vegetables.","es":"¿De qué compras mucho normalmente?","qau":"1f21b6c04d","aau":"935424a593"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe tu lista del mercado y describe qué tienes y qué no en tu cocina con much, many, some, any, a lot of y envases (a bag of, a can of…).","kw":["much","many","some","any"],"n":5,"model":"I need a carton of milk and a loaf of bread. There isn't any coffee left. We don't have many eggs. There's a lot of rice in the cupboard. I want to buy some apples and a bottle of olive oil."}},{"id":"t11p2","topic":11,"part":2,"title":"A piece of advice","es":"Un consejo","acts":["learn","conciergeDesk","dialogue","fill","oddOneOut","speak"],"tip":"<p>⚠️ Algunas palabras son <b>contables en español</b> pero <b>incontables en inglés</b>. ¡Nunca llevan <i>a/an</i> ni <i>-s</i>!</p>\n<p>🧳 <b>advice</b> (consejo) · <b>information</b> · <b>furniture</b> (muebles) · <b>luggage / baggage</b> · <b>equipment</b> · <b>homework</b> · <b>news</b> · <b>research</b> · <b>feedback</b></p>\n<p>✅ Para contarlas: <b>a piece of</b> → <i>a piece of advice</i>, <i>two pieces of furniture</i>, <i>a piece of news</i>.<br>\n❌ <s>an advice</s>, <s>informations</s>, <s>furnitures</s></p>\n<p>📰 <b>news</b> termina en -s pero es <b>singular</b>: <i>The news <b>is</b> good.</i></p>\n<p>🔄 Palabras que <b>cambian de significado</b>:<br>\n☕ <i>coffee</i> (el café) / <i>a coffee</i> (una taza) · 📄 <i>paper</i> (papel) / <i>a paper</i> (un periódico o un ensayo)<br>\n🥛 <i>glass</i> (vidrio) / <i>a glass</i> (un vaso) · 🛏️ <i>room</i> (espacio) / <i>a room</i> (una habitación)<br>\n💼 <i>experience</i> (experiencia laboral) / <i>an experience</i> (una vivencia)</p>","tips":["<b>advice</b> (sustantivo) termina en sonido <i>s</i>: <i>əd-VÁIS</i>; <b>advise</b> (verbo) en <i>z</i>.","<b>furniture</b> suena <i>FÉR-ni-chər</i>.","<b>luggage</b> y <b>baggage</b> son sinónimos; en el aeropuerto escucharás <i>baggage claim</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"a piece of advice","es":"un consejo","img":"u:photo-1573497620053-ea5300f94f21","v":"f","au":"0573d0e281"},{"en":"some information","es":"(algo de) información","img":"u:photo-1763577485341-b30e30279dc7","v":"m","au":"b952ec74df"},{"en":"furniture","es":"muebles","img":"u:photo-1693578616322-c8abe6c7393d","v":"f","au":"bd8bf51112"},{"en":"luggage","es":"equipaje","img":"u:photo-1648737967037-96967e9151b5","v":"m","au":"ca59e99ad3"},{"en":"The news is good.","es":"Las noticias son buenas.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"62eb23ba9d"},{"en":"equipment","es":"equipo (aparatos)","img":"u:photo-1486257293255-8810a92c541f","v":"m","au":"8a8c24e6d0"},{"en":"a coffee / coffee","es":"un café / el café","img":"u:photo-1619860703338-9c70a1af6a63","v":"f","au":"fabc8d6f7b"},{"en":"a paper / paper","es":"un periódico, un ensayo / papel","img":"u:photo-1495020689067-958852a7765e","v":"m","au":"6f1d4302fe"},{"en":"a glass / glass","es":"un vaso / vidrio","img":"u:photo-1534616042650-80f5c9b61f09","v":"f","au":"cddbb2447e"},{"en":"a room / room","es":"una habitación / espacio","img":"u:photo-1618773928121-c32242e63f39","v":"m","au":"c4de486d54"},{"en":"an experience / experience","es":"una vivencia / experiencia laboral","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"f","au":"60c72d093b"},{"en":"homework","es":"tarea (incontable)","img":"u:photo-1522202176988-66273c2fd55f","v":"m","au":"b29cb0e80f"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Let me give you a piece of advice: always read the contract.","es":"Déjame darte un consejo: siempre lee el contrato.","img":"u:photo-1573497620053-ea5300f94f21","v":"f","au":"05d3d6ea67"},{"en":"The news is good: we got the contract!","es":"Las noticias son buenas: ¡conseguimos el contrato!","img":"u:photo-1549923746-c502d488b3ea","v":"m","au":"4507bf033a"},{"en":"Can I have two coffees and a muffin, please?","es":"¿Me da dos cafés y un muffin, por favor?","img":"u:photo-1619860703338-9c70a1af6a63","v":"f","au":"14a1e55e86"},{"en":"We need some new furniture for the office.","es":"Necesitamos muebles nuevos para la oficina.","img":"u:photo-1631193816258-28b44b21e78b","v":"m","au":"01038d2043"},{"en":"How much luggage are you checking?","es":"¿Cuánto equipaje va a documentar?","img":"u:photo-1760581176635-2cea8ae93b5f","v":"f","au":"5fcb852e06"},{"en":"She has a lot of experience in marketing.","es":"Ella tiene mucha experiencia en marketing.","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"m","au":"9a13f354c3"}],"fill":[{"s":"Can you give me some ___ about the hotel?","a":"information","o":["informations","an information"],"h":"information es incontable","full":"Can you give me some information about the hotel?","au":"01ba1eb971"},{"s":"That's a great piece of ___.","a":"advice","o":["advices","an advice"],"h":"a piece of advice","full":"That's a great piece of advice.","au":"0ff8282108"},{"s":"The news ___ really surprising.","a":"was","o":["were","are"],"h":"news es singular","full":"The news was really surprising.","au":"9e7fb265fb"},{"s":"We bought new ___ for the living room.","a":"furniture","o":["furnitures","a furniture"],"h":"furniture es incontable","full":"We bought new furniture for the living room.","au":"12c5b7760d"},{"s":"I'll have ___ coffee, please. Black, no sugar.","a":"a","o":["an","many"],"h":"pedir una taza → a coffee","full":"I'll have a coffee, please. Black, no sugar.","au":"55682acd03"},{"s":"There isn't enough ___ for a sofa here.","a":"room","o":["rooms","a room"],"h":"room = espacio (incontable)","full":"There isn't enough room for a sofa here.","au":"bf7c86c761"},{"s":"He has a lot of ___ in sales.","a":"experience","o":["experiences","an experience"],"h":"experiencia laboral (incontable)","full":"He has a lot of experience in sales.","au":"d22f9026eb"}],"dialogue":{"title":"At the hotel front desk","es":"En la recepción del hotel","img":"u:photo-1759038085950-1234ca8f5fed","lines":[{"who":"Receptionist","v":"f","t":"Good evening and welcome to the Bayview Hotel in San Diego. How can I help you?","au":"0c7ab7cdfe"},{"who":"Mr. Ruiz","v":"m","t":"Hi, I have a reservation under Ruiz. And I have quite a lot of luggage, I'm afraid.","au":"5d35a518ca"},{"who":"Receptionist","v":"f","t":"No problem. A bellhop will take your bags to your room.","au":"a95d13ee18"},{"who":"Mr. Ruiz","v":"m","t":"Great. Could you also give me some information about restaurants nearby?","au":"a0341ff2dc"},{"who":"Receptionist","v":"f","t":"Of course. Here's a map. A piece of advice: try the fish tacos at the harbor.","au":"8465855386"},{"who":"Mr. Ruiz","v":"m","t":"Thanks! Is there enough room in the safe for a laptop?","au":"36b17e05e0"},{"who":"Receptionist","v":"f","t":"Yes, there's plenty of room. And breakfast is served until ten.","au":"37c5084b32"},{"who":"Mr. Ruiz","v":"m","t":"Perfect. I'll definitely need a coffee before my meeting tomorrow!","au":"9314f8b320"}],"q":[{"q":"What does Mr. Ruiz have a lot of?","a":"Luggage.","o":["Furniture.","Homework."]},{"q":"What advice does the receptionist give?","a":"Try the fish tacos at the harbor.","o":["Take a taxi.","Eat breakfast early."]},{"q":"What will Mr. Ruiz need before his meeting?","a":"A coffee.","o":["Some paper.","A new room."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To use tricky uncountable nouns and nouns that change meaning correctly.","es":"Usar correctamente incontables difíciles y sustantivos que cambian de significado."},"warm":[{"q":"What is the best piece of advice you've ever received?","au":"e57898d6a6","es":"¿Cuál es el mejor consejo que has recibido?","ex":"The best piece of advice I've received is 'never stop learning'."},{"q":"Where do you usually get your news?","au":"4b91f026eb","es":"¿Dónde sueles informarte de las noticias?","ex":"I usually read the news on my phone."}],"reading":{"title":"Moving to Portland","img":"u:photo-1766040923580-16ad32fae8b4","text":"When Isabel accepted a job at a design studio in Portland, she asked her friends for advice. Her friend Jake gave her a great piece of advice: \"Don't move your furniture. It's cheaper to buy new stuff there.\" So she sold almost everything and took only two suitcases. Still, the airline said she had too much luggage and charged her sixty dollars. The first week was chaotic. Her apartment had a lot of light but not much room, and she couldn't find any information about recycling rules. Then came the good news: her new company offered to pay for some equipment for her home office. Isabel has a lot of experience in graphic design, but working in English was a new experience for her. \"My homework every night is learning new vocabulary,\" she says. On weekends she reads a paper at a café and orders a coffee with a croissant. \"The news isn't always good,\" she says, \"but the coffee is excellent.\"","au":"8dad8f616c","q":[{"s":"Jake advised Isabel to move all her furniture.","a":"no"},{"s":"The airline said she had too much luggage.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her apartment had a lot of room.","a":"no"},{"s":"Her company offered to pay for some equipment.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Working in English was a new experience for Isabel.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Can you give me a piece of advice about learning English?","a":"Sure. Listen to podcasts every day.","es":"¿Me puedes dar un consejo para aprender inglés?","qau":"0a95368a82","aau":"8acaca6d37"},{"q":"How much luggage do you usually take on a trip?","a":"I usually take just one suitcase and a backpack.","es":"¿Cuánto equipaje llevas normalmente en un viaje?","qau":"2696d47d28","aau":"75f40abda8"},{"q":"Is there enough room in your house for guests?","a":"Yes, we have a spare room.","es":"¿Hay suficiente espacio en tu casa para invitados?","qau":"7013a9120e","aau":"7adf75639c"},{"q":"How much experience do you have in your job?","a":"I have about ten years of experience.","es":"¿Cuánta experiencia tienes en tu trabajo?","qau":"3fec05dada","aau":"2ee8a49021"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un mensaje a un amigo que se va a mudar. Usa advice, information, furniture, luggage, news y una palabra que cambie de significado (a coffee, room, a paper…).","kw":["advice","information","furniture","luggage"],"n":5,"model":"Here's a piece of advice: don't take much luggage. You can buy new furniture there. I found some useful information about apartments. The news about your new job is great! Let's have a coffee before you leave."}}]},{"n":12,"title":"A Few / Few / Little / A Little","es":"A few, few, little, a little","cover":"u:photo-1534616042650-80f5c9b61f09","parts":[{"id":"t12p1","topic":12,"part":1,"title":"Optimist or pessimist?","es":"¿Optimista o pesimista?","acts":["learn","halfFull","sort","fill","quizShow","speak"],"tip":"<p>😃 Con <b>a</b> = sentido <b>positivo</b> (es poco, ¡pero alcanza!):<br>\n<b>a few</b> + contable plural → <i>I have <b>a few</b> friends in Seattle.</i> (unos cuantos 👍)<br>\n<b>a little</b> + incontable → <i>We have <b>a little</b> time. Let's get coffee.</i> (un poco 👍)</p>\n<p>😟 Sin <b>a</b> = sentido <b>negativo</b> (casi nada, no alcanza):<br>\n<b>few</b> + contable → <i><b>Few</b> people came.</i> (casi nadie 👎)<br>\n<b>little</b> + incontable → <i>There's <b>little</b> hope.</i> (casi ninguna 👎)</p>\n<p>📈 <b>quite a few</b> = bastantes (¡un número grande!) · <b>only a few</b> = solo unos pocos · <b>very few / very little</b> = muy pocos / muy poco.</p>\n<p>💡 En conversación, <i>few</i> y <i>little</i> solos suenan formales; es común decir <b>not many / not much</b>.</p>","tips":["<b>a few</b> se dice como una palabra: <i>ə-FIÚ</i>.","<b>little</b> en EE. UU. suena <i>LÍ-rəl</i>: la <i>tt</i> es una <i>r</i> suave.","<b>quite</b> (bastante) suena <i>kuáit</i>; no lo confundas con <b>quiet</b> (<i>kuáiət</i>, silencioso)."],"vocab":[{"en":"a few friends","es":"unos cuantos amigos","img":"u:photo-1511988617509-a57c8a288659","v":"f","au":"ccbadfb5a0"},{"en":"few people","es":"poca gente (casi nadie)","img":"u:photo-1574966739987-65e38db0f7ce","v":"m","au":"0afd078bd3"},{"en":"a little money","es":"un poco de dinero","img":"u:photo-1574607383476-f517f260d30b","v":"f","au":"4887298264"},{"en":"little time","es":"poco tiempo (casi nada)","img":"u:photo-1643288298077-f1d624de82ed","v":"m","au":"28ec69e0ee"},{"en":"quite a few","es":"bastantes","img":"u:photo-1501386761578-eac5c94b800a","v":"f","au":"ac5750aefa"},{"en":"very little","es":"muy poco","img":"u:photo-1765211003392-7eeb5250d988","v":"m","au":"ad036d0498"},{"en":"only a few","es":"solo unos pocos","img":"u:photo-1641447093043-241f064568fb","v":"f","au":"edf2c55e59"},{"en":"a little bit","es":"un poquito","img":"u:photo-1673791031093-eb8eefa60083","v":"m","au":"0bbc743472"},{"en":"spare time","es":"tiempo libre","img":"u:photo-1519095614420-850b5671ac7f","v":"f","au":"39854940fb"},{"en":"savings","es":"ahorros","img":"u:photo-1768839721719-c5ed97c1fd58","v":"m","au":"4743548781"},{"en":"half full","es":"medio lleno","img":"u:photo-1534616042650-80f5c9b61f09","v":"f","au":"a4d5748cac"},{"en":"half empty","es":"medio vacío","img":"u:photo-1506372023823-741c83b836fe","v":"m","au":"a1968f9def"}],"sentences":[{"en":"I have a few friends in Seattle, so I won't feel lonely.","es":"Tengo unos cuantos amigos en Seattle, así que no me sentiré solo.","img":"u:photo-1583606784123-7c244f00d29c","v":"f","au":"173930732f"},{"en":"Few people know that Alaska has more coastline than all the other states combined.","es":"Poca gente sabe que Alaska tiene más costa que todos los demás estados juntos.","img":"u:photo-1673114819432-1aa36952dd3e","v":"m","au":"6345be873f"},{"en":"There's a little coffee left. Do you want some?","es":"Queda un poco de café. ¿Quieres?","img":"u:photo-1506372023823-741c83b836fe","v":"f","au":"cfbe25f70f"},{"en":"We have very little time before the meeting starts.","es":"Tenemos muy poco tiempo antes de que empiece la reunión.","img":"u:photo-1643288298077-f1d624de82ed","v":"m","au":"3c6d58c309"},{"en":"Quite a few employees work from home on Fridays.","es":"Bastantes empleados trabajan desde casa los viernes.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"3394ec5b10"},{"en":"He has little patience with people who are always late.","es":"Él tiene poca paciencia con la gente que siempre llega tarde.","img":"u:photo-1495704907664-81f74a7efd9b","v":"m","au":"3cb9808a1b"}],"fill":[{"s":"Don't worry, we still have ___ time. Let's get a coffee.","a":"a little","o":["little","a few"],"h":"positivo + incontable","full":"Don't worry, we still have a little time. Let's get a coffee.","au":"976296e314"},{"s":"___ people came to the meeting, so we canceled it.","a":"Few","o":["A few","Little"],"h":"negativo + contable","full":"Few people came to the meeting, so we canceled it.","au":"62054fdb74"},{"s":"I know ___ words in Italian, enough to order food.","a":"a few","o":["few","a little"],"h":"positivo + contable","full":"I know a few words in Italian, enough to order food.","au":"a1ced86667"},{"s":"There's ___ hope that the store will reopen. It's closed for good.","a":"little","o":["a little","a few"],"h":"negativo + incontable","full":"There's little hope that the store will reopen. It's closed for good.","au":"8731075043"},{"s":"___ of my coworkers are from Mexico. Maybe six or seven.","a":"Quite a few","o":["Very little","Little"],"h":"quite a few = bastantes","full":"Quite a few of my coworkers are from Mexico. Maybe six or seven.","au":"3e0bc95c4f"},{"s":"I need ___ help with this report. Do you have a minute?","a":"a little","o":["a few","few"],"h":"un poco (incontable)","full":"I need a little help with this report. Do you have a minute?","au":"b5d342cb72"}],"sort":{"cats":["😃 positive","😟 negative"],"items":[{"w":"a few friends","c":"😃 positive","au":"ccbadfb5a0"},{"w":"a little money","c":"😃 positive","au":"4887298264"},{"w":"quite a few options","c":"😃 positive","au":"6ef2d6037e"},{"w":"a little time to relax","c":"😃 positive","au":"447779b44d"},{"w":"a few good ideas","c":"😃 positive","au":"fb46a934db"},{"w":"few friends","c":"😟 negative","au":"5626b0a01f"},{"w":"little money","c":"😟 negative","au":"6ace9d0187"},{"w":"very little hope","c":"😟 negative","au":"35dea327ad"},{"w":"very few options","c":"😟 negative","au":"c1e03644d8"},{"w":"little interest","c":"😟 negative","au":"16ef817dec"}]},"goal":{"en":"To show a positive or negative attitude with a few, few, a little and little.","es":"Mostrar una actitud positiva o negativa con a few, few, a little y little."},"warm":[{"q":"Do you have a few close friends or a lot of friends?","au":"021a25ebb8","es":"¿Tienes unos pocos amigos cercanos o muchos amigos?","ex":"I have a few close friends, and that's enough for me."},{"q":"Do you have a little free time today?","au":"360557ea1c","es":"¿Tienes un poco de tiempo libre hoy?","ex":"Yes, I have a little time after lunch."}],"reading":{"title":"Two roommates, two attitudes","img":"u:photo-1534616042650-80f5c9b61f09","text":"Jessica and Paula share an apartment in Boston, but they see the world very differently. Last month they both lost their jobs on the same day. Jessica said, \"We have a little money in savings, so we can relax for a few weeks and look for something better.\" Paula disagreed. \"We have very little money and few options. Few companies are hiring right now.\" Jessica just smiled. \"I know a few people at a marketing agency. I'll call them.\" Paula sent quite a few applications but received few answers, and she had little patience with the slow process. Jessica, on the other hand, made a few calls, went to a couple of interviews and got an offer in three weeks. Paula found a job a little later, and it was actually a better one. Now, when Jessica says the glass is half full, Paula answers, \"Maybe. But there's still a little water left for me.\"","au":"9132792b29","q":[{"s":"Jessica and Paula live in Boston.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Jessica thought they had a little money to relax for a while.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Paula thought they had a lot of options.","a":"no"},{"s":"Paula received many answers to her applications.","a":"no"},{"s":"Paula eventually got a better job than Jessica.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you have a few minutes to talk?","a":"Sure, I have a few minutes.","es":"¿Tienes unos minutos para hablar?","qau":"8027495007","aau":"b0824751e0"},{"q":"How much free time do you have during the week?","a":"Very little. I work from Monday to Saturday.","es":"¿Cuánto tiempo libre tienes durante la semana?","qau":"e6313d621d","aau":"af968c3a23"},{"q":"Do many people in your family speak English?","a":"Few people do. Only my sister and me.","es":"¿Muchas personas de tu familia hablan inglés?","qau":"153a8a367f","aau":"eacdba6457"},{"q":"Do you know quite a few words in English now?","a":"Yes, I know quite a few words now.","es":"¿Ya sabes bastantes palabras en inglés?","qau":"93ff737a1a","aau":"0c6305aeaa"}],"hw":{"es":"Describe tu semana dos veces: primero como optimista (a few, a little) y luego como pesimista (few, little).","kw":["a few","a little","few","little"],"n":6,"model":"I have a few friends at work, and I have a little time to rest on Sunday. I saved a little money this month. I have few friends at work, and I have little time to rest. I saved very little money this month."}},{"id":"t12p2","topic":12,"part":2,"title":"Fewer, less & plenty of","es":"Menos, menos y de sobra","acts":["learn","chartTalk","dialogue","fill","spinWheel","speak"],"tip":"<p>➖ <b>fewer</b> + contable plural (<i>fewer cars, fewer people</i>) · <b>less</b> + incontable (<i>less traffic, less money</i>).<br>\n💬 En conversación muchos nativos dicen <i>less people</i>, pero en exámenes y escritura usa <b>fewer</b>.</p>\n<p>👍 <b>plenty of</b> = más que suficiente (contable o incontable): <i>We have <b>plenty of</b> time.</i></p>\n<p>🙈 <b>hardly any</b> = casi nada / casi ninguno: <i>There's <b>hardly any</b> milk left.</i> · <i><b>Hardly any</b> customers complained.</i></p>\n<p>📊 Para informes y datos:<br>\n<b>a large number of</b> + contable (<i>a large number of users</i>) · <b>a great deal of</b> + incontable (<i>a great deal of money</i>)<br>\n<b>the majority of</b> = la mayoría · <b>a handful of</b> = un puñado (muy pocos).</p>","tips":["<b>fewer</b> suena <i>FIÚ-ər</i> y <b>less</b> suena <i>LES</i> con <i>e</i> abierta.","<b>hardly</b> no significa “duro”: significa <i>casi no</i>. Se pronuncia <i>JÁRD-li</i>.","<b>survey</b> como sustantivo se acentúa al inicio: <i>SÉR-vei</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"fewer cars","es":"menos autos","img":"u:photo-1589123592035-32858c974713","v":"f","au":"8638faf0a1"},{"en":"less pollution","es":"menos contaminación","img":"u:photo-1686179225818-c07909cd2911","v":"m","au":"3fa76fad46"},{"en":"plenty of options","es":"muchas opciones (de sobra)","img":"u:photo-1488459716781-31db52582fe9","v":"f","au":"35624d88ac"},{"en":"hardly any","es":"casi nada / casi ninguno","img":"u:photo-1789353527986-8ed7c7e75dc8","v":"m","au":"2355df3ab6"},{"en":"a great deal of","es":"una gran cantidad de","img":"u:photo-1766040923580-16ad32fae8b4","v":"f","au":"18cb6e7278"},{"en":"a large number of","es":"un gran número de","img":"u:photo-1573358695783-005699a7fc94","v":"m","au":"241fa4e87b"},{"en":"the majority of","es":"la mayoría de","img":"u:photo-1626287935075-3275d2d9025e","v":"f","au":"7ad30a5ea0"},{"en":"a handful of","es":"un puñado de","img":"u:photo-1574607383476-f517f260d30b","v":"m","au":"96ec0c6df7"},{"en":"survey","es":"encuesta","img":"u:photo-1758599668338-4c55a3bd0ce0","v":"f","au":"8c8c958613"},{"en":"percentage","es":"porcentaje","img":"u:photo-1669399213378-2853e748f217","v":"m","au":"7b72fbba1e"},{"en":"remote workers","es":"trabajadores remotos","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"0d4c75b623"},{"en":"commute","es":"trayecto al trabajo","img":"u:photo-1461088945293-0c17689e48ac","v":"m","au":"f45ad0c01d"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Fewer people commute by car now that remote work is popular.","es":"Menos personas van al trabajo en carro ahora que el trabajo remoto es popular.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"f","au":"fc518f5dcf"},{"en":"We should use less plastic and more reusable bags.","es":"Deberíamos usar menos plástico y más bolsas reutilizables.","img":"u:photo-1574365569389-a10d488ca3fb","v":"m","au":"ec07baadb5"},{"en":"Don't rush. We have plenty of time before the flight.","es":"No te apures. Tenemos tiempo de sobra antes del vuelo.","img":"u:photo-1553619948-505cc1cdc320","v":"f","au":"c6846ce856"},{"en":"Hardly any customers complained about the new prices.","es":"Casi ningún cliente se quejó de los nuevos precios.","img":"u:photo-1556742031-c6961e8560b0","v":"m","au":"7ca1efbe77"},{"en":"A large number of employees answered the survey.","es":"Un gran número de empleados respondió la encuesta.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"b3ee794bb1"},{"en":"There's a great deal of interest in the new product.","es":"Hay muchísimo interés en el nuevo producto.","img":"u:photo-1505373877841-8d25f7d46678","v":"m","au":"af3dc4c40d"}],"fill":[{"s":"There are ___ cars downtown on Sundays.","a":"fewer","o":["less","little"],"h":"fewer + contable plural","full":"There are fewer cars downtown on Sundays.","au":"c7dfaf6306"},{"s":"I drink ___ coffee than I used to.","a":"less","o":["fewer","few"],"h":"less + incontable","full":"I drink less coffee than I used to.","au":"0281dded9a"},{"s":"We have ___ of chairs. You don't need to bring more.","a":"plenty","o":["lots","many"],"h":"plenty of","full":"We have plenty of chairs. You don't need to bring more.","au":"fca488f965"},{"s":"There's hardly ___ milk left.","a":"any","o":["some","none"],"h":"hardly any","full":"There's hardly any milk left.","au":"d38a727ce3"},{"s":"A large ___ of students passed the exam.","a":"number","o":["amount","deal"],"h":"a large number of + contable","full":"A large number of students passed the exam.","au":"9d8695a7eb"},{"s":"They spent a great ___ of money on the project.","a":"deal","o":["number","many"],"h":"a great deal of + incontable","full":"They spent a great deal of money on the project.","au":"03cf12064b"},{"s":"___ people took the bus this year than last year.","a":"Fewer","o":["Less","Little"],"h":"fewer + personas","full":"Fewer people took the bus this year than last year.","au":"edc07ac472"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Reading the survey results","es":"Leyendo los resultados de la encuesta","img":"u:photo-1669399213378-2853e748f217","lines":[{"who":"Karen","v":"f","t":"So, what did the employee survey show?","au":"7b427f58e1"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Some interesting things. The majority of people prefer a hybrid schedule.","au":"1e7f0ef862"},{"who":"Karen","v":"f","t":"Really? How many want to come to the office every day?","au":"5d217623a6"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Hardly any. Just a handful of people in sales.","au":"d70744a6bf"},{"who":"Karen","v":"f","t":"Interesting. And what about the parking problem?","au":"21288440d7"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Well, there are fewer cars in the lot now, so there's less stress in the mornings.","au":"2f0e2f241c"},{"who":"Karen","v":"f","t":"That's good news. Did anyone complain about the new coffee machine?","au":"acd997a0a0"},{"who":"Luis","v":"m","t":"Quite a few people, actually. They say it makes very little coffee!","au":"6f2e9bab3f"}],"q":[{"q":"What does the majority of employees prefer?","a":"A hybrid schedule.","o":["Working at the office every day.","Working only from home."]},{"q":"How many people want to come to the office every day?","a":"Hardly any.","o":["Quite a few.","The majority."]},{"q":"What did quite a few people complain about?","a":"The coffee machine.","o":["The parking lot.","The survey."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To describe data and quantities with fewer, less, plenty of, hardly any and a large number of.","es":"Describir datos y cantidades con fewer, less, plenty of, hardly any y a large number of."},"warm":[{"q":"Do people in your city drive less than before?","au":"b8514e9292","es":"¿La gente de tu ciudad maneja menos que antes?","ex":"Yes, fewer people drive because of the traffic."},{"q":"Do you have plenty of time to study English?","au":"9c5aa73145","es":"¿Tienes tiempo de sobra para estudiar inglés?","ex":"Not really. I have hardly any time during the week."}],"reading":{"title":"How we commute now","img":"u:photo-1461088945293-0c17689e48ac","text":"A recent survey of five thousand office workers in Denver shows how much the way we commute has changed. The majority of employees now work from home at least two days a week. As a result, there are fewer cars on the highways during rush hour and less pollution downtown. A large number of workers said they spend less money on gas and lunch. On the other hand, hardly any of them want to give up the office completely. Only a handful of people said they would prefer to work from home every day. Many workers said that there is plenty of time to finish tasks at home, but very little chance to meet colleagues informally. Companies are reacting. Several have spent a great deal of money redesigning offices with fewer desks and more meeting spaces. The conclusion? \"People don't hate the office,\" says the report. \"They just want less commuting and more flexibility.\"","au":"fad105037c","q":[{"s":"The majority of workers now work from home at least two days a week.","a":"yes"},{"s":"There are more cars on the highways during rush hour.","a":"no"},{"s":"A large number of workers spend less money on gas.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Many people want to work from home every day.","a":"no"},{"s":"Some companies are redesigning offices with fewer desks.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"Do you spend less time commuting than before?","a":"Yes, I spend much less time commuting now.","es":"¿Pasas menos tiempo en el trayecto al trabajo que antes?","qau":"1da757eb9a","aau":"9a80752ed7"},{"q":"Are there fewer people at your office on Fridays?","a":"Yes, there are far fewer people on Fridays.","es":"¿Hay menos gente en tu oficina los viernes?","qau":"cdaf3f6bf6","aau":"d7b128e7e3"},{"q":"Do you have plenty of time to relax on weekends?","a":"Not really. I have hardly any free time.","es":"¿Tienes tiempo de sobra para descansar los fines de semana?","qau":"e53658a34c","aau":"27a230dd7b"},{"q":"What do the majority of people in your city do on Sundays?","a":"The majority of people go to the park or visit family.","es":"¿Qué hace la mayoría de la gente de tu ciudad los domingos?","qau":"d8c69c94f5","aau":"2791c02181"}],"hw":{"es":"Inventa los resultados de una encuesta en tu trabajo o barrio y descríbelos con fewer, less, plenty of, hardly any y the majority of.","kw":["fewer","less","hardly any","majority"],"n":5,"model":"The majority of my neighbors drive to work. Fewer people take the bus now. We have less traffic on weekends. Hardly any people ride bikes. There are plenty of parks, but they're not used much."}}]},{"n":13,"title":"Linking Words","es":"Conectores","cover":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","parts":[{"id":"t13p1","topic":13,"part":1,"title":"Although, despite & whereas","es":"Aunque, a pesar de y mientras que","acts":["learn","bridgeBuilder","sort","fill","unscramble","speak"],"tip":"<p>🌉 Los conectores de <b>contraste</b> unen dos ideas opuestas. ¡Lo difícil es qué va DESPUÉS de cada uno!</p>\n<p>1️⃣ <b>although / even though / whereas</b> + <b>oración</b> (sujeto + verbo):<br>\n<i><b>Although</b> the flight was delayed, we arrived on time.</i> · <i>I love cities, <b>whereas</b> my husband prefers the country.</i></p>\n<p>2️⃣ <b>despite / in spite of</b> + <b>sustantivo</b> o <b>verbo-ING</b>:<br>\n<i><b>Despite</b> the rain, …</i> · <i><b>In spite of</b> being tired, …</i> · ❌ <s>Despite it was raining</s> → ✅ <i>Despite <b>the fact that</b> it was raining</i></p>\n<p>3️⃣ <b>However / Nevertheless</b> = empiezan una <b>nueva oración</b>, con coma:<br>\n<i>The plan was risky. <b>However,</b> it worked.</i></p>\n<p>💡 <b>even though</b> es más enfático que <i>although</i>. <b>whereas</b> compara dos cosas o personas.</p>","tips":["<b>although</b> suena <i>ol-DHÓU</i>: la <i>gh</i> no suena.","<b>whereas</b> se acentúa al final: <i>uer-ÁZ</i>.","Después de <b>However</b> haz una pequeña pausa (la coma): <i>However… it worked.</i>"],"vocab":[{"en":"however","es":"sin embargo","img":"#However, …","v":"f","au":"cdaf2764e9"},{"en":"although","es":"aunque","img":"u:photo-1611014502587-47142e5fbab2","v":"m","au":"20960baba7"},{"en":"even though","es":"aun cuando (más fuerte)","img":"u:photo-1610354878912-08f1ab8ae913","v":"f","au":"08e29e2367"},{"en":"despite","es":"a pesar de","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"m","au":"d0aa67fd9e"},{"en":"in spite of","es":"a pesar de","img":"u:photo-1623975522495-82ea8c48de56","v":"f","au":"e63b487d48"},{"en":"whereas","es":"mientras que (contraste)","img":"u:photo-1524503033411-c9566986fc8f","v":"m","au":"f05d874b06"},{"en":"nevertheless","es":"no obstante","img":"u:photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a","v":"f","au":"e77659392a"},{"en":"despite the rain","es":"a pesar de la lluvia","img":"u:photo-1519692933481-e162a57d6721","v":"m","au":"7506959c38"},{"en":"although it was late","es":"aunque era tarde","img":"u:photo-1599939571322-792a326991f2","v":"f","au":"5bb5b9d27f"},{"en":"despite being nervous","es":"a pesar de estar nervioso","img":"u:photo-1553690300-93871c6a6654","v":"m","au":"c2b220e007"},{"en":"whereas my sister","es":"mientras que mi hermana","img":"u:photo-1663627650051-9fdc3a53a075","v":"f","au":"e07a6708b3"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Although the flight was delayed, we arrived in time for the wedding.","es":"Aunque el vuelo se retrasó, llegamos a tiempo para la boda.","img":"u:photo-1746125047145-d6698eef563a","v":"f","au":"eb7fe3c874"},{"en":"Despite the rain, thousands of runners finished the Boston Marathon.","es":"A pesar de la lluvia, miles de corredores terminaron el Maratón de Boston.","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","v":"m","au":"36d3cd468a"},{"en":"She accepted the job even though the salary was lower.","es":"Ella aceptó el trabajo aun cuando el salario era más bajo.","img":"u:photo-1686771416282-3888ddaf249b","v":"f","au":"7827dee5a0"},{"en":"I love big cities, whereas my husband prefers the countryside.","es":"Me encantan las grandes ciudades, mientras que mi esposo prefiere el campo.","img":"u:photo-1571524188026-cc1d649962ea","v":"m","au":"f47ed67f49"},{"en":"The plan was risky. However, it worked perfectly.","es":"El plan era arriesgado. Sin embargo, funcionó perfectamente.","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"14b009408c"},{"en":"In spite of his experience, he didn't get the promotion.","es":"A pesar de su experiencia, no consiguió el ascenso.","img":"u:photo-1560250097-0b93528c311a","v":"m","au":"c84c6e3d58"}],"fill":[{"s":"___ the traffic, we got to the airport on time.","a":"Despite","o":["Although","However"],"h":"despite + sustantivo","full":"Despite the traffic, we got to the airport on time.","au":"98f7a22eb7"},{"s":"___ it was expensive, they bought the house.","a":"Although","o":["Despite","However"],"h":"although + oración","full":"Although it was expensive, they bought the house.","au":"643546792a"},{"s":"The hotel was nice. ___, the staff wasn't very friendly.","a":"However","o":["Although","Despite"],"h":"nueva oración + coma","full":"The hotel was nice. However, the staff wasn't very friendly.","au":"790dcf55f7"},{"s":"She went to work ___ feeling sick.","a":"despite","o":["although","however"],"h":"despite + -ing","full":"She went to work despite feeling sick.","au":"a5713cfe2a"},{"s":"I like coffee, ___ my wife prefers tea.","a":"whereas","o":["despite","in spite"],"h":"contraste entre dos personas","full":"I like coffee, whereas my wife prefers tea.","au":"40b53cdd62"},{"s":"In spite ___ the noise, I fell asleep.","a":"of","o":["to","the"],"h":"in spite of","full":"In spite of the noise, I fell asleep.","au":"96fefdfd51"},{"s":"___ though he studied a lot, he failed the test.","a":"Even","o":["Despite","However"],"h":"even though + oración","full":"Even though he studied a lot, he failed the test.","au":"450c45fbd9"}],"sort":{"cats":["✍️ + clause","📦 + noun / -ing","🆕 new sentence"],"items":[{"w":"although","c":"✍️ + clause","au":"23f7784298"},{"w":"even though","c":"✍️ + clause","au":"08e29e2367"},{"w":"whereas","c":"✍️ + clause","au":"5eebb65e06"},{"w":"while","c":"✍️ + clause","au":"698e483d22"},{"w":"despite","c":"📦 + noun / -ing","au":"bf8a8ce5c2"},{"w":"in spite of","c":"📦 + noun / -ing","au":"e63b487d48"},{"w":"regardless of","c":"📦 + noun / -ing","au":"a40561e4fb"},{"w":"However,","c":"🆕 new sentence","au":"722fc657ac"},{"w":"Nevertheless,","c":"🆕 new sentence","au":"df601536c5"},{"w":"On the other hand,","c":"🆕 new sentence","au":"8b70a626f9"}]},"goal":{"en":"To contrast ideas with however, although, even though, despite and whereas.","es":"Contrastar ideas con however, although, even though, despite y whereas."},"warm":[{"q":"Have you ever done something even though you were scared?","au":"1117ba5d52","es":"¿Alguna vez has hecho algo aunque tenías miedo?","ex":"Yes, I went skydiving even though I was terrified."},{"q":"How are you different from your brother, sister or best friend?","au":"d7b2974eb7","es":"¿En qué eres diferente de tu hermano, hermana o mejor amigo?","ex":"I'm very organized, whereas my sister is very spontaneous."}],"reading":{"title":"Despite the odds","img":"u:photo-1613936360976-8f35cf0e5461","text":"Rosa Delgado had never run more than five miles when she signed up for the Chicago Marathon. Although her friends thought she was crazy, she started training in January. Despite her busy schedule as a nurse, she ran four times a week, usually at five in the morning. Her husband, whereas he supported her, preferred to stay in bed. In spite of a knee injury in July, Rosa didn't give up. She went to physical therapy and adjusted her training. However, the hardest moment came on race day: it was raining heavily and the temperature was only forty degrees. Even though she was cold and exhausted, she kept going. At mile twenty, she wanted to stop. Nevertheless, she saw her two daughters holding a sign that said \"Go, Mom!\" and found new energy. She finished in five hours and twelve minutes. \"It wasn't fast,\" she says, \"but I finished despite everything.\"","au":"4347cbcd95","q":[{"s":"Rosa was an experienced marathon runner.","a":"no"},{"s":"She trained even though she had a busy schedule.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Her husband also ran every morning.","a":"no"},{"s":"It was raining on race day.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Rosa finished the marathon despite the difficulties.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What do you do even though you don't enjoy it?","a":"I go to the gym even though I don't enjoy it.","es":"¿Qué haces aunque no lo disfrutes?","qau":"a46786c3bd","aau":"bfc6978417"},{"q":"Do you work or study despite being tired?","a":"Yes, I study at night despite being tired.","es":"¿Trabajas o estudias a pesar de estar cansado?","qau":"3baca6a178","aau":"32c3ab15a9"},{"q":"How are you different from a family member?","a":"I'm an early bird, whereas my brother is a night owl.","es":"¿En qué eres diferente de un familiar?","qau":"9832823086","aau":"2d7681630a"},{"q":"Can you tell me something good about your city? However, …","a":"It's beautiful. However, the traffic is terrible.","es":"¿Puedes decirme algo bueno de tu ciudad? Sin embargo, …","qau":"3ad12d87cb","aau":"b5a93d7725"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe sobre un reto que superaste. Usa although, even though, despite/in spite of, however y whereas.","kw":["although","despite","however","whereas"],"n":5,"model":"Although I was nervous, I applied for the job. Despite my lack of experience, I got an interview. Even though the interview was in English, I did well. However, I didn't get the job the first time. My friend gave up, whereas I tried again and succeeded."}},{"id":"t13p2","topic":13,"part":2,"title":"Therefore, moreover & on the other hand","es":"Por lo tanto, además y por otro lado","acts":["learn","investorPitch","dialogue","fill","sayPop","speak"],"tip":"<p>➕ <b>Añadir</b> información: <b>moreover / furthermore / in addition / what's more</b> (al inicio, con coma)<br>\n<i>The apartment is close to the subway. <b>Moreover,</b> the rent is reasonable.</i><br>\n👉 <b>In addition to</b> + sustantivo / -ing: <i><b>In addition to</b> a good salary, …</i></p>\n<p>➡️ <b>Resultado</b>: <b>so</b> (informal, une oraciones) · <b>therefore / as a result / consequently / for this reason</b> (formales)<br>\n<i>It rained all week. <b>As a result,</b> the concert was canceled.</i> · <i>Sales grew; <b>therefore,</b> we hired more staff.</i></p>\n<p>⚖️ <b>Contrastar argumentos</b>: <b>On the one hand … On the other hand …</b><br>\n<i>Remote work saves time. <b>On the other hand,</b> it can feel lonely.</i></p>\n<p>🎯 <b>Not only … but also</b>: <i>She speaks <b>not only</b> English <b>but also</b> Portuguese.</i> · <b>To sum up,</b> = para concluir.</p>","tips":["<b>therefore</b> suena <i>DHÉR-for</i>, con la <i>th</i> suave de <i>the</i>.","<b>moreover</b> se acentúa en <i>OU</i>: <i>mor-ÓU-vər</i>.","<b>furthermore</b> suena <i>FÉR-dhər-mor</i>."],"vocab":[{"en":"therefore","es":"por lo tanto","img":"u:photo-1671059451144-9047992feaee","v":"f","au":"e4b8a01c38"},{"en":"so","es":"así que","img":"u:photo-1688382575775-9aaa5025524e","v":"m","au":"bd3fbeeca8"},{"en":"as a result","es":"como resultado","img":"u:photo-1519692933481-e162a57d6721","v":"f","au":"adca40a7df"},{"en":"consequently","es":"en consecuencia","img":"u:photo-1611147533125-9ca445f32036","v":"m","au":"fdfdb256c6"},{"en":"moreover","es":"además (formal)","img":"u:photo-1758518729466-827cd8293992","v":"f","au":"dd2b28edcf"},{"en":"in addition","es":"adicionalmente","img":"u:photo-1549923746-c502d488b3ea","v":"m","au":"bdf987d641"},{"en":"furthermore","es":"además (formal)","img":"u:photo-1580894732444-8ecded7900cd","v":"f","au":"da74215a6e"},{"en":"what's more","es":"es más","img":"u:photo-1489278353717-f64c6ee8a4d2","v":"m","au":"2e7e0a6967"},{"en":"on the other hand","es":"por otro lado","img":"u:photo-1518644730709-0835105d9daa","v":"f","au":"dfcb4accca"},{"en":"for this reason","es":"por esta razón","img":"u:photo-1623679780844-343be02a038e","v":"m","au":"dcffbe6b30"},{"en":"to sum up","es":"en resumen","img":"u:photo-1758518731706-be5d5230e5a5","v":"f","au":"136e5d79ff"},{"en":"not only … but also","es":"no solo … sino también","img":"u:photo-1758691736975-9f7f643d178e","v":"m","au":"a08debd8b8"}],"sentences":[{"en":"Sales increased by thirty percent; therefore, we hired five new employees.","es":"Las ventas aumentaron un treinta por ciento; por lo tanto, contratamos cinco empleados.","img":"u:photo-1576267423048-15c0040fec78","v":"f","au":"4dad0ec49a"},{"en":"The apartment is close to the subway. Moreover, the rent is reasonable.","es":"El apartamento está cerca del metro. Además, el arriendo es razonable.","img":"u:photo-1521075821520-ae40128c1ea0","v":"m","au":"03ae234cb3"},{"en":"It rained all week. As a result, the outdoor concert was canceled.","es":"Llovió toda la semana. Como resultado, se canceló el concierto al aire libre.","img":"u:photo-1519692933481-e162a57d6721","v":"f","au":"c94c646bdd"},{"en":"Remote work saves time. On the other hand, it can feel lonely.","es":"El trabajo remoto ahorra tiempo. Por otro lado, puede sentirse solitario.","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","v":"m","au":"3d1922f765"},{"en":"In addition to a good salary, the company offers great benefits.","es":"Además de un buen salario, la empresa ofrece excelentes beneficios.","img":"u:photo-1549923746-c502d488b3ea","v":"f","au":"3afc54812f"},{"en":"She missed the deadline, so she apologized to her manager.","es":"No cumplió el plazo, así que le pidió disculpas a su jefe.","img":"u:photo-1714976694720-01c558074a80","v":"m","au":"0adfe53ca1"}],"fill":[{"s":"The product is cheap. ___, it's very reliable.","a":"Moreover","o":["However","Therefore"],"h":"añadir una idea positiva","full":"The product is cheap. Moreover, it's very reliable.","au":"daa61c6a76"},{"s":"He didn't save any money; ___, he couldn't travel.","a":"therefore","o":["moreover","however"],"h":"resultado","full":"He didn't save any money; therefore, he couldn't travel.","au":"7197bed029"},{"s":"___ to the gym, the hotel has a spa.","a":"In addition","o":["Moreover","Furthermore"],"h":"in addition to + sustantivo","full":"In addition to the gym, the hotel has a spa.","au":"6a71ae6787"},{"s":"Living in Miami is exciting. On the ___ hand, it's expensive.","a":"other","o":["another","one"],"h":"on the other hand","full":"Living in Miami is exciting. On the other hand, it's expensive.","au":"14d6e37667"},{"s":"The roads were icy. As a ___, many schools closed.","a":"result","o":["consequence","reason"],"h":"as a result","full":"The roads were icy. As a result, many schools closed.","au":"70602b7ff4"},{"s":"I was exhausted, ___ I went to bed early.","a":"so","o":["therefore","moreover"],"h":"so (informal, con coma)","full":"I was exhausted, so I went to bed early.","au":"1c86f2ed9a"},{"s":"She speaks four languages. ___, she has an MBA.","a":"What's more","o":["However","As a result"],"h":"añadir (informal)","full":"She speaks four languages. What's more, she has an MBA.","au":"8cec7dc1e1"}],"dialogue":{"title":"Pitching a new idea","es":"Presentando una nueva idea","img":"u:photo-1580894732444-8ecded7900cd","lines":[{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Thanks for coming, everyone. I'd like to propose a four-day work week.","au":"e3c7b8e575"},{"who":"Mark","v":"m","t":"Interesting. What are the advantages?","au":"6afb58f016"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"Employees would be happier. As a result, they'd be more productive.","au":"64893c5d5d"},{"who":"Mark","v":"m","t":"OK. On the other hand, our clients expect us to be available five days a week.","au":"76427ac4a3"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"True. Therefore, we could rotate teams so that someone is always available.","au":"8be303672f"},{"who":"Mark","v":"m","t":"That makes sense. What about costs?","au":"688b879dff"},{"who":"Rachel","v":"f","t":"We'd use less energy in the office. In addition, we'd attract better candidates.","au":"5d4396e692"},{"who":"Mark","v":"m","t":"Not only is it creative, but it's also well planned. Let's try it for three months.","au":"1e3bc569e2"}],"q":[{"q":"What does Rachel propose?","a":"A four-day work week.","o":["A new office.","Hiring more clients."]},{"q":"What is Mark's concern?","a":"Clients expect them five days a week.","o":["Employees are unhappy.","Energy is expensive."]},{"q":"What is Rachel's solution?","a":"Rotating teams.","o":["Working on Saturdays.","Closing on Fridays."]}]},"goal":{"en":"To build clear arguments with therefore, as a result, moreover, in addition and on the other hand.","es":"Construir argumentos claros con therefore, as a result, moreover, in addition y on the other hand."},"warm":[{"q":"What are the advantages of working from home?","au":"6c33912b71","es":"¿Cuáles son las ventajas de trabajar desde casa?","ex":"You save time. Moreover, you save money on gas."},{"q":"Would you prefer a higher salary or more vacation days?","au":"118341b554","es":"¿Preferirías un salario más alto o más días de vacaciones?","ex":"More vacation days. On the other hand, money is important too."}],"reading":{"title":"Should our company go remote?","img":"u:photo-1524508762098-fd966ffb6ef9","text":"Last month, the CEO of a small software company in Raleigh asked her team to write a report on whether to close the office and go fully remote. The report began with the advantages. Remote work saves employees an average of ten hours a week of commuting. As a result, many feel more rested and productive. Moreover, the company would save around eighty thousand dollars a year on rent. In addition to saving money, it could hire talent from anywhere in the country. On the other hand, the team identified some serious risks. New employees often feel isolated and learn more slowly. Furthermore, spontaneous conversations, which often lead to the best ideas, are much less common online. For this reason, the report did not recommend closing the office completely. Instead, it proposed a hybrid model: three days at home and two in the office. To sum up, the team concluded that flexibility, not distance, is the real key to happiness at work.","au":"0404fb8e44","q":[{"s":"The report was about going fully remote.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Remote work saves employees about ten hours a week.","a":"yes"},{"s":"Going remote would cost the company more money.","a":"no"},{"s":"The team found no risks in remote work.","a":"no"},{"s":"The report recommended a hybrid model.","a":"yes"}]},"keyq":[{"q":"What are the advantages of learning English? Moreover, …","a":"It helps you get a better job. Moreover, you can travel easily.","es":"¿Cuáles son las ventajas de aprender inglés? Además, …","qau":"7462a569aa","aau":"55cc2586a4"},{"q":"What happens if you don't sleep enough? As a result, …","a":"I feel tired. As a result, I can't concentrate.","es":"¿Qué pasa si no duermes lo suficiente? Como resultado, …","qau":"ca3cb85cd6","aau":"9769bdebf4"},{"q":"Is living in a big city good? On the other hand, …","a":"There are many jobs. On the other hand, it's expensive.","es":"¿Es bueno vivir en una ciudad grande? Por otro lado, …","qau":"0bad5f7a8e","aau":"dfee60f875"},{"q":"Why do you study English? Therefore, …","a":"I want to work in the U.S.; therefore, I study every day.","es":"¿Por qué estudias inglés? Por lo tanto, …","qau":"87d9850918","aau":"b5eaf95c5c"}],"hw":{"es":"Escribe un párrafo de opinión: ¿trabajo remoto o en la oficina? Usa moreover/in addition, therefore/as a result, on the other hand y to sum up.","kw":["moreover","therefore","on the other hand","to sum up"],"n":6,"model":"Working from home has many advantages. It saves time. Moreover, it saves money on gas. As a result, people feel less stressed. On the other hand, it can be lonely. Therefore, I think a hybrid model is best. To sum up, flexibility is the key."}}]}],"letters":{"A":"6d717a50cb","B":"80c0feee5f","C":"d87275787d","D":"82c3a5fb2d","E":"9f7b646ba8","F":"d60431768d","G":"7cba883078","H":"c26de21099","I":"11b70e698d","J":"7280c01c88","K":"8f887ac900","L":"8e684bf3bf","M":"ab15838f42","N":"adbb42df84","O":"7b127b9991","P":"61fb4061f6","Q":"5e7027877b","R":"b634d637b4","S":"5b84a3506b","T":"77a78fbc1b","U":"df6d7e37af","V":"354ccded81","W":"d3d0b1df88","X":"64808c2c00","Y":"5724debb9c","Z":"9d81304034"},"praise":{"Awesome!":"98561b5346","Great job!":"a88a2d51d2","Perfect!":"9abc262823","Excellent!":"54f1859c38","Well done!":"b93b9f5f0f","You got it!":"1a9de5fa28","Fantastic!":"d5bfd68ea5","Nice work!":"aa2b15da71"},"retry":{"Try again.":"e4bbac6f81","Almost! Listen again.":"2ace7bd775","Not quite. You can do it!":"8b4c184411"}};
